Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, has made it clear that the law on the amendment of the election law will come into force soon. And the prince also wants to know what all those extremist opposition groups will do next. While the prince had just received information from an internal meeting of the opposition in Phnom Penh, his boss ordered him to remain silent.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered that boycotting the election of those who believe in the incitement of three generations of traitors is equivalent to killing their own political life. Samdech emphasized that in the event that all of them did not vote on July 23, they will definitely not be eligible to stand for election in 2028, because the conditions for standing for the National Assembly are valid until they have voted twice. Times.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed the competent forces and all those involved must jointly strengthen and take preventive measures in accordance with the law to prevent any activities that attempt to destroy or cause other phenomena that affect the process. The 7th National Assembly election will be held on July 23, 2023.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister added that in the past, the Royal Government of Cambodia has always given favors to opposition politicians, but to cross the red line is no choice but to take legal action. In the case of law enforcement and still committing the opposite, there is nothing but a prison, because prisons are designed to put corrupt people, people who commit illegal acts.
