At the same time, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has been promoting the implementation of the strategic plan for the development of employment and vocational training, especially the modernization of the technical and vocational education and training system to build a clear professional workforce. Innovative and highly competitive. This afternoon, Samdech Techo chaired a meeting to review the report of the 6th mandate of the Royal Government Working Group.
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Monday, June 19, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will chair a meeting to review the report of the sixth mandate. Local Government Working Group.
The local government working group has the role of promoting leadership, coordinating and supporting sub-national administrations in promoting the provision of services, local development, and solving problems for local people.
In carrying out the work, the working group has no role or authority to decide on behalf of other ministries and institutions. The Minister, the head of each institution still has roles and responsibilities in accordance with the same legal principles. At the same time, the working group does not have the role of managing the work on behalf of the sub-national administration and the competent authorities.
The working group shall lead and encourage the sub-national administration, departments, specialized units to improve the efficiency of the work in accordance with the defined roles, duties and responsibilities.
In case of unresolved challenges, the working group should urge the relevant ministries and institutions to solve and monitor the results of the solution to report to the Royal Government.
On average, there were 113 participants in one public forum in the sixth mandate, compared to 125 in the fifth mandate.
Rural development, security, public order, land administration, water resources and meteorology, education, youth and sports, and the public and transport sectors accounted for about 64 percent of all issues, leading the way.
Rural development, land administration, public works and transportation, security, public order, water resources and meteorology, provision of all kinds of services and governance, and electricity, accounted for 71% of the leading cases in the sixth legislature.
The report shows that the local government working group has coordinated and cooperated well with the administration of the capital, provinces, municipalities, districts, Khans, communes and sangkats to achieve positive results, solve many concerns, suggestions and proposals of local, but there are still challenges. Some things that need to be improved are:
1: The Royal Government working group in the capital and provinces has been slow to collect data or report and send it to the Secretariat of the CCHR on a regular basis.
2. Resolving the challenges as the requests or concerns of the people raised in the public forum, the working group is still slow to resolve in response to the people.
3: Some members of the working group of the Royal Government have a lack of means (mission money and fuel, etc.) for regular visits to the base on time.
4: Secretariat of the CCHR Lack of means for carrying out missions in organizing meetings, workshops, guidance to the Capital and Provincial Secretariat and local visits to disseminate the results and activities to the sub-national level.
5. The working group of the Royal Government to visit the capital and provinces has not yet been composed of representatives of all ministries and national institutions in the working groups of the Royal Government to visit the capital and provinces.
6: Promote the establishment of secretariats in each ministry, institution, capital, province and municipality, district, Khan in accordance with the guidelines of the Royal Government.
Overall results: Working groups at all levels have resolved and are taking measures to address the challenges. Proposals for the 6th legislature accounted for 86% of the total 36,340 cases and the remaining 14% will seek guidance from the national level. Response measures.
In particular, for the direction for the implementation of the Royal Government working group to visit the capital and provinces:
* Must cooperate and create conditions for the process of preparing for the 7th National Assembly election, which will take place on July 23, 2023.
* Strengthen the dissemination of measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 by the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health; Citizens to ensure real community solicitation.
* Continue to co-organize local public forums on a regular basis, focusing on meeting the poor, vulnerable and people who have not participated in public forums in the past. Come to continue to directly understand the challenges, requests, concerns and concerns, as well as receive feedback from the people without discrimination and without prejudice to political tendencies that vary from situation to situation.
* In addition to organizing public forums, the team needs to work together to find ways to understand the well-being and stigma of the people by visiting the people in the back of each house.
* Meet with the sub-national administration and relevant professional authorities to update the list of challenges, requests of the people at least every 3 months.
* Continue to cooperate and pay attention to solving the problems that are being solved and the problems that have not been solved yet, based on the principles and measures that have been set.
* Each relevant ministry and institution has received the request of the working group of the Royal Government to go to the grassroots level, which cannot be resolved, and efforts must be made to solve the challenges and requests in an appropriate and timely manner within the competence of each relevant ministry and institution.
Prepare regular summary reports to be sent to the Secretariat of the Royal Government Working Group on Capital, Province (RCAF) at regular intervals every three months.
