(Battambang): Mr. Chan Saruth, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, called for the implementation of all measures to reduce the destruction of soil quality, unsustainable land use and destruction of ecosystems.
The call comes on the occasion of Chan Saruth presiding over the World Day Against Deterioration and Drought 2023.
The day was also attended by the leadership of the Ministry of Agriculture, Deputy Governor of Battambang, Mr. Soeum Bunrith and many other stakeholders. The ceremony was held at Wat Phnom Slek, Boeung Ampil village, Sdao commune, Rattanak Mondul district, Battambang province on June 17, 2023.
Mr. Chan Saruth said that the celebration of the World Day Against Deterioration and Drought 2023 is to show the will, commitment and participation of the world within the framework of the implementation of the Convention and to Encourage and increase the interest of all stakeholders to understand this important event.
To celebrate this meaningful World Day, Mr. Chan Saruth would like to provide some key messages to the whole ceremony to consider further implementation as follows:
1. Implement sustainable and climate-resilient agriculture based on ecological principles. At the same time, it is necessary to identify and disseminate good agricultural practices intelligently with climate change, and to improve the management of natural disaster stores and the ability of clusters to be aware of climate change at all levels.
Mr. Chan Saruth continued that in particular, we must work together to consider all possibilities to solve the challenges mentioned above, aimed at reducing production costs, increase revenue, ensure environmental sustainability for our people and our motherland. .
2. All measures must be taken to reduce the destruction of soil quality, unsustainable land use and destruction of ecosystems. At the same time, the specialized unit must pay high attention to the appropriate identification of agricultural land and wide dissemination for long-term direction. At the same time, it is necessary to promote land use policies and related policies.
3. All stakeholders must participate in protecting, restoring and implementing the sustainable use of natural resources and environmental systems, especially to prevent the implementation or activities that cause degradation or deterioration of soil quality, that is, to divert from Live by relying on non-timber forest products and practices, as well as the practice of subsistence farming, modern intensive farming, sustainable land management to improve livelihoods.
