70 people claim to have cheated the GC Orussey Market project on Russian Boulevard, some paid up to 40,000 USD, but the market has not yet hit the ground
(Phnom Penh): About 70 people claimed that they shot at the market project of GC Orussey Ek Company, located on Russian Boulevard, Teuk Thla Village, Sangkat Teuk Thla, Khan Sen Sok, they paid between 2 Tens of thousands of dollars to more than 40,000 dollars, so far, the project Ori Russey Market has not even hit the ground.
They said that when purchasing the project, the company promised that if there is no construction until March 2023, the company will return all the money to the customer with a valid written letter recognized by the company. As of the date of the refund agreement, no indemnity has been initiated.
All 70 of them pointed out that until now, the company has not recognized the contract that it has prepared, refusing to pay back, causing customers to lose confidence in the company.
Starting from all these problems, the 70 people submitted a letter requesting the intervention of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to help solve them while the company tried to evade responsibility.
Regarding this accusation, GC Orussey Company has also commented, claiming that it still maintains a strong position in implementing the GC Orussey Market project and abides by the contract made with customers.
