This Morning, Samdech Techo Inaugurates Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant, Phase 1
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, June 19, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen inaugurated the Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant. The largest water treatment plant in Cambodia.
The first phase of Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant was opened in February 2021 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. The first phase of the Bak Kheng water treatment plant will be built on an area of 15 hectares with a total production capacity of 195,000 cubic meters per day. The plant has been piloting the production and distribution of clean water since April 21, 2023, and the construction will be completed on May 5, 2023, with a construction period of 36 months.
The first phase of Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant has added to the existing water production capacity of 640,000 cubic meters per day, bringing the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority with a total capacity of 835,000 cubic meters in Days to increase the supply to about 170,000 families and help solve the problem of clean water of people living on the outskirts of Phnom Penh and 3 communes in Takhmao.
At the beginning of 2024, after the operation of Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant, Phase 2, Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has the capacity to produce and supply more than 1 million cubic meters of clean water per day.
This gives the people living in Phnom Penh and Takhmao, especially those living on the outskirts of Phnom Penh, access to clean water supply, which ensures better water pressure and closes the current water shortage trend. Early 2024.
Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant has a pumping station on the Mekong River and the installation of a two-meter diameter pipeline along Win-Win Boulevard and the drilling of a 800-meter-long pipeline through the Tonle Sap River. . The Tonle Sap Pipe Backing Project is the largest project to be implemented in Cambodia.
The Bak Kheng Water Supply Project has received two concessional financing from the French Agency for Development (AFD) for the construction of the two-phase Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant.
For the second phase, the budget of the French Agency for Development (AFD) is 100 million US dollars, both of which are funded by the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority of 80 million US dollars.
Total investment in Bak Kheng water treatment plant, Phase 1 and 2, total cost nearly 400 million US dollars.
The growth of the population, the growth of businesses, as a result, Phnom Penh has a growing supply demand from year to year. The Royal Government has also continuously increased the capacity of this clean water supply. At the beginning of 2024, after the opening of the second phase of Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant, the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority will have the capacity to produce and supply a total of more than 1 million cubic meters of clean water per day.
Please note that at present, Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority is operating 5 water treatment plants, including: Chroy Changvar factory, Prek village factory, Chamkarmon factory, Niroth factory and Bak Kheng factory, Phase 1, while Bak Kheng Phase 2 is scheduled to start operating. 2024.
