Cambodia strengthens customer protection governance for CEOs and shareholders or the Board of Directors of banking and financial institutions
The training, which took place on June 14, is the first ever training course that requires the top management of all banking and financial institutions to join in a concerted effort to ensure customer protection. In Cambodia.
Mr. Raymond SIA, President of the Banking Association of Cambodia, noted that this training was a positive sign for the banking sector, investors, stakeholders and the public about the commitment of the members of the Banking Association of Cambodia in the practice of good corporate governance through the implementation of the Code of Conduct. Contained in the policies and procedures of all those members.
"The role of the shareholders and the top management of the institution is very important in ensuring consumer protection and market execution," he said.
He added that banking and financial institutions must maintain good and effective governance at all times to ensure their professional business ethics and code of conduct and ensure that all products and services are designed to meet your needs. Consumer satisfaction is always a priority for organizations in designing and developing their products and services.
It should be noted that the opening ceremony of the training program on the importance and role of governance of banking and financial institutions in ensuring the effective implementation of customer protection was attended by the CEO, shareholders, Board of Directors of banking and financial institutions and more than 100 regulators. People. Eight training courses will be held in 2023 and more in 2024.
