This is an opportunity for both local and foreign investors to invest in processing for export.
However, the challenge is that Cambodia does not seem to be able to process much domestically yet, so far only 5% of processed grain exports, while more than 90% of unprocessed grain exports. To neighboring countries such as Vietnam, Thailand and India. Therefore, Cambodia only needs processing to be competitive and well-packaged for future exports.
He said that if the relevant institutions, including the Ministry of Commerce, the Ministry of Industry, the Ministry of Agriculture, development partners and the private sector, implement the "National Policy on Cashew 2022-2027" effectively and objectively, it will push Cambodia to achieve. Imperial countries export cashew in the future.
At the same time, some farmers even get a certificate of organic farming, while some farmers grow in protected areas, which contributes to forest protection. This will make Cambodian cashews more value-added and more attractive to the global market, especially in Europe, the United States, Australia and the Middle East.
According to the Minister of Commerce and the President of the Cambodian Cashew Federation, Cambodia's cashew nuts, which are recognized as the number one quality in the world, are M23.
In order to promote Cambodia to become the next emperor of cashew exports, ARDB, a state-owned bank, has provided loans at reasonable interest rates to cashew business owners to invest in the purchase of cashew peeling machines, the construction of warehousing. Drying and expanding cashew cultivation, purchasing fertilizers and maintenance.
Dr. Kao Thach, Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Rural Development Bank for Agriculture and Rural Development (ARDB), encourages farmers and companies to consider applying for a loan from ARDB Bank by simply using dried cashew stock as collateral. The bank can provide loans up to 70% of the value of cashew nuts in stock.
