Japan lends nearly $ 200 million to improve rural roads and expand water supply in Siem Reap
(Phnom Penh): The government provides nearly 200 million more loans to improve rural roads and expand the water supply capacity in Siem Reap in the third phase.
Mr. Prak Sokhon, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and Mr. UENO Atsushi, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, will sign the loan agreement on June 20, 2023.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the assistance underscores Japan's unwavering commitment to support the Royal Government of Cambodia's ongoing efforts to promote socio-economic development.
This support will also contribute to the strengthening of long-term relations and close cooperation between the two countries, which have recently upgraded bilateral relations to the level of "comprehensive strategic partnership". The two are celebrating the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations.
