Cambodian People's Network Association launches action plan to strengthen tourism services in local communities to improve community livelihoods
(Phnom Penh): Seeing the huge benefits in communities with tourism potential, the Cambodian People's Network Association (LNFA) has been working on action plans to strengthen tourism services, train community capacity for development. These communities to become new tourism destinations, encourage people to earn more income from tourism, improve local livelihoods, contribute to the development of sustainable tourism.
The preparation of action plans and related tasks was presented at the first general meeting of the Cambodian People's Network Association (LNFA) held on 18 June 2023 at ECHO Community. Trapeang Sangke Tourism is located in Trapeang Sangke Commune, Teuk Chhou District, Kampot Province, under the chairmanship of Mr. Ny Phally, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and Chairman of the Board of the United Nations Association.
At least 41 community representatives and 18 reserve members (observers) from Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Thom, Pursat, Battambang, Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Takeo, Kampot, Kep, Sihanoukville, Koh Kong, etc. represented a total population of 100,000. . Most of these communities are forest protection communities, fishing communities, agricultural communities, natural resource protection communities, ecotourism communities, tourism communities and so on.
Mr. Ny Phally said that the meeting reported and evaluated the general situation in the member communities and the monitoring community, as well as highlighted the challenges, needs and requests from the member and reserve members. He added that the UN has also recorded the challenges to be ready to cooperate with the Ministry, professional institutions, relevant authorities and partners in the future.
The association will also address other needs of the member community, while some members need community headquarters for day-to-day operations, infrastructure support for tourism services to tourists, equipment for patrols, protection of natural resources in the community, aesthetics In the community and seek cooperation to provide additional training to the community as well.
Mr. Thuon Sinan, Secretary General of the United Nations, also stated that the main mission of the United Nations is to support and coordinate through legal forms to the member communities in case of any problems, vocational training. Tourism, agriculture, handicrafts, etc., as well as help promote community tourism destinations to domestic and foreign tourism markets to help develop the local economy, improve the livelihood of the community through tourism.
The expert, who has more than 20 years of experience in the field of tourism, stated that the new tourism potential available in those communities will become more new tourism products to attract and serve national and international tourists. .B will also help attract tourists to the community as a member directly.
