(Siem Reap): Prof. Mam Bun Heng, Minister of Health and the accompanying delegation inspected the construction site of the new building of Siem Reap Provincial Hospital under the project to upgrade the Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital, which is a grant from the government and People of Japan through the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) to the Royal Government and the people of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The new building will be built on a total area of 37,380 square meters, with a total area of 8,320 square meters, 4 floors high, including the ground floor and 200 beds, which began construction in December 2021 and will Construction will be completed by the end of September 2023.
The new building includes the emergency department, paramedics, hospitalization department, surgery department, medical imaging department and support unit. The new building will contribute to improving efficiency, quality, safety and equity not only for the people of Siem Reap, but also for the people around Siem Reap and to reduce the referral of patients to Phnom Penh.
