(Phnom Penh): The National Blood Transfusion Center of the Ministry of Health has continued to call on people to donate blood voluntarily, as the current donation in Cambodia does not meet the actual needs, up to 40 percent.
Speaking on June 17, 2023, Dr. Khay Sokheng, Deputy Director of the Technical Office of the National Blood Transfusion Center, thanked the public and private sectors as well as philanthropists who always donate blood to save lives.
"We receive blood donations every day. We welcome your voluntary blood donation. ” This is according to Dr. Khay Sok Heng when receiving the blood donation.
On World Blood Donation Day, Mr. Sok Po, President of the National Blood Transfusion Center, said that the demand for blood in 2022 is only 0.62% of the total population of Cambodia, with a total population of 17 million. . Cambodia needs a blood tattoo to save a patient's life every six minutes.
According to the World Health Organization (WHO), 17 percent of the population must donate blood, meaning that 17 million people will be able to donate until there are 170,000 volunteers. But the current situation is only 0.62 percent. Cambodia is still in dire need of more than 40 percent to have enough blood to supply throughout the country.
