(Preah Sihanouk): Twelve gangsters were arrested by Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police after they attacked and stabbed each other anarchically in front of Casino Yapor in Group 10, Village 2, Sangkat 3, Preah Krong. Sihanouk on June 12, 2023.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Chuon Narin told Fresh News this morning, June 18, 2023, that on the day of the incident, there were about 30 suspects, some of them wearing helmets and belts. A stick and a recycled sword attacked a group of 7 victims (3 males and 4 females), causing one victim to suffer serious head injuries and died at Preah Kosomak Hospital.
According to the General Commissioner, after the incident, he ordered the specialized force of the Sihanoukville Police Inspectorate to conduct an urgent search and arrest 12 suspects for questioning. The 12 suspects are currently being held at the Sihanoukville Police Inspectorate for questioning and further proceedings. As for the remaining factions, they are fleeing, and the authorities are conducting a professional investigation.
Samdech Techo Youth Volunteer (TYDA) Provides Free Treatment to Nearly 2,000 Poor People in Chamkar Mon District
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Youth Volunteer Doctors on June 17, 2023 examined and treated a total of 1,900 people in poor communities, equivalent to 3,547 cases under the chairmanship of Mrs. Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet, Vice Chairman of the Board of the Association, cooperates with local authorities and other relevant departments.
Examination and treatment include general diseases, oral, dental, echocardiography, minimally invasive surgery, hemorrhoids, joints, skin, ears, nose, throat, blood tests, radiology, gynecology, ophthalmology, laboratory in Boeung Trabek High School, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
Dr. Pech Chanmony added that what is special is that today's mission TYDA led a team of more than 200 doctors, including doctors from Malaysia to specialize in treating people here. She also thanked the relevant authorities and all partners.
On that occasion, Mr. Kieng Leak, Governor of Chamkar Mon District, expressed his deep gratitude to Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet, Vice Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Association, who led a group of doctors to visit the people here for free. Is to reduce the poverty of the people to another level.
