Keo Remy Inaugurates CPP Office in Kampong Preang Commune, Sangke District
(Battambang): Mr. Keo Remy, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Party Working Group visited Roka and Kampong Preang communes this morning, June 17, 2023, presided over the ribbon-cutting ceremony of the party's headquarters. Cambodians, Kampong Preang commune.
The ceremony was attended by Deputy Governor of Sangke District, Commune Party Committee, Commune Council, Commune Chief, Village Chief, Post Chief, Youth Activist, CPP member and 308 people.
The new building of the party office of Kampong Preang commune is a one-story building with a height of 8 meters, a width of 7.30 meters, a length of 12.40 meters, 1 meter wings, concrete, tiled roof and a warehouse and separate rooms.
The construction of the new party headquarters building due to the old building, which was built in 1997, is in a dilapidated condition, narrow and flooded, which does not meet the needs of the commune party today.
After receiving permission from the Sangke District Party Committee on January 24, 2023, the construction of a completely new building began in February 2023, with additional landfilling, and so far almost achieved. 100% remaining on the ceiling, bathroom and warehouse only. Construction took four and a half months and cost about $ 40,000.
The construction was carried out under the guidance and guidance of Mr. Keo Remy through the Kampong Preang Commune Party Committee, under the direct leadership of Mr. Khieu Tola and with the active participation of all party working groups in Kampong Preang commune.
On that occasion, Mr. Keo Remy expressed his gratitude to the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party, with Samdech Te as the Prime Minister as the President of the party, who brought complete peace, so that Cambodia has developed in all areas today with great achievements. Many of the Royal Government, including democracy, human rights and the rule of law.
In addition, he congratulated the new achievements of the Kampong Preang commune party and thanked the commune party committee, working group and all party members.
He said that Cambodia adheres to democracy and respect for human rights is at the forefront of the region. The amendment of the election law does not affect the rights of the electorate, but maintains the democratic process and the people participate in the full exercise of their right to elect their preferred representatives.
Finally, Mr. Keo Remy instructed to participate in the maintenance of the new party headquarters building to serve the interests of all party members in Kampong Preang commune, both in party work and development in the whole commune.
