Pailin Provincial Administration Issues a Press Release on the Cause of Unable to Issue a Construction Permit to a Family After Posting Allegations on Social Media
(Pailin): The Pailin Provincial Administration on June 17, 2023 issued an urgent press release rejecting the publication of "Life and Sports Lives" which published baseless information on why The Pailin provincial administration could not issue a building permit to Mr. Phuong Savuth and Ms. Chheng Youkiang.
In connection with this news release, the Pailin Provincial Administration has completely rejected all publications from the first to the eighth period, because the content that the lawyers and spokespersons of the provincial administration have clarified in the past, but the above press continues. Publish and refuse to correct the content it has published.
The provincial administration spokesman also reiterated to the public and social media why the provincial administration could not issue a building permit to Mr. Phuong Savuth and Ms. Chheng Youkiang:
1. Pailin Provincial Administration has received a complaint from the people asking for the intervention of the owner of the construction land to open a public road according to the plan of the authorities to determine the size of 10 meters, the owner of the above violated the public land of 7 meters.
2. The construction owner did the construction before requesting the law from the provincial administration, the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral, and the provincial administration issued a letter prohibiting the construction owner from temporarily suspending construction. Instead, the owners continue to build arbitrarily.
3. Mr. Phuong Savuth and Ms. Chheng Youkieng were the owners of the land and the applicants for the construction permit, but Roeun Borey was the complainant to the provincial administration. This story also shows the irregularity and irrationality.
Based on the above three basic reasons, the Pailin Provincial Administration could not issue a building permit, as the provincial administration is examining the relevant expertise to find a solution in accordance with legal procedures.
