During a visit to Cambodia, Kim In-One, Director General of the Korea Health Promotion Association (KAHP) earlier this week, said that in 2023, his association was implementing a project to manage non-communicable diseases in Cambodia, such as hypertension. Blood and Diabetes, etc. by providing counseling, education to the people, diagnostic tests and treatment of diabetes conducted at Prek Pnov Referral Hospital.
He said that so far, the Korea Health Promotion Association has helped treat and treat diabetes and high blood pressure to hundreds of Cambodians, especially to improve the health and lifestyle of the people. Avoid or prevent these non-communicable diseases.
According to Mr. Son Sophea, 43 years old, living in Sangkat Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh, who came to receive counseling and diagnosis of non-communicable diseases, said that before he was in poor health, high blood pressure, weight did not rise. Proportion with the body, but after receiving information from the village chief announced that there will be a Korean Association for counseling and medical examination, he also came to receive the service.
"I came for a medical check-up and was diagnosed with high blood pressure, which left my body weak," said Son Sophea. The doctor taught me how to take care of my health to avoid high blood pressure and diabetes and told me how to live my daily life with both diet and exercise, especially not to eat salty, sweet foods and "Too much fat."
"After a period of treatment, I have recovered and now I am also a member of the association's fitness club, especially now that I have become more aware of my health and love for myself." Additional remarks by Mr. Son Sophea.
Please be informed that during the implementation of the above project for more than a year, the association's gym also selected about 300 members. This year, 150 more will be selected.
He continued, "I am very happy to see our people change their attitude, know how to take care of their health and come for regular treatment according to the doctor's appointment, especially to come to the gym and monitor their health with the above association to see that their health is better." Before.
The director of the Referral Hospital also thanked the Korean side, especially the Korean Health Promotion Association, which has worked hard to improve the health of Cambodia and have an understanding of how to prevent all these non-communicable diseases. At the same time, he also asked the association to continue to help on this project, as well as other projects to help improve the health of the Cambodian people.
