Ministry of Foreign Affairs presents the results of the second bilateral consultations between Cambodia and the Czech Republic
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Cham Vidya, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and Mr. Jiří Kozák, Deputy Foreign Minister of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Czech Republic, co-chaired the Second Bilateral Consultation. Between the two countries. The meeting was held on June 15, 2023 at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation.
According to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the two sides noted with satisfaction the traditional good relations and the growing cooperation between the two countries. They both expressed their commitment to promoting broader cooperation, which is in the common interest for the better.
Dr. Cham Vidya expressed his deep gratitude to the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia for the Government and the Czech people for their generous assistance over the years since the liberation of the Cambodian people from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot. Important to the well-being and development of Cambodia. The Secretary of State also briefed his Czech counterpart on the political situation and economic development of Cambodia.
Jiří Kozák praised Cambodia's rapid economic growth, its chairmanship of ASEAN in 2022 and its successful prevention of the Kovid-19 epidemic. He also said that Cambodia's political stability and dynamic economic growth have encouraged Czech investors to invest in Cambodia.
At the end of the talks, the two sides expressed great interest in continuing the dialogue through bilateral consultations between the two Ministries of Foreign Affairs, which are effective mechanisms for monitoring previously agreed actions to strengthen bilateral ties. Departments in all areas deepen.
