Mr. Robin Nay: We must work together to keep the peace, to have respect for human rights
(Central): Robin Nai, a member of the National Committee Against Torture, said in front of a representative of the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia that peace is the only way to respect human rights.
He added that peace is very valuable for the Cambodian people because peace in Cambodia comes from the struggle for life and the great sacrifice of the Cambodian leaders. Therefore, the Cambodian people, including the international community, must participate in maintaining peace.
Mr. Robin Nay said this on the occasion of announcing the opening of training and education on national and international standards and roles and responsibilities of the National Committee against Torture in Kandal province on the morning of June 15, 2023.
He added that the Royal Government of Cambodia, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, is highly committed to respecting human rights and strengthening the rule of law. The fight against torture is also highly regarded in accordance with the Universal Declaration of Human Rights and the United Nations Convention against Torture.
Mr. Robin Nay said that Cambodia is the only country in the region that has ratified the most international instruments, and according to research, Cambodia is also a leading country in the region that has established a national body in charge of anti-torture before. They too. This proves that the Royal Government of Cambodia is highly committed to the implementation of its obligations under international instruments as a State Party.
On that occasion, Mr. Robin Nay instructed all participants to pay attention to take the knowledge of this educational course to share to lower officials to use in the daily work of the Royal Government as well as the people. People in the whole of Kandal province.
At the same time, he also praised the relevant authorities for their efforts to fulfill their duties and responsibilities with high responsibility to contribute to the image of the Royal Government on the international stage in the field of human rights.
It should also be noted that on the morning of June 15, 2023, the National Committee Against Torture, in cooperation with the Kandal Provincial Administration, organized a training and dissemination course on national and international standards on prevention and control of torture and the duties and responsibilities of the National Anti-Torture Committee. Torture under the chairmanship of Mr. Nut Sa An, Chairman of the National Committee Against Torture.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Prak Sarath, Deputy Governor of Kandal Provincial Board of Governors, Mr. Liv Sreng, Prosecutor of Kandal Provincial Court, representatives from the judiciary, police, military police, prisons and relevant authorities under Kandal Provincial Administration, a total of 350 people. .
The purpose of this training and outreach is to share knowledge, experience and good practice in order to raise awareness and strengthen the capacity of the competent authorities and relevant actors in Siem Reap to ensure the prevention and elimination of torture. All forms in Cambodia.
Mr. Sok Siphana: In the next 10 years, the Cambodian economy will be heavily dependent on the ASEAN Agreement
This statement by Mr. Sok Siphana was made this morning, June 16, 2023, on the occasion of presiding over a lecture on "Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership: Geopolitical Perspectives and Economic Geography" this morning. This is June 16, 2023.
At the same time, Mr. Sok Siphana also encouraged and encouraged the dissemination of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP) to all traders or stakeholders to learn more about the benefits and benefits of trade. On this agreement.
Mr. Sok Siphana also said that the ASEAN Agreement is the largest free trade agreement in the world with 15 members, including the 10 ASEAN member countries and 5 ASEAN free trade partners: Australia, China, Japan, South Korea and New Zealand. This agreement is an initiative of ASEAN and was announced to start negotiations in 2012 after coming into force on January 1, 2022.
According to Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, the Asean Agreement is very important for Cambodia. Because Cambodia is a country in the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP).
Dr. Yong Pov also reminded that it is necessary to have a clear understanding of international affairs in order to adapt the policy to the times, so if we do not understand the politics of the region and the world, it will make it difficult for us to do business with Countries and so on.
According to the Ministry of Commerce, the agreement covers about 2.2 billion people of the world's population, about $ 26.2 trillion in GDP and trade volume. About 28% of the total world trade volume by 2021.
According to a study by the Economic Research Institute for ASEAN and East Asia (ERIA), Cambodia is expected to grow 7.3% in annual exports, 23.4% in investment and 2% of GDP. %.
