(Kampong Cham): It is amazing that a worker in Prey Chhor district, Kampong Cham province, despite being a widow and living in poverty, is determined not to give up in the face of adversity and is determined to provide for her children to get a good education. The future is better and better.
Ms. Lon Thida lives in Takeo village, Kor commune, Prey Chhor district, Kampong Cham province and has been working in a shoe factory in Cheung Prey district. She has two sons, one 13 years old and the other 8 years old.
More than eight years ago, Lon Thida worked in a factory in Phnom Penh with her husband. When she gave birth to her second child, she returned home and was abandoned by her new husband.
She recalled that that was a very difficult time. As a widow, she had a baby and had to support her elderly mother in the home. But she overcame all difficulties for life.
Currently, her first son is in 8th grade and her second son is in 2nd grade. She points out that she not only raises two sons, but also an elderly mother.
Working as a laborer, Lon Thida earns between $ 200 and $ 300. As a widow raising children and mothers, the income from work between more than $ 200 to $ 300 makes her daily life more difficult.
Despite the hardships of life, Lon Thida is committed to educating her two sons. Ms. Lon Thida is of the opinion that only education, only knowledge, can help her children have a better future and avoid difficult situations like hers today.
She also told Fresh News that every day, despite being tired at work and at home, she monitors her children's education and always educates their children to study hard. 249 Former Candlelight Party Members and Other Parties in O'Chrov District, Banteay Meanchey Province Apply to Join the CPP
