It is the first time in nearly six years that a US submarine, the SSGN, or a cruise missile-equipped submarine has docked in South Korea. In April this year, South Korean President Yoon Soo-yul and US President Joe Biden agreed in Washington to further increase US strategic weapons on the Korean Peninsula.
At the time, the two leaders also agreed that Washington would send a nuclear ballistic missile (SSBN) submarine to visit South Korea for the first time since the 1980s to help demonstrate The United States' commitment to defending South Korea from North Korean attacks. However, no specific date has been given for the visit of the nuclear submarine.
The arrival of the US nuclear-powered submarine comes after North Korea fired two short-range ballistic missiles on Thursday this week after a failed attempt. Launched Pyongyang's first spy satellite last month.
