Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak said the Philippines is a good market as the country has high demand for rice and is currently experiencing food shortages.
He pointed out that this is the first time exports to the Philippines have been made after the Philippines changed its rice import policy from state to private. At the same time, the new Prime Minister of the Philippines was the Minister of Agriculture, who urged Cambodia to work closely with him and reach out to import rice from Cambodia for the first time.
"This is a starting point to hope for more because the Philippines is a country that needs rice and he sees that our rice is good, delicious, affordable and has a lot of exports," he said.
According to the report of the Rice Federation of Cambodia, at the beginning of 2023, Cambodia just exported the first large volume of 2,575 tons of rice to the Philippines.
According to the Minister of Commerce, in addition to exporting to the Philippines for the first time, Cambodia has also started exporting to Singapore, but in small quantities.
Please note that the Philippines is a rice producer and also a major importer of rice in Asia. In fact, in 2022, the Philippines imported 3.82 million tons of rice from countries, most of which are plain white rice.
