Senior official of the Ministry of Environment: Cambodia loses millions of dollars a year due to climate change (Video inside) (Pursat): A senior official of the Ministry of Environment said that according to previous studies, Cambodia lost millions of dollars in Every year due to climate change.
Speaking to the media during a campaign with the media and journalists on Cambodia's climate change program in Pursat province, Chuob Paris, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Environment, said: "Cambodia loses hundreds of millions of dollars a year from the wind. "The demolition of houses, floods, flooding of crops, damage to infrastructure, roads, schools and drought, the loss of crops of many people."
However, compared to other countries, it is far more difficult than Cambodia, such as the Philippines, because the countries in this archipelago often change the climate, which greatly affects the development of the country.
It should be noted that the macroeconomic report entitled "Cambodian Impact of Economic Growth Model" prepared by the Ministry of Finance and the National Council for Sustainable Development with technical support from UNDP (UNDP) said. By 2050, climate change will affect labor productivity due to the rising temperature, which is the main cause of workers fatigue and reduced work activity.
Climate change is causing more floods, droughts and hurricanes, which will reduce resource productivity, especially in agriculture and fisheries, and will increase damage due to severe weather events affecting roads, water supplies and infrastructure. Other infrastructure.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration Continues to Bid for 2023 Commune / Sangkat Development Fund Project in 3 Communes in Stung Hav District to Develop and Facilitate Local Travel
(Preah Sihanouk): Stung Hav District Administration received the 2023 Commune / Sangkat Development Fund project, which will receive the construction of concrete roads to facilitate the travel of people in the three communes received: Otres Commune, Commune Kampenh and Tumnup Rolok commune, located in Stung Hav district, Preah Sihanouk province.
The communes that received the three commune development fund projects were made after the bidding for the joint fund project was held at Otres Commune Hall on the morning of June 13, 2023, with the coordination of Mr. Sao Borey Vattanak, District Governor. Stung Hav and Mr. Kheang Phearum, Director of Investment Planning, Chairman of the District Council, 3 Commune Chiefs, Provincial Technical Working Group, 3 Commune Procurement Committees and companies that submitted bids.
Mr. Kheang Phearum said that in order to solve the difficulties for the local people, the Commune Development Fund Project 2023 has launched a series of auctions throughout Sihanoukville.
In fact, this morning, June 13, the Stung Hav District Administration has opened a bid for the 2023 Commune / Sangkat Development Fund.
The director of the office emphasized that the bidding project was carried out smoothly in accordance with the procedures and transparently in accordance with the standard of the whole process, and as a result, Kampenh commune project to build a concrete road, 250 meters long and 5 meters wide, Tumnup Rolok commune has a 300-meter-long, 5-meter-wide, 0.15-meter-thick concrete road project in Otres commune.
In that, the owner of the bidding company has committed and implemented the construction according to the design plan. The company that did not receive the bid also said that the bidding was transparent and acceptable.
At the same time, the director of the management, after receiving the successful bid, he instructed all companies to build the road according to the design standards to be good and durable for the people and ask the local authorities. The impact of the people must be addressed peacefully so that the process of road construction is smooth, fast and fast for the people to use in time.
