After a wide-ranging discussion, all members pledged to continue to work together to fight, prevent and eradicate the spread of HIV and to work together to end HIV / AIDS by 2025 and to sustain the AIDS Response Program 2023. 2028 The second plenary meeting of the National AIDS Authority 2022 sets out the following decisions:
* First, promote the strategy to achieve the 95th goal (95% of people living with HIV are aware of their HIV status) by promoting HIV / AIDS prevention work. Efficacy and motivation for skeptics to get HIV testing services as soon as possible.
* Second, the Ministry of Tourism continues the mechanism to encourage all entertainment establishments, hotels and entertainment venues across the country to participate in the implementation of the policy of 100% condom use widely.
* Third, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports promotes education and dissemination of awareness about HIV and AIDS in schools, public and private higher education institutions to prevent and reduce HIV infection among young people.
* Fifth: Support the launch of the National AIDS Eradication Policy by 2025 and the sustainability of the AIDS Response Program 2023-2028.
