"National Policy on Cashew 2022-2027" is officially launched, pushing Cambodia to become the Cashew Emperor
(Phnom Penh): "National Policy on Cashew 2022-2027" was officially launched by the Ministry of Commerce on the afternoon of June 14, 2023, which will be an effective driving force for strengthening the productivity of Cashew production, exports to push Cambodia to become the next cashew emperor.
The launching ceremony of the National Policy on Cashew 2022-2027 was presided over by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and was attended by leaders of the Ministry of Commerce, leaders and representatives of ministries, institutions, governors. The 25 development partners of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, the Cambodian Cashew Federation, the Cambodian Cashew Association, associations and the private sector, a total of about 250 people.
At the same time, he mentioned the potential of Cambodian cashew, which is an agro-industrial crop and one of the priority crops that the Royal Government has been focusing on increasing productivity and competitiveness through quality. High value processing and exports.
He added, "This national policy aims to develop cashew production, processing and marketing, ensure sustainability and economic diversification, and aim to turn Cambodia into an important producer and supplier of cashew products." "Local, regional and global markets."
At the same time, he strongly believes that the introduction of the National Policy on Cashew 2022-2027 will help promote the development of the Cambodian cashew sector to turn Cambodia into a large cashew processing and export country soon. In the future, in accordance with the highest recommendation of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
According to sources from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, cashew production in 2022 will have a cultivated area of 435,733 hectares, a harvested area of 330 61 hectares, a yield of 508,283 tons, and exports of raw cashew nuts 471,520 tons and exports. 1557 tons of processed cashew nuts.
