General Sem Sovanny presents National Defense Medal to 800 Veterans in Siem Reap Province
(Siem Reap): General Sem Sovanny, Second Vice President of the Cambodian Mines Authority and Director General of the National Peacekeeping Center and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Banteay Srei District on June 14, 2023. To 800 Cambodian Veterans in Banteay Srei District, Siem Reap Province
In this ceremony, General Sem Sovanny brought greetings to all veterans from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense.
General Sem Sovanny said that all the veterans who came to join today, they have been serving in the army for a long time, some of them from the 286th unit, from the 179th unit, the 196th unit and so on. From other units came together, expressing the joy of gathering together as ex-combatants served together.
Together, they joined the army, joined Samdech Techo to find peace for the country and the people of Cambodia, and thanked Samdech Techo for allowing this talk.
General Sem Sovanny stated that under the leadership of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen used his life as a capital to seek complete peace for the people throughout the country and led the country with continuous development every day and make Cambodia Have equal rights on the international stage.
General Sem Sovanny called on all of them to go to the polls for the 7th legislature on July 23, 2023 and vote for those who have sought complete peace to lead a country as developed as it is today.
After the meeting, General Sem Sovanny paid a personal visit, expressing his happiness, smiling and showing his nostalgia to each other.
In this ceremony, General Sem Sovanny brought Samdech Techo's precious gift to distribute to all 800 veterans, each received a krama and 50,000 Riels.
