Cambodia thanks the Czech Republic for its continued support for the health sector, especially during the global crisis of the Kovid-19 epidemic.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Youk Sambath, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, thanked the Czech Republic for its support of the Cambodian health sector, especially the National Children's Hospital, during the Cambodian and global crises epidemic crisis. The Czech Republic has provided some medical assistance to the National Children's Hospital to prevent a response to the Kovid-19 epidemic.
The Permanent Secretary of State expressed her congratulations on the occasion of the 67th Anniversary of the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between Cambodia and the Czech Republic, which highlighted the traditional good relations and the growing cooperation between the two countries, bringing harmony. And sustainable socio-economic progress for the people of both countries, which will also contribute to peace, stability and development in the region and the world.
The Permanent Secretary of State also emphasized that these great achievements came from the proactive leadership, long-term vision and wisdom of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, especially in maintaining peace, political stability, security, order and social security. Kovid 19 - Maintaining economic growth, growth and livelihood stability, promoting Cambodia's prestige on the regional and international stage through independent foreign policy based on the rule of law.
