(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce has officially launched an automated system for applying for a business license or license electronically to facilitate the application for a business license.
The ceremony to announce the launch of this automation system took place on the morning of June 14, 2023, presided over by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce. The ceremony was also attended by the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, advisors and leaders of the Ministry of Commerce.
The Minister added that the Royal Government approved the Law on Electronic Commerce on November 2, 2019 and Sub-Decree No. 134, dated August 27, 2020 on determining the types, procedures and procedures of Issuance of licenses or licenses to intermediaries and individuals providing e-commerce services and exemptions.
Pursuant to the above laws and sub-decrees, the Royal Government has entrusted the Ministry of Commerce with the responsibility to manage and grant licenses or licenses to intermediaries and individuals providing e-commerce services, and the Ministry of Commerce has issued a Prakas on the issuance of licenses or Licenses to brokers and individuals providing e-commerce services since October 9, 2020.
The Minister also stated that the automation system has two stages: the first stage for applying for a license or license and the second stage for applying for various modifications, and the team has prepared 100 percent for the first stage, which will be Connect with CamDX technology nursery as well. The second phase will begin development after the first phase is connected to the CamDX technology nursery.
During the ceremony, the Minister thanked the leaders of the Ministry and professional officials, including INTECH DAV CO., LTD. Co-working with the Ministry of Commerce to set up this automation system and expressed strong hope that this automation system will be part of the promotion of e-commerce better.
The telephone meeting between Qin and Blinken comes ahead of the US Secretary of State's visit to Beijing this Sunday. In February this year, Blinken canceled a planned visit to China after the high-altitude balloon incident, which Washington accused of being a Chinese spy balloon over US airspace.
The February visit is part of an agreement reached between Xi Jinping and US President Joe Biden, who met in Indonesia in November 2022 with the aim of easing tensions. That includes the decision to send Blinken to Beijing.
Minister Prum Sokha delivers a lecture on "Innovative and Qualitative Leadership in Public Administration" to Professors, Civil Servants and Students of the Royal University of Fine Arts
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Works and Chairman of the Public Administration Reform Committee, gave a lecture on "Innovative and Qualitative Leadership in Public Administration" to professors, civil servants and students at the Royal University of Fine Arts. .
The ceremony took place on the morning of June 13, 2023 at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall, with the participation of leaders and officials of the Ministry of Public Works, as well as the management team, professors, civil servants, students and monks of the Royal University of Fine Arts. 700 units / person.
Following the welcoming remarks by Dr. Heng Sophady, Rector of the Royal University of Fine Arts, Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Works, began his lecture on "Leadership, Innovation and Merit in Public Administration", focusing on five key topics. Including: First. Leadership and innovation II. Companion 3. Public Administration Reform 4. The role of the government and 5th. Conclusion.
Through this lecture, the Minister highlighted some of the case studies that occur in the world around leadership, especially in Cambodia, the high leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister. Bring Cambodia out of war, from national division, bring Cambodian society to peace, national unity and prosperous development today.
Minister Prum Sokha sincerely hopes that through this shared lecture, it will become an inspiration for all students who participate now to be able to use it for the benefit of career building, life and future. Its.
Please be informed that this is the 15th lecture of the Minister and for this year 2023, he has already shared his knowledge to students, civil servants at various universities, approximately 6,000 people / person.
