The Minister of Health thanked the benefactors who volunteered to donate blood to save lives and continue to call for more good deeds for the society.
(Phnom Penh): Speaking on the occasion of the World Blood Donor Day on June 14, 2023, Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, thanked all the donors who volunteered to donate blood to save lives and Continue to call for more good deeds for our society.
Minister Mam Bunheng expressed his pleasure to participate in the blood donation campaign under the theme "Together we can donate blood and plasma many times to save lives" on June 14, 2023, which is World Day. Mr. of blood donors.
"I think that our people, grandchildren, youth, students, artists, employees of private companies, civil servants invited at this time is really aware that donating blood is a good deed because we hope "That really saved the lives of people or our dear friends."
In addition, the Minister realized that the movement of participation of young people, students, artists, employees of private companies, government officials in donating blood can create a good culture for our society, meaning that we can donate blood, plasma. Many times to save lives. Despite the failure to mark World Blood Donor Day three years ago due to the Kovid-19 crisis.
On this happy and meaningful occasion, the Professor thanked the Phnom Penh Administration, the Cambodian Red Cross, the Phnom Penh Branch, the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, the Club of Love, Universities, Cambodian Blood Donors Association, private companies and partners with the National Center. Donate all your blood to sponsor the campaign.
At the same time, the Minister expressed his appreciation for the attention of civil servants and staff of the National Blood Transfusion Center who have worked hard to organize this campaign and have contributed to the improvement of health services. At the same time, I would like to thank all the volunteers who donated blood, are donating blood and continue to donate blood regularly every year to save lives.
Please be informed that the National Blood Transfusion Center celebrated the World Blood Donor Day on June 14, 2023 to celebrate and thank all the voluntary blood donors and encourage young men and women to become As more and more new blood donors, healthy people should continue to donate blood regularly to save the lives of all types of patients.
Of course, some patients need blood for the rest of their lives. Regular voluntary blood or plasma donations can make the supply of blood and blood products safer to meet the needs of patients at any time, which the people of each country can do.
