The UNHCR said in its annual report released on Wednesday that about 19 million people were forced to flee in 2022, the largest annual increase on record. A total of 108.4 million people by the end of 2022.
Since then, that number has risen to 110 million, mostly due to Sudan's eight-week conflict. This also includes those seeking safety in their own country as well as those who have crossed the border abroad.
Prior to the Syrian conflict in 2011, there were only about 40 million refugees and had been stable for about 20 years, but the number has increased every year since then.
