On the occasion of continuing to visit nearly 20,000 workers in Phnom Penh this morning, June 14, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that this ceremony will be held at the Ministry of National Defense without going directly to the area. Koh Thmor, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the commemoration will be attended by officers, deputies and soldiers, who will present what happened by highlighting the historical factors related to the political victory. Victory and departure of the prince in the journey to seek national liberation.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "June 20 is the 46th anniversary of the journey to national liberation. Uncle had to go to the Ministry of National Defense to introduce himself. "Where it used to be, but we will talk to the army to reconcile all the historical factors related to the political victory and the departure and the role of the uncle in the process of national liberation."
In this sense, Samdech Techo Prime Minister, who dared to use his life as capital to liberate the country from the flames of war, still reminds the invaluable value of "peace" to all workers to make them Participate in maintaining and safeguarding the peace that Cambodia is having now to have the opportunity to continue its development.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that please do not remember when peace is lost, then let's shout for peace, that is, to maintain the peace that Cambodia is having. The prince stressed that war is very easy to happen because it is decided in just a few minutes, it will explode immediately, so it is very difficult to be like today, so we must work together to maintain peace and achievements.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Yesterday I met with nephew San Sochea In the past, he used to preach, but now we are looking for support, and we also need the monks who have left the seminary. "Knowing the right dharma is continuing according to Buddhism, helping to educate society, educate the mind, how to use dharma for peacekeeping, maintaining political stability, and especially building good deeds in society for our people."
Please note that Mr. San Sochea has been studying Dharma under the shadow of Buddhism for more than 30 years. He gained high popularity among the Buddhists through his propaganda, enlightenment, and interpretation of the Dharma.
Mr. San Sochea left the seminar on May 21, 2023 in Australia. Despite leaving the seminary, Mr. San Sochea continued his seminary as a layman and continued to spread the Dharma.
