(Phnom Penh): On Wednesday, June 14, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued to meet with a total of nearly 20,000 workers from Nine factories operating in Phnom Penh. The meeting took place at a land location in Por Sen Chey district.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that in 2017 and 2018, Samdech Techo Prime Minister had already met with workers in Phnom Penh 14 times, with more than 210,000 workers.
According to the Minister, the nine factories that allow workers to meet with Samdech Techo include: six garment factories, one travel product and one bag, and two shoes. The products of these factories are exported to international markets such as the European Union, the United States, Canada and Japan.
Phnom Penh, the heart of Cambodia, is a potential trade and investment center under government policy. In 2023, Phnom Penh has 9,314 factories with more than 660,000 workers. There are 727 garment factories with a total of more than 338,000 workers.
Today's meeting is the 11th meeting for the second round. The 11 meetings had a total of about 210,000 workers. Samdech Techo plans to meet eight more times, which will meet a total of 135,000 workers.
