India urges Myanmar to speed up trade in local currency (Video inside) (New Delhi): India urges Myanmar government to speed up trade settlement process Use the currencies of the two countries as a mechanism previously agreed upon. According to Reuters.
Myanmar, which is facing a shortage of foreign exchange reserves, announced last year that it would soon adopt the Indian rupee, along with the Thai baht and Chinese yuan, as official payment currencies for trade. To reduce dependence on the US dollar.
The EEPC said the agreement would facilitate the export of medicines and manufactured goods from India, as well as more imports of goods such as grain, timber and other products from Myanmar.
Shah said trade between the two countries would increase significantly from the current level of $ 1.8 billion when a new trade mechanism using the local currency was launched.
Under the mechanism, Myanmar will accept payment for all of its exports to India in Indian rupee, and the same export earnings can be used to settle, the EEPC said. Prices of goods and services imported from India. According to Reuters.
