Within the framework of the Special Fund for Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation 2023, a total of nine Cambodian projects will receive financial support of approximately US $ 2,000,000 (US $ 2 million). These projects will be more effective in areas such as transportation and logistics, information technology, food security, research, capacity building, as well as heritage conservation.
NBC Senior Official: Identity card, family book or residence book is not a collateral item, it is strictly forbidden to accept credit.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Rath Sovannarak, Assistant Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia (NBC), once again reminded that all banking and financial institutions are not allowed to take ID cards, family books or books from customers to provide credit because of both This is a letter, not a valuable collateral.
Mr. Rath Sovannarak's Remarks was made during the opening of the dissemination workshop on “Microfinance in Cambodia to Stakeholders in Santuk District, Kampong Thom Province on 13 June 2023.
Mr. Rath Sovannarak requested the relevant authorities, especially local authorities to participate in educating and explaining to the people who use their local loans to understand the benefits of using the loan, that is, all loans must be used on purpose and in accordance with Repayment obligation.
At the same time, educate the people not to fall prey to the irrational propaganda of scammers or illegal moneylenders, as all loans must be targeted and comply with repayment obligations. Borrowing must be done at a microfinance institution recognized by law to get out of debt and get progress for the family.
Mr. Rath Sovannarak stated, "The National Bank of Cambodia still strictly prohibits all banking institutions and financial institutions from accepting ID cards or original family and residence books for permanent or binding purposes to provide credit because these documents "This is a letter, not a valuable item for collateral."
According to the information sharing report of the Cambodian Microfinance Association, in the first quarter of 2023, about 18,000 families in Santuk district received loans with a total loan amount of approximately 69 million US dollars from microfinance institutions. 17 items operating locally.
Mr. Sok Voeun, Chairman of the Board of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia, stated at the dissemination school on "Microfinance in Cambodia" organized by the National Bank of Cambodia on June 13, 2023 in Santuk District, Kampong Thom Province.
Mr. Sok Voeun said that with the provision of loans to the people, the 17 microfinance institutions operating in Santuk district also received deposits from about 18,700 customers with a total deposit balance of 3 million US dollars.
The President of the Association noted that the microfinance sector is currently growing significantly, reflecting the growth of the financial environment, including credit balances, as well as deposits have increased steadily and more. Improving financial literacy among Cambodians. The 37th two-day ICC-Angkor Technical Committee successfully concludes
