Thank you, Dr. Kantha Bopha! Pediatric brain tumor successfully removed within 8 hours
(Phnom Penh): The sadness of the parents and family of the boy Lim Ranout has become fresh and happy after the big tumor in the brain of the boy was successfully removed by the teachers. Kantha Bopha Hospital, Wat Phnom location, 8 hours.
Lim Ranout, a 13-year-old boy from Kampi village, Sambok commune, Chit Borei district, Kratie province, was brought by his parents for treatment at Kantha Bopha Hospital, Wat Phnom branch last week. Lim Ranout has been suffering from a headache for about two years. Every time a headache occurs, the mother takes painkillers for the child to swallow without knowing the source of the illness.
Two years later, when the tumor grew bigger, the painkillers were no longer effective, so it was decided to take the child to Kantha Bopha Hospital, a large charitable doctor in Cambodia.
Doctors found that Ranut had a brain tumor and that the tumor was large enough to cover almost the entire brain. The condition requires urgent surgery to save the boy.
Both parents and boy Ranout, a meek child, were shocked and shocked to receive this information. In particular, Ranut, a child who is grateful to his parents, seems to be aware of the life-threatening condition of this disease. They worry about not seeing their parents, not studying, not seeing their little brother at home, especially not seeing the beauty of this planet.
Upon hearing of his condition, Ranut urged doctors to rescue him as best he could. After a thorough follow-up in accordance with medical rules, a team of doctors at Kantha Bopha Hospital, led by Dr. Kong Vuthy, opened the operation of Koranut on Tuesday morning, June 13.
Dr. Kisanti, director of Kantha Bopha Hospital in Cambodia, told Fresh News that the operation to remove the brain tumor took up to eight hours without a doctor's leave. He said that before the surgeons discussed in detail, making a clear diagnosis through a CT scan of the brain system that received a clear image.
"Surgery of brain tumors is generally at high risk, which requires patience in the entire surgical team, and the surgery is often time consuming," the doctor said. On average, 6 to 8 hours, as is the case today, we operate on the tumor and there is a large tumor in the tumor, which we need 8 hours. "Doctors have to go to the bathroom without food or water. Get ready and stand for up to eight hours."
Dr. Kisenti considers the surgery a success. After surgery, the patient has normal communication with the parents.
However, doctors need to take the tumor further analysis to see if the tumor is malignant or benign. If the rash is further treated with chemotherapy or radiation therapy.
The director of Kantha Bopha Hospital in Cambodia also said that neurosurgery at Kantha Bopha Hospital can be done by Cambodian doctors who have nearly 10 years of experience and regularly exchange experiences with doctors in France.
"Fifteen years ago, when a child had a tumor or a brain tumor, we could not afford treatment and the child was at risk of death. But for almost 10 years now, we have helped a lot of children and our children are destined to live and learn. ” This is the confirmation of Dr. Kisanti.
Dr. Kisanti added, "Our children are lucky that we have a Kantha Bopha doctor in particular and the leadership of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia, the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Switzerland, which allows us to save children and reduce the pain of children from "Many serious diseases that contribute to the health and well-being of children under the leadership of the Ministry of Health."
With joy after seeing the successful operation, Ranut's parents expressed their deep gratitude to the director of the hospital, the surgeons, as well as all the doctors in Kantha Bopha Hospital for their hard work. Mind and knowledge save your child from the scourge of this tumor.
The boy's parents also thanked Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, for her regular monitoring of the tumor operation.
