NEC starts registering political party agents from 14 to 20 June 2023
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has issued a press release on the registration of political party agents from June 14 to 20, 2023.
Meeting with Election Stakeholders chaired by Mr. Duch Son, Member of the NEC and Chair of the Meeting Protect the security of candidates and the registration of political party agents in the 7th National Assembly election on July 23, 2023.
Mr. Duchson stated that the parliamentary elections must be held in a proportional system, with the provincial capital as the constituency. There are 125 seats in the National Assembly (one hundred and twenty-five) divided by capital and provincial constituencies. He also recalled the process of registration of political parties and the list of candidates that has just been completed, with 18 political parties officially recognized to participate in the 7th National Assembly election in 2023.
Regarding the right to security of candidates, Mr. Duch Son stated that all candidates and all political parties have equal rights to protect security and safety during the election period as stated in the laws and regulations. Code of Conduct and Inter-Institutional Planning between the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of National Defense and the NEC.
He said that if a candidate could provide evidence or there was a clear reason that his security and safety were being threatened, he could immediately appeal to the NEC for a working meeting. Security to resolve complaints by opening an investigation and at the same time taking all necessary measures to provide security and safety to candidates.
He added that once the investigation finds evidence of threats to the security and safety of candidates, the NEC must address the election law and procedures.
Mr. Duch Son stated that Candidates for the National Assembly, Governor, Deputy Governor of the Capital, Province, Municipality, District, Khan, Councilors of the Capital, Province, Municipality, District, Khan, Commune, Sangkat, Village Chief, Assistant Village Chief and the Armed Forces are not allowed. Act as a political party agent to observe the election process and count the ballots at all stages.
