Neak Oknha Kith Meng and Family Donate 20 Million Riels to Angkor Hospital for Children through Wing Bank
(Phnom Penh): Duke Kith Meng and his family donated 20 million Riels to Angkor Hospital for Children on the occasion of the "10th Solidarity Flower Festival" which was held for the purpose of raising funds for medical treatment. Free Cambodian Pediatrics.
This year 2023 is the fourth year that the duke and his family through Wing Bank have supported this hospital. In addition, Wing Bank has always provided a means for Angkor Hospital for Children to receive free donations from various philanthropists to contribute to the hospital's sustainable operations.
"Children are the future pillar of the nation," said Hor Bunthe, Deputy General Manager of Wing Bank. Therefore, we need to ensure that our children are healthy. "I see this Solidarity Flower Festival as a great initiative that allows the public to contribute to working together to improve children's health as well as our society."
Currently, Angkor Hospital for Children plays an important role in rescuing Cambodian children. According to statistics from Angkor Hospital for Children, in 2022, the hospital provided free consultation and treatment services to more than 97,978 children nationwide, and an average of more than 300 children per day visited the hospital. This. This is a charity work of the hospital has positively contributed to the health and well-being of many Cambodian children.
Dr. Nguon Chanpheaktra, President of Angkor Hospital for Children, said, “We would like to thank the Duke and his family for their continued support as well as Wing Bank for their charitable activities in support of Angkor Hospital for Children. Saving the lives of Cambodian children. We believe that every child deserves good health and careful care. ”
Funds raised by philanthropists for the "10th Solidarity Flower Festival" will be used for operations as well as sustainability of medical supplies, equipment, as well as staff training and for infrastructure improvements. Of the hospital as well.
According to Angkor Hospital for Children, the hospital needs more than $ 6 million a year to operate and support its medical services.
