Cambodia-China Friendship Radio Mine Authority meets with 4th Military Zone to prepare for demining work in 4th Military Zone in Preah Vihear and Oddar Meanchey Provinces
(Siem Reap): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has brought many great historical achievements for the country and the people of Cambodia, including demining work for more than 30 years. Without Samdech Techo leading Cambodia, there would be no demining work and the Cambodian people would continue to suffer from landmines and explosive remnants of war.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chairman of the Mine Authority, expressed his deep gratitude and appreciation to the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces for participating in liberating the country from the genocidal regime under the high leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister. .
The Senior Minister praised the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces for all sacrifices and sacrifices for the peace and cause of the motherland, as well as for helping to save the lives of the people by clearing mines and explosive remnants of war during the nation. Get complete peace.
The Senior Minister added that without Samdech Techo Hun Sen's peace, no demining achievements would have been possible and the participation of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces was necessary and indispensable.
At the same time, the Senior Minister mentioned two important points in the demining work in Cambodia. Providing safe land and rescuing Cambodians everywhere is a great desire of Samdech Techo to see all Cambodians, both urban and rural, free from the threat of landmines and secondly. Respond to the Ottawa Convention, of which Cambodia is a member of the State Party, with the obligation to clear all mines from Cambodia.
The Senior Minister continued that in response to both points, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has set out a clear vision to lead Cambodia to end the landmine threat known by 2025 as stated in the 2018 Mine Action Strategic Plan. 2025, in which the participation of the Army is an indispensable part.
According to Lt. Gen. Ouch Vantha's report, since 2022, the Army has been involved in humanitarian demining, with technical support and resources from the Mine Authority through the Samdech Techo Mine Action Project and the Cambodia Mine Action Fund 2025.
Currently, the Army has been deploying 35 demining forces and preparing up to 45 troops to participate in the humanitarian demining. By 2023, the Army has received demining plans from the Mine Authority for more than 46 square kilometers in Banteay Meanchey and Oddar Meanchey provinces, achieving 90% of the plan and is scheduled to be completed in July 2023.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Ouch Vantha, on behalf of the Commander of the Army, would like to express his deep gratitude to the Mine Authority for always providing both material and technical support to the Army in the demining work in Cambodia.
