Ministry of Environment Organizes 4-Day Media Awareness Program on "Fighting Climate Change in Cambodia" in Pursat
(Pursat): The Ministry of Environment, in collaboration with the Pursat Provincial Department of Environment, organized a 4-day mainstreaming program on "Fighting Climate Change in Cambodia" with local journalists from 13 to 15 June. 2023 in Pursat province.
The training was conducted in the presence of Mr. Chuob Paris, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Khvay Atiya, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, Director of the Pursat Provincial Department of Environment, and the participation of experts from the Ministry of Environment, representatives of conservation organizations and about 20 national journalists. People.
Through this program, journalists learn more about carbon credit and the REDD + program, livelihood development in protected areas, the impact of ecotourism, culture and social development.
The Undersecretary of State continued that in accordance with the high leadership recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, who is allowed to meet with journalists once a year on January 14 every year, the campaign project with the media and local journalists related to The environment sector will further contribute to the journalists' good relations and dialogue with the Royal Government, especially in the field of environment and natural resources.
In line with the specific objectives of the Royal Government of Cambodia, with the Ministry of Environment as the staff to strengthen the capacity of journalists from environmental knowledge to contribute to a wider dissemination of the 2050 target strategy for zero emissions. Xi Jinping says China is willing to start free trade talks with Honduras
BEIJING: Chinese President Xi Jinping said on Monday that China is willing to start talks on a free trade agreement with Honduras "as soon as possible". This is according to the publication by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, June 13, 2023.
Xi made the remarks during the first visit of President Honduras to Beijing since the establishment of diplomatic ties in March.
According to state-run CCTV, Xi said China will actively promote Honduras products into its markets. China also encourages Chinese enterprises to participate in Honduras's investment projects in areas such as energy, infrastructure and telecommunications.
Honduras began diplomatic relations with Beijing after severing ties with Taiwan and is also seeking Chinese support to reduce its debt burden.
