Since the railway opened in December 2021, the train has carried 4,097,300 tons of imported and exported goods, Xinhua reported citing the Lao news agency KPL on Monday.
Most of the goods shipped from Laos to China include rubber, iron ore, zinc ore, lime, fruit, potato starch and barley. Meanwhile, products shipped from China to Laos include electrical appliances, spare parts and home appliances.
Business operators in Laos, Thailand, Vietnam, Cambodia and Myanmar are using the China-Laos railway to transport goods to and from China, according to Xinhua.
Thailand is transporting more and more goods to China by rail, mostly agricultural products. It takes three days to transport goods by train faster than by road.
The China-Laos Railway, a major project that demonstrates high-quality belt and road cooperation, was launched in December 2021. The railway crosses a 1,035-kilometer border connecting the southwestern Chinese city of Kunming with the Lao capital Vientiane.
Cambodia will sell carbon credits on the voluntary market in 2024 in three more natural resource protection areas (Video inside) (Pursat): Chuob Paris, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Environment, said that under the Cambodian government's efforts to preserve the forest Provide opportunities for Cambodia to earn revenue from forests, while three more natural resource protection zones will be sold carbon credits on the voluntary market in 2024.
On the morning of June 13, 2023, Mr. Chuob Paris told reporters at the Pursat Provincial Department of Environment that the three natural resource protection areas were: Phnom Samkos, and the northern part of the lake. Tonle Sap, Preah Vihear province and 3rd: Kandal Kravanh mountain range.
Mr. Chuob Paris said that for the past 10 years, under the leadership of HE Say Sam Al, 7.2 million hectares of forest have been designated as protected areas, and Cambodia has reached another milestone: we have protected the forest. Keep the forest standing and get the original income until we cut the trees to get the money, now we keep the forest standing to earn income by selling carbon credits.
Mr. Chuob Paris emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia, with the Ministry of Environment as its staff, will do its best to use the forest function to attract revenue.
He said that after Cambodia achieved full peace, there were opportunities and opportunities to protect and conserve natural resources, which changed the context of Cambodia, from logging for money, but turning to saving timber to earn a living. Income that carbon credit and through tourism seals the territory.
It should be noted that Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, once said that Cambodia has ambitions to expand the area of carbon credit sales to more than 2 million hectares, while now Cambodia has more than 1.4 million. Hectares are sold carbon credits on the voluntary market. Areas for the implementation of the carbon credit market include: Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary, Cardamom Mountain Range, Koh Kong Province, Pursat Province.
To date, Cambodia has sold carbon credits to major international companies with environmental responsibility, and the proceeds from the sale of carbon credits have been used to strengthen, protect, conserve and conserve natural resources. On economic development for local communities.
Proceeds from the sale of carbon credits will be donated to local communities around wildlife sanctuaries across the country to help protect and conserve national and wildlife resources, especially to strengthen people's economies to eliminate old-fashioned logging. Hunting wood and so on.
Since 2016, the Ministry of Environment has organized and is implementing three REDD + projects, including: REDD + Keo Seima, REDD + Cardamom South and REDD + Prey Lang. The three REDD + projects have so far received about $ 11.6 million from the sale of carbon credits, which have been distributed to local communities. Preah Keto Mealea Hospital Introduces MRI, Medical and Surgical Techniques to Physicians
