Buffalo chased at Poipet fish market, injuring 6 people
(Banteay Meanchey): A buffalo ran into a fish market and chased people, causing six injuries. This incident happened on June 12, 2023 in Kbal Spean 2 village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet city.
Taing Ly Heng, a member of O'Chrov commune council, said that a male buffalo had thrown into a fish market north of Poipet's Akka market, chasing a motorcyclist on the street, injuring six people, four of them seriously. People were rescued at Poipet City Referral Hospital.
O'Chrov Sangkat Councilor confirmed that after the male buffalo chased the villagers, the police and the military police together with the villagers chased the buffalo to ensure its safety after spending. Nearly two hours later, a villager sneaked close to the buffalo, touched the egg and head, took the leash and tied the four legs and took it to the Poipet City Inspectorate.
Mr. Taing Ly Heng confirmed that after arresting one male buffalo, he chased the villagers, causing six minor injuries, and the buffalo was taken and kept at the Poipet City Police Inspectorate. The owner of the buffalo above is also responsible for the law. People in Khleang Meas commune are happy after the working group leader helped the commune CPP to open a new road paved with red stone
