Lt. Gen. Yim Leang Praises Bodyguard Department's Success in Defending Important National Events and Leaders
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Yim Leang, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, praised all the bodyguards of the National Police General Commission for their successful work in the past, especially in providing security in important events. Cambodia hosts and hosts national and international leaders who visit Cambodia.
Lt. Gen. Yim Leang made the remarks on the morning of June 12, 2023, on the occasion of presiding over the ceremony of announcing the position and equipping the rank of Deputy Chief of Police of the Bodyguard Department.
Lt. Gen. Yim Leang emphasized that the historic achievements in the defense plan of the 40th and 41st ASEAN Summits, the 43rd IPA General Assembly and related meetings under the chairmanship of Cambodia have made the Department of Bodyguards Received praise from senior leaders of the Ministry of Interior, leaders of the National Police and other relevant institutions.
The Deputy Chief of the National Police also claimed that the bodyguard also played an important role in protecting security, order and safety in the recent major events such as the Sea Festival, Angkor event. Sangkran, the 32nd SEA Games 2023 and the 12th ASEAN Para Games for the Disabled.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Yim Leang also introduced and instructed some important work as follows:
* First: Be loyal to the nation, religion, the King and the Royal Government
* Second: To implement the policies of the Royal Government, especially to adhere to the five approaches of Samdech Techo Hun Sen: mirroring, diving, scrubbing, treatment and surgery.
* Third: To respect the law, the discipline of the police force and other regulations, to strive to do a good job set by the General Commission of the National Police.
* Fourth: Must strive to serve the interests of the nation and the people and must not do anything to harm the interests of the nation and the people
* Fifth: Must have a spirit of solidarity, good cooperation with colleagues and with relevant offices, units and institutions
* Sixth: To strive to learn in all areas of police work, law, discipline, ethics, professionalism, technical skills to increase the understanding and experience in insuring all the tasks assigned by superiors.
* Seventh: To continue to improve the quality of bodyguard police officers by adopting exemplary activities with dignity and virtue in order to enhance the honor, prestige and excellence of the National Police Force.
