(Kampong Speu): Mr. Muong Sopheak, Chief of the Young Researchers, who visited the Suramarit Kosamak National Park "Kirirom" directly claimed that there was no deforestation in the Kirirom area as alleged by some crooks. But the area is increasingly booming in eco-tourism.
He found that the companies that invest in the Suramarit Kosamak National Park "Kirirom" are all companies that invest in ecotourism, not deforestation, as alleged by the opposition. . The company has also improved the livelihoods of local people by providing employment to people in the area and providing revenue to the Royal Government.
Mr. Muong Sopheak confirmed: “We, the young people, want to come and see for ourselves, who want to know that the area is being destroyed, as he said, in fact, the view in Kirirom is as beautiful as nature from the beginning. "Even the companies he mentioned in the development did not see any demolition and saw that the income of the people here increased more than I had before."
Mr. Sopheak said that the development of ecotourism sites in Preah Suramarit Kosamak Kirirom National Park has attracted more tourists to increase employment opportunities for local people as part of reducing poverty. Migration has also contributed to the elimination of deforestation, logging and hunting.
The head of the Young Researchers group said that the development of tourism areas in national parks or mountainous areas with potential for ecotourism is a development that makes the tourism sector profitable (smoke-free tourism) and brings local income. .
Mr. Muong Sopheak also said that for the development of the national park, the forest area as a natural tourist destination is not only Cambodia. In fact, Thailand has also allowed a company to develop a natural tourism area in a national park.
