Phnom Penh Deputy Governor: E-cigarette products are very dangerous for Cambodian society by destroying the future of children and youth
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Im Ron Hassan, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, stated that e-cigarettes and HTP products are very dangerous for Cambodian society by destroying the future of children and youth, which is an important bamboo vine.
Im Ron Hassan said that the sale, distribution and trading of e-cigarettes and HTP products have been banned since 2014 because these products cause a lot of harm to our society, especially young people and children. Which is an important human resource future that we need to pay close attention to.
He added that the sticky liquid called E-Liquid used in e-cigarettes and HTP products contains many harmful chemicals such as glycerin, propylene glycol and flavoring chemicals. These chemicals are extremely harmful to consumers and inhalers, causing serious lung cancer, heart disease, impaired memory and concentration.
Im Ron Hassan said that the use of these products greatly affects the education of children and young people, moreover, it can lead them to use other drugs. In recent months, the authorities and relevant officials have been active in cracking down on the use, sale, distribution and trade of e-cigarettes and HTP products, which has significantly reduced this illegal business.
On that occasion, Mr. Im Ron Hassan also issued some recommendations to help eliminate e-cigarettes and HTP products such as:
1. Strictly and strictly prohibit the use, sale, distribution and trading of e-cigarettes and HTP products in accordance with the laws of their respective localities. Suppress crimes that occur in the local area 3: Continue to cooperate with the relevant authorities and local people to identify the crime and close the location of this type of business.
According to Dr. Mom Kong, Executive Director of the Cambodian Movement for Health, to prevent children and youth from starting or stop using e-cigarettes, the relevant authorities should have additional legal mechanisms to punish e-cigarette sellers and intervene to ban them. Imported e-cigarette card, because without import, there is no use.
