Ministry of Health Receives Donation of Oxygen Medical Equipment from UNICEF
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Yok Sambath, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, on behalf of Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, received a donation of oxygen medical equipment from UNICEF on the morning of June 12, 2023 at the Food Program Warehouse. The world with the participation of Mr. Wil Parks, UNICEF Country Director for Cambodia.
On behalf of the Ministry of Health, the Permanent Secretary of State thanked UNICEF for its support of the Ministry of Health since 1952 and for returning to Cambodia before any organizations since January 7, 1979.
Dr. Yuk Sambath said that UNICEF has played a prominent role in the system to promote the health and well-being of children in Cambodia through a number of programs, including maternal and child health, immunization, nutrition, hygiene (WASH), and child protection. Both training health workers to identify and respond to cases of child abuse and support the development of child protection policies and systems.
In addition, in response to the Kovid-19 outbreak and ensuring the continuity of vital health services for children and women, especially during the Kovid-19 outbreak, UNICEF provided technical support for Develop national deployment and vaccination plans (NDVP), as well as operational guidelines and protocols, assistance and supplies for COVID-19 vaccine procurement, improvement of cold chain and infection control, prevention and case management.
UNICEF has worked closely with the Ministry of Health to ensure the continuation of immunization services during the epidemic and has provided technical assistance and supplies for vaccination campaigns and upgrades to cold chain equipment and transportation. Vaccines.
