According to the report, 1,450 workers and people who came for medical treatment today, equivalent to 2,917 cases, were referred to partner hospitals for treatment. 17 cases. "Constitution Monument" Construction Begins While Dr. Ly Raksmey As Architect
(Phnom Penh): On June 12, 2023, at the park west of the Independence Monument, the Constitutional Council held a groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the "Constitutional Monument" under the presidency of Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council. Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The ceremony was also attended by Samdech, members of the Constitutional Council, ministers, secretaries of state, representatives of ministries and institutions, as well as leaders, civil servants and contracted national agencies of the General Secretariat of the Constitutional Council.
Dr. Prohm Vichet Akhara, spokesman for the Constitutional Council, said that the construction of the "Constitution Monument" would take 12 to 15 months. Dr. Ly Raksmey, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, was selected as the Architect.
The architectural concepts of the Constitution Palace include:
* Constitution Pillar: A hexagonal pillar at the top with a throne holding the six corners of Shiva for the preface of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia in Khmer and the languages of the five great powers. The pillar is housed in the center of the Constitution Museum, adorned with a square wall.
1: West corner door: The values of the rule of law on the false door of this corner is designed as a Roman style deity, one side is a deity, one side is a man, one side is a woman deity, wearing a crown, dressed like an official, but not wearing ordinary shoes and talking A book on a shining head. This image represents all levels of Cambodian society, including kings, princes, officials, and people from all walks of life under the rule of the Constitution.
2: South Corner Door: Democracy values The false door of this corner has a Roman-style deity design, standing on a pedestal, with the left hand holding the ballot box and the right hand pointing, representing the practice of liberal multiparty democracy. Cambodia, which has basic elections.
3: North Corner Door: The value of the separation of powers of the three powers on the false door of this corner is designed as a Roman-style deity, standing on a pedestal with his right hand holding a trisol, which represents this trisol. The three powers and the right hand holding the Bible represent the exercise of the three powers in accordance with the law.
4: East Corner Gate: The values of human rights on this corner gate are designed in the shape of a rudder, with five radii, inscribed with five rights, including five basic rights: political rights, economic rights, social rights Cultural rights and civil rights. And this circle is inscribed in a triangle as a symbol of the three powers that represent the Cambodian people to exercise their rights through the three powers.
General Plan The current Khmer Constitution is influenced by the Western Constitution, especially from France, in which the design of the Constitutional Monument is based on the two basic concepts of integration:
1: Concept of Roman architecture, designed as a rectangular room, in the center of which is a pillar with the preface of the Constitution, above the room, which represents the 1993 Constitution of Cambodia, which embraces the values of the Constitution. Western.
2: Visit the ancient Khmer architecture designed to hold the constitution on top of the room, which represents the implementation of the 1993 Constitution in the context of the Khmer, a sovereign state with good civilization and traditions since ancient times. Come on.
The general layout of the Constitution Monument was studied based on the combined architectural concept of Trimurti and studied in the style of Piman Akas and Prasat Neak Pean, which Piman Akas represents the village that protects the kingdom. Brahmanical views. As for Neak Pean temple, it was a temple of the Mohanakor Hospital and a symbol of bringing the world to heaven, namely Nirvana according to the views of Khmer Buddhism.
The top of the copper hut is made of seven levels, representing Mount Sumeru, with seven mountains surrounding Mount Sumeru. The pinnacle of the flower symbolizes heaven, Nirvana. This mountain is the location of Chatom Maharajika Tevata and Tavatus Tevata.
* The hive is made of copper, has legs, and is adorned with elaborate pillars and decorative ornaments.
* The quadrangular room represents the four elements, including earth, fire, air, the architectural concept of the Neak Pean temple, a symbol of bringing beings to heaven, namely Nirvana, from the perspective of Khmer Mahayana Buddhism.
* Khoeun is shaped like a cross, has the architectural concept of Neak Pean temple and has a Roman architectural pattern that shows the meaning of the establishment of the Cambodian Constitution.
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Men Eng, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province, on the afternoon of June 11, 2023, led a joint force to crack down on forest land crimes at the Krasaing Forest Rehabilitation and Restoration Station in Romeas Hek District, Svay Rieng Province.
In this mission, Mr. Men Eng, Representative of Mr. Men Vibol, Provincial Governor, and with the participation of Mr. Sou Mol, Governor of Romeas Hek District, and his team, the District Working Group of Tros and Andong Trabek Commune and the three forces and the relevant authorities, a total of 73 People.
