The family, who received this precious gift, was born on June 6, 2023, the second child (the first child, a boy) with a father named Kim Ratharani, 30 years old, a car mechanic and a mother named Lay Sothy Deth, 32 years old. Occupation: Nurse at Calmette Hospital, residence: Doeum Sleng, Sangkat Chbar Ampov II, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh.
On that occasion, Mr. Seng Teang conveyed his deepest condolences from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, both of whom always send their condolences to the people everywhere. In Cambodia.
Mr. Seng Teang continued that all these donations are not gifts from the Royal Government, donations from the Cambodian Red Cross or gifts from political parties, instead, they are gifts from the heart. Highly thoughtful Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit who have realized the real difficulties for people who have given birth to three or four twin babies.
Ms. Lay Sothy Det expressed her deepest gratitude and gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who have always considered the poor and vulnerable people as their own hardships. She considered Samdech Techo's donation as a big help to alleviate the difficulties in raising these three twin babies to live and have a good future like other citizens in this prosperous society.
According to Mr. Seng Teang, from 1999 to the present, more than 23 years ago, 398 families gave birth to triplets or triplets and received generous donations from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit in supporting the hardships in daily life, especially raising three twin babies, are the grandchildren of both Samdech when they give birth.
