He said the most cultivated area for the main annual season is the Northeast, which relies on rainfall for cultivation.
Under normal circumstances, the annual main rice output is 24 million tons, of which 8 million tons are produced during the off-season. Chookiat added that off-season production should be good because there is enough water supply for irrigation during this time.
"Concerns about the drought have spread across Asia, affecting major rice producers and exporters such as Vietnam, India and China," he said. "Importing countries are increasing their rice purchases significantly due to this concern," he added. "The Philippines, Indonesia and China have placed large orders for rice, with the Philippines and China buying large quantities from Vietnam."
Vietnam's rice exports totaled 4 million tonnes in the first five months of this year, while Thailand exported 3.4 million tonnes during the same period.
