Many killed and injured in attacks on two police stations in central Vietnam
HANOI, June 11 (Xinhua) - Several people were killed and injured in a shooting at two police headquarters in the central highlands of Vietnam on Sunday (June 11), authorities said. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Sunday, June 11, 2023.
According to the Ministry of Public Security's website, six people have been arrested in connection with the shooting in Dak Lak province.
The Central Highlands, home to many ethnic minorities, is considered a sensitive area by the Vietnamese government and has long been a hotbed of discontent over issues including rights. Land and so on.
Gun violence is extremely rare in Vietnam, and the possession of firearms is illegal for Vietnamese citizens. The black market share for guns is also limited.
In January 2020, four people were shot dead in the illegal Duke betting ring on the outskirts of Ho Chi Minh City. In another rare shooting in 2016, two high-ranking officials in the northern province of Yen Bai were killed by colleagues in their office before the gunman shot himself.
