ARDB CEO encourages farmers to use credit to better manage cashew production chains
(Kratie): Mr. Kao Thach, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Rural Development Bank for Agriculture and Rural Development (ARDB), encouraged cashew farmers to consider borrowing from the Agricultural Bank to manage the cashew production chain. Its better.
He said this in a program to promote credit principles to support the cashew production chain project and connect the cashew market in Sangkat Or Russey, Kratie City, Kratie Province on June 11, 2023, with the participation of cashew farmers and Processed cashew nuts and packaging and more than 100 students of Kratie University.
The Director General informed the farmers that the Royal Government of Cambodia has a policy to support and want to turn Cambodia into an all-cashew emperor in the future. Therefore, in order for Cambodia to become a cashew emperor in the future, the various challenges raised by farmers need to be addressed.
He also suggested that farmers with a large area of cashew cultivation should be organized as a community or a group of producers by conspiring to prepare with a plan to grow and link to the market.
He encouraged farmers to apply for loans as investment capital for the construction of warehouses to prevent the price of cashews from falling on the market.
He said that in the case of community representatives or community members or farmers who want a loan to expand cultivation or expand the cashew production line, can apply for a loan from ARDB at a reasonable interest rate to buy fertilizers, pesticides, cashew nuts to build a warehouse. Lean Hal, etc., and this interest rate is a concession interest and is the consideration of the Royal Government for farmers in rural areas to expand the cultivation of cashews and other crops in agriculture.
Mr. Kao Thach encouraged farmers to consider applying for a loan from ARDB Bank by using dried cashew stock as collateral and the bank can provide credit up to 70% of the value of cashew nuts in the warehouse.
He also suggested that all farmers should study the techniques of cultivation, care to increase production and processing in accordance with the food standard to sell to the market when receiving a loan from the bank.
It should be noted that the area under cashew cultivation throughout Kratie province is more than 80,000 hectares.
