Understand the business: UAE will be a new market for Cambodia's rice sector to expand exports
(Phnom Penh): After the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates was signed on the afternoon of June 8, 2023, the Minister of Commerce of Cambodia and the President of the Cambodian Rice Federation are optimistic that the United Arab Emirates will become Major markets for Cambodia Expand rice exports and connect to other countries.
Oknha Chan Sokheang, President of the Cambodian Rice Federation, told Fresh News that the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates has provided potential and a new location for the Cambodian rice sector to expand in the future. .
"Because the United Arab Emirates, as well as the United Arab Emirates, has a history of doing business for thousands of years. "The Arabs continue to do this more broadly."
Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, said that the United Arab Emirates is an important country for the export of agricultural products due to the country's need for food security. In the future, he expects the United Arab Emirates to become a major market for Cambodian rice exports.
Under the agreement between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates, Cambodia will receive about 97.8% of the total tariff line, or 7,678 tariff lines. The main commodities that Cambodia gets in the market are almost all commodities, including agricultural products, including cashew rice, vegetables, fruits, bananas, mangoes, corn, pepper, durian, rice cakes, fruit desserts and so on.
"We are interested in exporting agricultural products and rice. In the past, some of our companies have participated in this work, and we can move forward to help the agricultural sector in Cambodia."
According to the Minister of Commerce, in addition to the United Arab Emirates market, Cambodia will also study the possibility of negotiating agreements with other countries such as Turkey, Switzerland, Pakistan, as Cambodia has potential in the agricultural sector to produce and process to both countries. That contributes to economic growth.
