(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, requested the Chinese Customs Administration to provide technical assistance in capacity building to further implement the strategy of reform and modernization of the Cambodian Customs Administration.
The meeting was held to strengthen and expand customs cooperation in accordance with the Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) on Cooperation and Mutual Assistance in Customs, signed on April 28, 2019. In Beijing, China.
In response to the request of the Cambodian Customs, the Deputy Minister of the Chinese Customs Administration expressed support for the proposal and requested that the Cambodian Customs raise specific requirements through the International Customs Cooperation Department of the two Customs administrations.
During the meeting, Minister Kun Nhim extended a warm welcome to the Chinese customs delegation and mentioned the special relations between the two countries in all fields.
Regarding the economic and trade sectors, the Minister emphasized that China is an important trade and investment partner of Cambodia, and accordingly, the two countries' customs administrations must cooperate actively, especially in smooth and efficient implementation. Of the Cambodia-China Bilateral Free Trade Agreement and the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP).
The Minister also briefed the Chinese customs delegation on the reform and modernization of the Cambodian Customs Administration. In this meeting, the leaders of the two customs administrations discussed, exchanged views and agreed on the following important agendas:
* Cooperate to prevent and crack down on tax evasion and transnational crimes such as drug smuggling, prohibited goods and endangered wildlife trade (CITES) by establishing contact points to exchange information in a timely manner.
* Discuss the joint implementation of the Authorized Economic Operators (AEO) program to increase trade facilitation
* Collaborate to exchange experiences on implementing risk management system
* Support each other in cooperating on customs operations at the regional and global levels.
To monitor the implementation of the spirit of this meeting and further strengthen the cooperation between the two customs administrations, the Deputy Minister invited Minister Kun Nhim and his colleagues to pay a working visit to the Chinese Customs Administration at an appropriate time in the future.
Overall, the two countries' customs administrations praised the results of the current bilateral meeting, which was held in a friendly and fruitful atmosphere. Interior Ministry Spokesman: 49 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on June 10
