(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government, has issued a decision to establish an inter-ministerial commission to implement the "Fun Chik Funan Techo" navigation.
The Inter-Ministerial Commission is chaired by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, with a total of 35 members.
The Inter-Ministerial Commission has the following roles and responsibilities:
• Review and advise on legal framework procedures and evaluate economic efficiency and propose investment forms for the Funan Techo canal project, which connects the Takeo canal of the Mekong Delta to the sea in Kep province.
Promote the preparation of this investment project clearly and in depth in all aspects and find investment partners to implement the project "Prek Chik Funan Techo" to be quality and effective, as well as review and negotiate investment agreements on this project.
• Accelerate the implementation of the "Prek Chik Funan Techo" navigation project to contribute to accelerating the development of Cambodia's inland waterway and sea transport sector to be more efficient, lower transportation costs and ensure sustainable growth. National Economy • Report on the results of work to the head of the Royal Government.
