This evening, Samdech Techo Hun Sen officially announced the "Cambodian Duke Association" and ate a solidarity meal
The Cambodian Duke Association represents the common voice, common philanthropic activities and the noble values of all the members of the Duke. The Cambodian Duke Association is registered as a legal association and officially recognized by the Ministry of Interior of the Kingdom of Cambodia by letter No. 5759 PRK. Dated this 25th day of October, 2022.
The Cambodian Duke Association was placed under the technical governance of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, as the Honorary President, through a letter from the Office of the Council of Ministers No. 350 and the NCC dated March 28. 2023.
The Cambodian Duke Association is officially recognized by the Royal Government, focusing on the Royal Government's partnership in promoting trade and investment in Cambodia.
The Cambodian Duke Association has a vision to maintain and promote the noble excellence of the Duke by participating in the sustainable social and economic development of Cambodia and the environment to create peace, harmony and improvement in the living standards of the people as well. Developed countries.
According to Trung Nga's 1973 Book of Khmer History, Part 1 and Part 2, the title "Duke" was used during the French colonial period, and this title refers to a senior official of the Central Administration, popularly known as the "Square". "
According to the Khmer dictionary, Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Chuon Nath revealed that "Oknha" is a word used by the ranks of high-ranking officials, such as high and low, such as tycoon, tycoon and tycoon. Currently, the Kingdom of Cambodia does not yet have a legal document for the management of the duke, the giving of the duke and the revocation of the duke.
In the past, the conferment of the title of tycoon was carried out in accordance with Sub-Decree No. 15 of the Office of the Council of Ministers dated April 5, 1994, in which the first point, Article 2, states: Ten thousand US dollars or more was awarded the first national construction medal and the Royal Government requested the high opinion of His Majesty the King of Life to place on the stone for His Majesty the King to confer the title of "Duke".
