(Kampong Thom): Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, on June 9, 2023, led a professional officer to inspect the condition of a road in Stung Sen City, which is planned to be built as a concrete road soon.
The provincial governor expressed his happiness and congratulations to the local authorities and the people for receiving the concrete road in the near future. This concrete road is 1,645 meters long, 6 meters wide and 1.5 meters thick from Slaket village, Prey Tahou commune and Achar Lak village, Achar Lak commune, Stung Sen city.
Cambodian Human Rights Committee Holds Second Consultation with Civil Society on UN Human Rights Committee Conclusions on Third Periodic Report
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Keo Remy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, on June 9, 2023, opened the second consultation with civil society on the follow-up to the Human Rights Committee on the Third Periodic Report - Gender on the Implementation of the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights.
The meeting was co-organized by the Cambodian Human Rights Committee and the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia at the Sun & Moon Riverside Hotel in Phnom Penh.
Mr. Ker Remy said that gender equality in Cambodia has improved significantly, especially the increase in the number of female students who have graduated from higher education.
He also stressed that education is a key factor in ensuring gender equality and combating gender-based violence that can make everyone aware of the value of women, who play an important role in promoting them. Gender equality through changing negative attitudes towards women.
Ms. Bun Chhit Veasna, Secretary General of the Cambodian National Council for Women, a representative of Dr. Ing Kantha Phavi, stated that the Ministry of Women's Affairs has done much to work on gender mainstreaming, eliminating domestic violence, combating trafficking in women and promoting women. Women's rights.
Ms. Roeida El Hage, Country Representative of the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia, also said that consultations with civil society and government agencies were a good example of encouragement and importance. Together promote and protect human rights.
She also took the opportunity to celebrate the 75th anniversary of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights, in which all UN member states are committed to the promotion and protection of human rights.
She said the OHCHR will be ready to host a high-level event on December 11-12, 2023, in relation to the Universal Declaration of Human Rights.
In this workshop, Ms. Camilla W. Ottsson, Director of the Swedish Office for Development Cooperation in Phnom Penh, also said that gender issues still exist in any country in the world. Therefore, we must all work together to eliminate all forms of gender discrimination and promote gender equality, as well as try to avoid violence against women.
