Disability Fund Donates to 50 Poor Families from 2 Districts in Kampot Province
(Kampot): Mr. Sim Sothoun, Secretary of State and Delegate of the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of the Disability Fund on June 9, 2023, attended the fundraising ceremony of the Disability Fund to 50 poor families from 2 District of Kampot Province.
Mr. Roeun Rithiroth said that on behalf of Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, he was very happy to meet the disabled people who came today.
He said that the package you received was the budget of the Royal Government of Cambodia led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, along with the budget of people across the country who donated money to the fund for the disabled. The fund for the disabled has been placed all over the country, such as public places, hotels, guesthouses, factories, enterprises, markets, pagodas, and resorts.
He added that the Disability Fund provides free rehabilitation services to people with disabilities throughout the country, in addition, people with disabilities also receive 3,000 riels per day and 10,000 riels for travel. Services at those rehabilitation centers for the poor with a disability equity fund The Disability Fund also provides 30,000 Riel per year for health screening and health care policies.
He added that not only people with disabilities in Kampot province have received gift packages, the Disability Fund has distributed a total of 650 gift packages to poor people across the province in 2022 and in 2023 will continue to provide gift packages. To 700 people with disabilities across the country. At the same time, the Disability Foundation has already built 38 houses for the poor.
He said that the above-mentioned is really confirming that the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, with the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation led by Minister Vong Soth as the staff and the Disability Fund. As an executive unit and does not leave people with disabilities.
