The Asian Vision Institute claims that the Facebook page of "ChhamChhany Chham Chany" recently used a video of Dr. Sok Siphana in the Higher Education Dialogue Forum without permission from the original owner. The video was produced with the addition of images, detracting from the original meaning of the dialogue with the intention of inciting distortion of facts to cause social unrest and instability.
1: The visit of the Cambodian delegation led by Dr. Sok Siphana is mandatory within the framework of strengthening the consultations of the European Commission, which began in March 2017.
2. The visit was made by both parties, namely the visit of the European Commission delegation to Cambodia and the Cambodian delegation to Brussels. Information on the consultation was made public on Cambodian media, and the European Commission also posted on social media about the Cambodian side's visit.
3. The purpose of the consultation is to address the concerns and misconceptions of the European Commission on the state of democracy and the human rights situation in Cambodia. This mission is a necessary work to be done to provide justice to the Royal Government of Cambodia on what Cambodia sees as a campaign to distort the facts related to Cambodia's development.
In light of the above, the Asian Vision Institute, an institution that promotes research and policy dialogue for the cause of peace, harmonization and sustainable social development and environment, condemns the individual "ChhamChhany Chham Chany".
The Asian Vision Institute also seeks the understanding and contribution of the public from all walks of life in preventing the sharing of false information by these individuals. Palestinian leader Mahmud Abbas to visit China next week
