Heavy rains hit southwest China, flooding several cities
BEIJING (Reuters) - Heavy rains in parts of southwest China on Friday caused flash floods in several cities, with roads and buildings flooded. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Friday, June 9, 2023.
Flood-prone China is warning of more extreme weather disasters due to climate change. In May, Guangxi experienced a rare drought, with rainfall falling to its lowest level in 60 years. Meanwhile, central China's Henan Province was recently hit by heavy rains, causing crops to be attacked, raising concerns about food security.
