(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hong So Hour, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, suggested that Cambodian investors who want to invest in the stock market should learn to look primarily at the companies they want to buy shares in, rather than just looking at them. Single stock price.
Mr. Hong Sohour's remarks were made at a forum of listed companies held at the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port.
Mr. Hong Sohour said, "I always encourage investors to check that if the price of the shares they buy does not increase, take another look at whether the company's business changes or increases. No? "Sometimes the share price goes down or stays the same, but if a company's annual business grows well, with a profit of 10 or 15 percent per year, that means the company is still doing well."
Mr. Hong Sohour said that the stock market really contributes a lot to support the Cambodian economy because we can not grow as much as possible if the stock market does not grow much, so investing in the stock market is a contribution to the economy. Cambodia to grow. Apsara Authority and New Zealand sign a memorandum of understanding on water management project in Angkor
