(Rattanakiri): The groundbreaking ceremony for the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship Building of the 2nd Border Guard Battalion, Ratanakkiri Military Operations Area of the 1st Military Zone was held on the morning of June 9, 2023 at
2nd Border Guard Battalion in Pak Thom Village, Pak Nhay Commune, O'Yadao District, Ratanakkiri Province, under the chairmanship of Lt. Gen. Khieu San, Deputy Secretary General of the Ministry of National Defense and Deputy Chairman of the Working Group for Organizing the 1st Ministerial Defense Friendship Meeting in Cambodia - Laos-Vietnam Representative General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief, Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chairman of the Working Group.
Speaking on this occasion, Lt. Gen. Khieu San said that the building is one floor high, measuring 48 meters x 14 meters, starting from today and will be completed in early November 2023 to put Inauguration before the celebration of the first Ministerial Defense Friendship Exchange Meeting of 3 countries, Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam, which will take place at the end of November 2023.
He added that this is a result of the cooperation between the two countries in the field of defense of Cambodia and Vietnam, which has made great efforts to support each other to strengthen and expand friendship, solidarity and neighborliness. It is good to perform security duties for the people of the two countries, especially to build infrastructure and develop human resources in the field of national defense.
In fact, the construction of this building will further contribute to the building of national defense capacity, security and order for Cambodia and for border security of the two countries.
