International community joins Canada in fighting wildfires
(Ottawa): Allies around the world have pledged to increase their aid to Canada in the fight against wildfires that have spread across the country during the worst wildfires ever. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Friday, June 9, 2023.
Wildfires that have raged since last month have forced tens of thousands of people to flee their homes and sent plumes of smog into much of the United States. About 4.3 million hectares have already been burned, about 15 times the annual average over the past decade. Meanwhile, hot and dry weather is expected to continue for the next few months.
Wildfires have affected mining operations in Canada and disrupted flights in the United States. Although wildfires are common in Nada, the simultaneous blaze in the east and west has forced the government to send troops to rescue as well as raise concerns about the consequences. Worse of climate change.
