(Siem Reap): General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, this morning, June 9, 2023, paid a courtesy call and presented national defense medals to veterans in Siem Reap province. 200 people.
On that occasion, General Ith Sarath brought a message of deep respect and affection from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Veterans Association and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen. All the veterans and their families living in Siem Reap city and province, even though they did not come down in person.
General Ith Sarath confirmed that all Cambodian veterans were the ones who made great sacrifices for the motherland of Cambodia in overthrowing the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, especially to prevent the regime from returning to cover the motherland of Cambodia again. During the period from 1979 to 1998.
General Ith Sarath reminded that for the cause of national defense, to protect the life and livelihood of the Cambodian people, the veterans have sacrificed and made all kinds of sacrifices, sacrificing fresh flesh and blood, crawling on the battlefield day and night in the rain and thunder. Hot, cold, sacrifice life without hesitation. In particular, some died, others survived, but are still paralyzed today.
General Ith Sarath emphasized that the unwavering dedication of our veterans is a great part of maintaining the light of Cambodia's peace and helping to push Cambodia to the stage of development in all areas as it is today.
Also among the 200 veterans were 55 disabled veterans, 136 retirees, six families of martyrs, two families of dead soldiers and one disabled soldier.
Please be informed that on that occasion, General Ith Sarath also donated his own money to 200 veterans, each of whom received 50,000 Riels.
