This morning, Provincial Road No. 312 in Prey Veng Province was opened for quality improvement and maintenance.
(Prey Veng): Provincial Road No. 312 in Prey Veng Province will be inaugurated this morning, June 9, 2023, under the presidency of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior, High Representative Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, Provincial Road No. 312 is 28,372 km long, starting from Samrong village, Lvea commune (at the intersection of National Road No. 1, km 77 + 08). 2) Up to Ko village, Banteay Chakrei commune (Cambodia-Vietnam border) of Preah Sdach district, Prey Veng province.
The project will rehabilitate and widen the road width, which is currently about 4 to 5 meters to a width of 12 meters, and upgrade the quality from a two-layer pavement (DBST) to a six-ply AC pavement. Cm and 8 cm and 25 cm thick reinforced concrete pavement with a total width of 11 m and lanes for cars and lanes for bicycles (2 lanes to and fro).
The project will also include the installation of all types of sewers along the road, as well as the installation of road markings, kilometer markers and safety posts in accordance with road technical standards.
(Phnom Penh): On Friday, June 9, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued to hold talks with nearly 20,000 workers. From 11 factories operating in Kampong Tralach and Samaki Meanchey districts, Kampong Chhnang province. The meeting will be held in Chamkar Svay village, Sethy commune, Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that today's meeting was attended by a total of 18,057 workers from 11 factories operating in Kampong Tralach and Samaki Meanchey districts of Kampong Chhnang province.
According to the Minister, the 11 factories that allow workers to meet with Samdech Techo are 3 types of garment factories, 2 travel products and bags, 1 printing on sports shoes, 1 and produce 1 resin and plastic. The products of these factories are exported to international markets, especially the European Union, the United States, Canada, Japan, etc.
Kampong Chhnang is a province that is benefiting from the policy of deploying factories and enterprises in the provinces from the Royal Government. In 2023, Kampong Chhnang has 173 factories with more than 50,000 workers. There are 20 garment factories with a total of more than 50,629 workers. There are 20 garment factories with a total of 47,585 workers.
Today's meeting is the seventh meeting for the second round. The seven meetings were attended by a total of 131,000 workers. Samdech Techo plans to meet 12 more times, which will meet a total of about 240,000 workers.
