NEC Introduces Posting of List of Political Parties and List of Candidates in 25 Capital and Provincial Polling Stations
(Phnom Penh): In accordance with the Law on the Election of the National Assembly and the Law on the Amendment of this Law and the Regulations and Procedures for the 7th National Assembly Election, the National Election Committee (NEC) Instruct the NEC, the CPP, and the political parties that have registered the political parties to stand for the official election on some of the work to be performed as follows:
First, the posting of the list of political parties and the list of candidates in the capital and provincial polling stations
All CECs must arrange for the public posting of the list of political parties and the list of all official candidates who have registered their political parties in their constituencies. The BCTC shall arrange for additional copies of these lists to be posted for the following purposes:
* 1 copy of the Secretariat of the National Election Commission * in some major cities. All CECs must inform all CECs of the deadline for applications for registration of political party agents as set out in point 2 below.
Second: Submitting and receiving applications for registration of political party agents, observers at polling stations and polling stations
* A political party that has registered a political party to stand for election in the Capital or Province constituency has the right to appoint one (one) full agent and one (one) reserve agent to observe the election and Count the ballots at each polling station and each counting station in the commune.
* The deadline for submitting and receiving applications for registration of political party agents is 7 (7) days after the date of posting the official list of political parties and the list of candidates is starting on the 14th. June 2023 ends on June 20, 2023.
All CECs must request cooperation and coordination with local authorities, especially commune authorities, in order to facilitate political parties to stand for election in connection with the request for the issuance of a certificate of registration in the commune / sangkat voter list for Complete the application form for registration as a political party agent in the CPP.
All CECs must disseminate this instruction to the competent authorities of registered political parties and the official list of candidates, associations and non-governmental organizations and other relevant parties within the framework of the Capital and Province. To be ready to cooperate and participate in the implementation of their respective duties in accordance with the laws, regulations and procedures of the election.
The NEC hopes that political parties, associations, national and international NGOs and election commissions at all levels will work together to promote the 7th National Assembly election. 2023 is a success.
