General knowledge: General Sun Ou and War Art Books
During his retirement from war and civil service, Sun Wu wrote a book on martial arts, known as the world's first military book, and served as the foundation of Chinese military science.
Sun Tzu's book Art of War has 13 chapters and 5,000 words. Each chapter has a different but related theme.
The chapter "Planning" refers to the possibility of war. Sun Jie said that war is a matter of death and life of a country. Moral laws, paradise, land, commanders, methods and discipline are the main deciding factors in the fight.
The "War" chapter emphasizes rapid victory. He claims that capturing prisoners of war is a way to beat opponents faster.
The "Tricks of Fighting" chapter emphasizes the plan of attack to win the battle, saying that "knowing the enemy and knowing yourself makes you win every battle."
The "Strategic Planning" chapter deals with the complete victory by taking advantage of material conditions. He argued that the benefits of material terms were based on military spending, the amount of supplies, the number of troops and the balance of power.
The "Power Consumption" chapter emphasizes the defeat of the enemy by joint efforts. Sun Jie advocated the use of favorable conditions to defeat enemies, such as unpredictable attacks or raids.
The "Army Mobility" chapter deals with the importance of taking advantage of specific situations to achieve a favorable position. Sun Jie said one should refrain from making hasty decisions about commanding troops and should understand the country's tendencies, be aware of road conditions and topography, and use intelligent guides who can deceive the enemy. Likewise, the consolidation and division of the army in different conditions and positions, the spirit and the military force of the enemy.
The "Strategic Variation" chapter is the basis for defining the pros and cons of troop mobility. This method has the ability to threaten, suppress and make enemies difficult to understand to tempt them.
The chapter "Military marches" deals with the importance of organizing and deploying troops, observing and gathering information from the enemy, as well as gathering officers and soldiers.
The "Topographic Classification" chapter emphasizes the relationship between different types of topography and military action.
The "Nine Situations" chapter deals with the nine different battles and the response to the situation.
This chapter, "Fire Attack," deals with the targets, types, materials, logistics, and environment necessary to carry out an attack. "The use of espionage" is a chapter that highlights the importance of espionage principles.
Today in Vietnam, Korea, Japan, Israel, Britain, Germany and Russia, all military experts welcome this book. In the preface to the book in English, the famous British strategist Liddell Hart says that the ancient Chinese military strategy, more than 2,500 years old, was very useful in modern warfare.
In addition, American economists point out that "many of the principles and theories found in the art of war remain indisputable to this day." Always respect the right of way, obey traffic signs and be right! Two killed, five injured in road accidents nationwide on June 8
