The West has repeatedly imposed sanctions on Moscow and its western neighbor Minsk after Russia launched a war in Ukraine in February last year.
The UK currently bans the import of gold, cement, wood and rubber from Belarus and bans the export of banknotes and machinery, as well as goods, technology and materials that can be used to make chemical and biological weapons.
The new measures will give Britain a reason to prevent the Belarusian media from spreading false information in the UK, including online.
Social media companies and Internet service providers will be required to restrict access to the websites of Belarusian media organizations, which are subject to the same sanctions as Russian shops.
The new measure also expands the sanctions criteria, giving the British government a basis to target a wider Belarusian population, such as Lukashenko's aides, advisers and ministers.
US suspends food aid to Ethiopia, saying its donations did not reach those in real need
The United States Agency for International Development (USAID) said on Thursday it would suspend food aid to Ethiopia because its donations were diverted from those in need. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Thursday, June 08, 2023.
A spokesman for the agency said in a statement that USAID, with the coordination of the Ethiopian government, had identified "a large-scale campaign diverting food aid from the Ethiopian people."
The statement did not specify who was behind the campaign.
The United States is by far the largest humanitarian donor to Ethiopia, with more than 20 million people in need of food aid, mostly due to the recent drought and war in the north. Tigray.
Based on internal reports from foreign donors donating to Ethiopia, USAID believes the food aid was diverted to the Ethiopian military.
However, a spokesman for the Ethiopian government and military did not immediately respond to a request for comment, while USAID declined to comment on the report.
Senior Officials of the Ministry of Rural Development Inaugurate Water Supply and Sanitation Projects in Ratanakkiri and Stung Treng Provinces
(Stung Treng): Mr. Thong Poch, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development, on June 8, 2023, inaugurated the water supply and sanitation projects in Ratanakkiri and Stung Treng provinces.
On that occasion, Mr. Yi Kimthan, Deputy Director of Plan International Cambodia, said that the water supply and sanitation project in Ratanakkiri and Stung Treng provinces received funding from the Korea Cooperation Agency (KOICA) and Plan International. Korea.
He said the launch of the project to achieve clean water supply and sanitation aims to improve the health and living environment of poor girls and their parents by increasing access to clean water and improving sanitation. Equality in Stung Treng and Ratanakkiri provinces through access to safe drinking water, improving village infrastructure, clean water communes and community-led sanitation.
(Battambang): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Province, on the afternoon of June 8, 2023, chaired a meeting between the Battambang Provincial Administration and the International Association of French Mayors (AIMF) via Zoom video and audio transmission system. To strengthen communication and discuss work for the implementation of various projects in Battambang province.
After listening to and watching the presentation of the International Association of French Mayors (AIMF), Mr. Sok Lou expressed his interest in the project to build a toilet mud treatment plant, a project that has been built in Phnom Penh and Siem Reap. Come on, because this toilet mud control station can also provide many benefits to Battambang province.
In addition, Loam also expressed interest in other projects related to the development of Battambang as a Smart City and the organization of Battambang with good governance and sustainability.
Mr. Sok Loo also said that the management of toilet mud is new to the Battambang Provincial Administration, need experts in this area, so the provincial administration will appoint experts to communicate and work with the AIMF to continue. Sustainability together and to conduct in-depth studies related to this and other areas.
He also added that the Battambang Provincial Administration is also trying to develop Battambang into a Smart City to make Battambang more attractive to national and international tourists and investors. .
Banteay Meanchey Provincial Armed Forces Send 4 Adolescents to Provincial Court Involved in Illegal Drug Use
(Banteay Meanchey): The Anti-Drug Office of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie on June 08, 2023, sent a group of four children with exhibits to the Provincial Court for legal proceedings related to the use of drugs. Illegal possession of illegal drugs.
According to Brigadier General Yan Sovann, Commander of the Serei Sophorn Municipal Gendarmerie, a group of four freelancers, along with some exhibits, were arrested at 11:40 pm on June 5, 2023 at In front of Sre Mam Guesthouse is located in Kbal Spean Village, Sangkat Preah Ponlea, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
After being arrested and interrogated, the four teenagers confessed that they had actually used illegal drugs. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the Municipal Gendarmerie sent the four children to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
