Interior Ministry Spokesman: 80 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on June 7
(Phnom Penh): At least 80 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on June 7, 2023 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on June 8, 2023.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 80 suspects, 17 were arrested in 13 criminal cases and 63 were arrested in 14 drug cases.
More than one million Rohingya refugees have been gathered in refugee camps in southeastern Bangladesh, becoming the largest refugee camp in the world.
During Thursday's demonstrations across the camp, young and old waved banners and chanted slogans, "No more refugees." "No verification, no security, no interview ... we want to go back to our homeland."
"We are Myanmar citizens by birth," he said. "We want to return home with all our rights, including nationality, freedom of movement, safe living and security."
"We want the United Nations to help us return to our homeland," he said. "We want the world community to help us maintain our rights in Myanmar."
