Senior Minister Osman Hassan Meets 86 Muslims to Hajj in Saudi Arabia
On that occasion, Dr. Osman Hassan said that the number of Muslims traveling to Hajj in Cambodia has increased to more than 1,100, with each person spending about $ 7,500, a total budget of about 8 Million dollars, while last year there were just over 500.
He said the increase was more than half due to the fact that by 2023, 19 cases of Kovid had been alleviated, there was no restriction on the age of Hajj participants, and Saudi Arabia had increased the number of quota participants worldwide. There is also Cambodia.
In particular, he highlighted that this is a sign that today, Muslims in Cambodia, as well as people across the country to enjoy a prosperous life and improve their living conditions forward as part. Of national economic growth under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, which has made the country peaceful and developed in all fields.
The private company that conducts the Hajj usually chooses a long period of 40 days or more. Especially because this year you have to return to fulfill the obligation to vote for the National Assembly, which will take place on July 23, 2023 in the near future.
Finally, he instructed and wished all those who came to perform Hajj today, as well as those who travel in the future, be safe and fulfill their duties in accordance with the rules of Islam.
The 86 Muslims who left this morning were led by the Jia Group, 56 of whom went private and were sponsored by 30 associations.
It is worth noting that attending the Hajj is the fifth of the five obligations of Islam, which every year Muslims from all over the world from all over the world come to celebrate this festival in Makkah, Saudi Arabia.
