It should be noted that Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates have officially announced the opening of negotiations on the Cambodia-UAE Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement on October 24, 2022. Prior to today's signing, the two countries' working groups held three high-level talks.
Through this agreement, Cambodia is expected to reap maximum benefits. Cambodia will be able to diversify its export markets to the United Arab Emirates and seize other Arab markets in the Middle East and North Africa. Some important Cambodian goods, especially clothing and footwear, will be tax deductible or exempt.
At the same time, Cambodia will consider importing high-quality and competitively priced priority goods to meet domestic demand, such as lubricants, rubber, pavements and animal feed.
Through this agreement, trade between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates will be more lively and the country's markets will be wider.
