Minister Thong Khon Presents Investment Opportunity in Tourism to Cambodia to UAE Minister of International Trade
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, informed about the potential of tourism in Cambodia and presented the investment opportunities in the tourism sector to the Minister of International Trade of the United Arab Emirates, Mr. Thany Bin Ahmed Al Jude, at a working meeting on June 8. 2023 at the Ministry of Tourism.
On that occasion, the Minister of International Trade of the United Arab Emirates expressed his interest in the development of Cambodia and wanted to explore tourism in Cambodia.
Minister Thong Khon informed the Minister of International Trade of the United Arab Emirates that Cambodia has many investment opportunities, especially in the tourism sector, which is in need of development to create new tourism products to contribute to the policy of attracting more international tourists, especially the Royal Government of Cambodia. High to every investor.
Minister Thong Khon said that the United Arab Emirates can contact the Cambodian Ministry of Tourism in Dubai for more information on Cambodia, government leadership, economic / social development, investment and tourism potential.
Mr. Thong Khon continued that in Cambodia, there is development in all areas, peace, stability, development of urban infrastructure, highways, which allows investors to see the potential of investment in Cambodia.
Minister Thong Khon also requested the Minister of International Trade of the United Arab Emirates to help promote the resumption of Fly Emirates direct flights from Dubai to Cambodia in order to increase the number of tourists from the United Arab Emirates to Cambodia and to cooperate. Promote the re-signing of the Memorandum of Understanding on Tourism Cooperation, which was signed in 2012 and has now expired.
It should be noted that in the past, between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates, there was a connection between Dubai-Yangon-Phnom Penh, which is a means for tourists to travel to both countries and attract tourists from third countries.
Pursat Provincial Administration Decides to Establish Provincial Committees and 9 Sub-Committees to Prevent and Suppress Crimes in Challenging Areas
The meeting was held at the first floor of the provincial hall under the chairmanship of Mr. Khoy Rida, Pursat Provincial Governor, Chairman of the Provincial Unity Command and Chairman of the Provincial Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes.
After the meeting to discuss and accept the common opinion, Pursat Provincial Administration decided to establish a working group of 9 provincial joint committees and sub-committees led by 9 deputy governors to conduct direct operations to prevent and suppress logging crimes. Invading forest land in Veal Veng and Phnom Kravanh districts, which are the most challenging target districts.
Each sub-committee will be implemented from June 12, 2023 until the end of the mission, and all expenditures, including budget, materials and means, will be borne by the provincial administration, which has a responsible financial office.
