The first batch of Cambodian agricultural products will be shipped from Koh Kong International Port to Liaoning Port, China by the end of June.
This statement was made by the President of Henan Chamber of Commerce at the inauguration ceremony of Koh Kong International Port Customer Service Center and a press conference on the date of the first trip was held in Phnom Penh on June 6, 2023. . Senior officials from the Ministry of Transport, General Department of Customs and Excise, General Department of Immigration and other relevant departments, private companies and media representatives attended.
Kor Raing said that on June 16, 2023, some agricultural crops in northern China will also be shipped to the Koh Kong International Port.
He said that the transport of Chinese agricultural products to Cambodia so that people know the taste of crops in northern China, while now he sees how much these fruits are sold in the Cambodian market. In particular, for the crops of Cambodian agricultural products that are sold on the market in the northern part of China, where the cold zone is also expensive. Therefore, the transportation of agricultural products of the two countries will reduce the price.
He claimed that arranging for the direct transportation of agricultural products between the two countries was his long-standing desire.
On June 5, the Governor of Koh Kong Province, Ms. Mithona, sent a letter to the Port of Inle in China, inviting the leaders of the Port of Inland to visit Cambodia to promote the development of the two ports. Signing of the Memorandum of Understanding on Friendship Port Cooperation and Establishment of Friendship Port.
On May 9, 2023, the port passed the official inspection and recognition of the relevant government departments and has the capacity to receive navigation for ships of 10,000 tons.
Please be informed that so far, Cambodia's agricultural products that can be exported to China include: rice, cassava, cashew nuts, bananas, mangoes, corn, lentils, Pailin (Ta Nen), fish, pepper, as well as 11 more natural fishery products. .
