Cambodia, UAE ready to sign formal Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement tomorrow
(Phnom Penh): The Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates has reached its official signing ceremony, which will be held under the highest presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on June 08. 2023 at the Peace Palace.
As the agreement is ready to be signed tomorrow, the Minister of Commerce of Cambodia, Mr. Pan Sosak, and Mr. Thani bin Ahmed Al Zeyoudi, Minister of International Trade of the United Arab Emirates, will meet on the afternoon of June 7, 2023. Courtesy and discussion to examine the possibility of further strengthening and expanding cooperation in all fields, especially trade and investment.
The talks were also attended by senior officials, businessmen and investors of both countries.
Cambodian Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak emphasized the benefits of the agreement, saying that Cambodia would be able to diversify its export markets to the United Arab Emirates and seize other Arab markets in the Middle East and Africa. North, which is a nearby area. Some important Cambodian goods, especially clothing and footwear, will be tax deductible or exempt.
At the same time, he said, Cambodia could consider importing high-quality, competitively priced priority goods to meet domestic demand, such as lubricants, rubber, paving and animal feed.
In addition, Cambodia can also attract investment companies from the United Arab Emirates and seize the growing number of tourists from this country.
The two sides agreed to push for the ratification of the agreement so that investors, businessmen, producers, traders and consumers of both sides can seize the economic benefits and business and investment opportunities that the agreement will provide in the future.
