Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to visit nearly 20,000 workers in Kampong Chhnang province
(Phnom Penh): On Thursday, June 8, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will continue to hold talks with nearly 20,000 workers. People from 5 factories operating in Kampong Tralach district, Kampong Chhnang province. The meeting will be held in Chamkar Svay village, Sethy commune, Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that Samdech Techo had already met with workers in Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province twice in 2018.
For tomorrow's meeting, this is the third meeting. Tomorrow's meeting was attended by a total of 18,095 workers from 5 factories operating in Kampong Tralach district, Kampong Chhnang province.
According to the Minister, the five factories that allow workers to meet with Samdech Techo are three types of garment factories, one travel product and one bag, and one shoe sewing machine. The products of these factories are exported to international markets, especially the European Union, the United States, Canada, Japan, etc.
Kampong Chhnang is a province that is benefiting from the policy of deploying factories and enterprises in the provinces from the Royal Government. In 2023, Kampong Chhnang has 173 factories with more than 50,000 workers. There are 20 garment factories with a total of more than 47,000 workers and it is the eighth province with the most industrial enterprises.
Tomorrow's meeting is the sixth meeting for the second round. The six meetings had a total of 113,000 workers. Samdech Techo is scheduled to meet 13 more times, which will meet with a total of 222,000 workers.
