Dr. HUN Manet: The Party Youth Organization, as well as all party members, is a force involved in implementing the party's political program to achieve the plan.
(Kampot): Dr. Hun Manet, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Central Youth Party, on June 7, 2023, attended the ceremony to announce the composition and talk with the CPP Youth Working Group. Cambodia, Kampot province.
Dr. Hun Manet said that the Cambodian People's Party was born in 1951 and in the past there has been a series of policy changes and reforms, but no change in the cause, in all circumstances. Strived to better serve the interests of the nation and the people.
Dr. Hun Manet said that the Party Youth Organization, as well as all party members are a force to participate in the implementation of the party's political program to achieve the plan for the benefit of the nation and the people.
At the same time, Dr. said that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Cambodian People's Party is committed to safeguarding the current achievements and continue to strive for further development as planned in the transformation of Cambodia into a rich country. High revenue by 2050, taking peacekeeping as the basis to maintain development opportunities in all areas.
He added that in addition to demonstrating the promotion of democracy through the exercise of voting rights, the successful results of the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022 are a testament to the CPP's support. Cambodia and giving confidence to the Cambodian People's Party to continue to serve and solve problems for the people.
In addition, Dr. Hun Manet also told the current generation of young people have three important tasks to complete:
First, to maintain all the achievements that the older generation has built. Second, to strive to expand more positive achievements for the next generation, and third: to make sure that the current youth and generation. The latter can continue the spirit of heroism and mission of the previous generation of youth as members of the Cambodian People's Party forever.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, this morning, June 7, 2023, presided over the consultation on the roadmap for national planning for sustainable beekeeping and wild bee conservation in Phnom Penh. Cambodia.
