The number 18 is the global hong shui number in many religious systems, religions, traditions around the world.
In Buddhism, the number 18 is the power, energy, energy of the Buddha's spirit, which represents the arahants or apostles of the 18 Buddhas (Buddhism), the Buddha's enlightenment. Because the 18 Arahants are: The Dhamma, the Eightfold Path, and the Ten Noble Truths, 18 are the enlightenment of the Buddha.
In the cosmology of Brahmanism, the number 108 is the number of the emperor and was copied to build the capital of Yasodharapura, with Phnom Bakheng as its center. All the towers of Phnom Bakheng temple have a total of 108 dedicated to Shiva or Iso, because in Brahmanical rituals such as chanting Keatha, all 108 chanting must be completed to reach the top. Therefore, the numbers 18 and 108 are synonymous with sacred numbers.
In both Mahayana and Hindu Buddhism, the number 108 is the sacred number of the monk's prayer beads. In Hinayana Buddhism, the Buddha that we worship every day has 108 shields called the 108 Bliss.
The spiritual significance of the number 18 is 1 + 8 is 9, which is considered a powerful spiritual number. Represents spiritual enlightenment, inner wisdom, and the completion and rebirth of a cycle, symbolizing good fortune, blessings, and longevity.
In Western culture, the number 18 is associated with success.
In meditation, the 18 evils are the bright light in front of you. When you take a deep breath and relax into a state of calm, all the good things will come into your life.
In love, the number 18 is the spiritual number of the love life, symbolizing the arrival of age and the beginning of puberty, finding a mate, commitment and eternal love.
In conclusion, Mr. Rath Sandab stated that in relation to the belief system on this number, for the Cambodian People's Party, which captured the 18th election number, in the Khmer belief system and the various ethnic belief systems in the world, it is a sacred number. A symbol of strength, power and abundant growth everywhere.
