Ninth Committee of the Senate fully supports the draft law on the ratification of the ASEAN Trade in Services Agreement
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, on the afternoon of June 6, 2023, led a delegation to a meeting with the Ninth Committee of the Senate to discuss and defend the draft law on the approval of the agreement. ASEAN Trade in Services (ATISA), chaired by Kong Sarach, Chairman of the Ninth Committee and a member of the Standing Committee, as well as members of all specialized committees of the Senate.
Mr. Kong Sarach, Chairman of the Ninth Commission and a member of the Standing Committee, warmly welcomed Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, on behalf of the Royal Government and his colleagues to discuss and defend the draft law.
In addition, the President also made a detailed report on the text of the draft law on the approval of the ASEAN Trade in Services Agreement, stating that the draft law was properly prepared in accordance with the provisions of the Constitution, laws and relevant legal norms. .
The Minister clarified and informed the Meeting of the objectives, contents as well as the benefits that Cambodia will receive from the ASEAN Trade in Services Agreement when this Agreement enters into force. At the same time, the Minister also answered in detail the questions of the members of the Senate regarding the draft law.
In addition, the Minister reiterated to the Meeting that the ASEAN Trade in Services Agreement (ATISA) will contribute to the implementation of strategies to further strengthen economic connectivity and provide better opportunities for economic development in the community. The ASEAN economy will increase trade and investment in trade in services, creating a wider market and economy by easing restrictions on trade in services.
On that occasion, the Chairman of the Ninth Commission highly appreciated the efforts of the Minister as well as the leaders at all levels and civil servants of the Ministry of Commerce who actively carried out their professional duties in accordance with the policy and strategy of the Rectangle. The Royal Government has achieved proud results, especially the drafting of laws and regulations under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
As a result, the meeting expressed its full support for the form and content of this draft law and sent it to the Standing Committee for review and request to be included in the agenda of the upcoming plenary session of the Senate.
