(Phnom Penh): The peace that has been hard to find under the hands and wisdom of Samdech Techo Hun Sen for more than 20 years is bringing rapid growth for the Cambodian nation. Many transport infrastructure achievements have also emerged, serving as a noble benefit for the once miserable nation of Cambodia.
Another new historical achievement in Cambodia, the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway, will begin construction on Wednesday morning, June 7, 2023, tomorrow. . The Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway is the second expressway in Cambodia after the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, which was officially launched in 2022.
The groundbreaking ceremony for the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway will be presided over by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Wang Vinthean. In addition to the groundbreaking ceremony for the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway, it is also linked to the opening of a bridge across the Mekong River and a bridge junction.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, highlighted that the groundbreaking ceremony was a testament to Cambodia's progress in road infrastructure development and, in fact, the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway. This is Cambodia's second expressway after the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway was officially opened more than half a year ago.
The Minister, who is Samdech Techo's outstanding officer in the field of transportation, said that this expressway is another new achievement among many important national achievements across the country that came from the efforts of Cambodia's Outstanding Leader is Samdech Techo Prime Minister and the indispensable contribution of Cambodia's friendly countries and development partners.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that the project to build the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway has a total length of 135.10 km, starting from Thmor Kor commune, Lvea Em district, Kandal province to Chrakmtes commune, Bavet city, Svay Rieng province. This road has a 4.1 km long road passing through Kandal province, 70.9 km long Prey Veng province and 60.1 km long Svay Rieng province.
This project will implement the following construction technical work:
Regarding the construction cost project, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway is planned to spend a total investment of 1.35 billion US dollars under the construction-operation-transfer (BOT) investment period. 50 years of operation, of which 20% is invested by China Bridge and Road Corporation and 80% is company loan.
Separately, the bridge across the Mekong River is planned to spend a total of 232.58 million US dollars, which is the investment budget of the Royal Government, along with the contribution for the clearance of landmines, unexploded ordnance and other taxes. Both projects will be built by the China Bridge and Road Corporation (CRBC), with a construction period of 48 months and scheduled for completion in 2027.
