Comment: "Disconnection" with China will add to the burden on the world economy
BEIJING (Reuters) - Over the past few years, the United States has pursued a number of discriminatory industrial policies to protect its hegemony and self-interest, as well as to curb development. The United States has accelerated the severance of ties and chains with China in the fields of economy, trade and technology.
Although politicians in Washington have called for a severance of ties with China, over the past two years, China-US trade volume has hit record highs in 2021. Exceeded 750,000 million US dollars in 2022, reaching nearly 760 billion US dollars, a significant increase compared to 583.37 billion US dollars in 2017.
Over the years, China has adhered to the deepening of reform and continuous opening up in the global economy, China has continuously served as a "balance instrument" and "source of momentum". Global economic recovery must reduce risks and diversify, leaving China isolated is not only impossible but also dangerous.
