Economist: What factors help reduce poverty in Cambodia?
(Phnom Penh): If we look closely, the poverty rate in Cambodia seems to be under pressure from critics, but if we look at economic policy, the world praises Cambodia for its rapid development and the well-being of the Cambodian people. .
Today, millions of people have been lifted out of poverty through the political, economic and development goals that Cambodians need. In the last 10 years, an additional 2 million Cambodians have been lifted out of poverty. From poverty. Currently, the poverty rate nationwide is only 11% of the total Cambodian population.
With this figure, the world notes that trade and economic policies that support local development and generate income are truly effective, with the world considering Cambodia as a model of regional and global economic development.
From 1993 to 2023, Cambodia has achieved the fruits of the process of economic development in line with the world's aspirations. First, the rate of high regional and global economic growth, which reached 7% on average annually; second, the poverty rate fell from 47% to 11% at present; and third, the volume of trade between the two countries. Which achieved about 70% of the total economic size.
There are a total of 3.8 million private sector jobs in Cambodia, of which about 400,000 are government officials. The local private sector has created about 2.3 million jobs and the foreign private sector has about 1 million jobs.
These five factors have helped to improve people's lives, which has reduced the rate of poverty reduction by more than half, the current poverty rate of 11%. But the World Bank warns that rural people who are free from poverty could fall back into poverty if they lose about 1,200 riel a day, which could raise the poverty rate to 40. % Again.
According to World Bank figures, there are more than 3 million people across the poverty line across Cambodia. To address these issues and improve the livelihoods of rural people, it is likely to have a strong local development plan, especially to help the three main priorities: the continued development of rural infrastructure and agricultural diversification; Invest in human resources and third, the implementation of the social protection system.
According to World Bank figures, rural agriculture has helped reduce poverty and improve the lives of 60% of the population, compared to the current 4% in urban areas. Therefore, relying on agriculture alone will not be able to improve people's livelihoods in the long run. In the medium and long term, non-agricultural economic activity is one of the main ways to reduce poverty in a sustainable way in Cambodia.
By: An Sithav The Ministry of Labor calls on people to be very careful about all advertisements about the recruitment and sending of Cambodian workers to Australia
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on June 6, 2023 called on people to be very careful about all advertisements about the recruitment and sending of Cambodian workers to Australia.
The call came after the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training received information that some crooks were conducting outreach and fundraising activities to ensure that they could be sent to work in Australia.
The Ministry would like to confirm that so far the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Australia have not cooperated on sending Cambodian workers to work in Australia. The Ministry calls on the people to be very careful about all advertisements about the recruitment and sending of Cambodian workers to Australia.
Meanwhile, according to Sub-Decree No. 190 dated August 17, 2011 on the control of sending Cambodian workers to work abroad through private recruitment agencies, all sending workers to work abroad must have permission from the Ministry. Employment and vocational training.
In this sense, sending workers to countries that do not operate on sending workers to Cambodia and without the permission of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training is a fraudulent act and could be a crime of human trafficking. CSX chief says Phnom Penh port share price almost tripled but still cheap for investors
