This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen inaugurated the Royal Academy of Justice in Cambodia and awarded diplomas to judicial students.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, June 6, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen inaugurated the Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia and Present diplomas to students, judges, clerks, bailiffs, notaries.
The presence of Samdech Techo for both programs today is a demonstration of the Prime Minister's high attention on training and capacity building of human resources in the field of justice as part of the Royal Justice Reform. The government aims to improve the quality and efficiency of justice services to the people.
Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, said that before 2002, Cambodia did not have a judicial vocational training school. At that time, judges, prosecutors and clerks were selected from the surviving human resources of the Pol Pot genocidal regime and sent abroad for short-term training or skills training before being selected to work in Through the courts and the prosecutors accompanying the courts.
Mr. Keut Rith said that at present, the Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia is a public training institution under the management of the Ministry of Justice and chaired by a Board of Directors and has the following subordinate structures: Royal School of Judges and Prosecutors, Royal School The registrar, the Royal School of Bailiffs, the Royal School of Notaries, the School of Law and the General Secretariat, as well as a scientific and pedagogical council.
Separately, all professional students, including students, judges, clerks, bailiffs and notaries who are studying at the Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia, a total of 270 (87 females).
For the graduation ceremony to be held under the presidency of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, this is the second official graduation ceremony for all 1,835 vocational students (432 females) who have successfully graduated since 2008 to 2022.
Currently, all professional graduates, including students, judges, clerks, bailiffs and notaries, have been serving as judges, prosecutors, clerks and bailiffs in all courts and prosecutors. Class and notary public in various notary departments in the Kingdom of Cambodia, as well as some are working in public administration.
Regarding the office of the Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia, the Minister of Justice said that initially in 2002, the Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia had a small office space with only seven rooms and was part of the school building. Royal Administration for use in both administrative and training functions.
Until 2005, under a grant from Japan, the Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia received a new 4-storey building on the same location as the Royal School of Administration, with 20 offices, 5 classrooms, and a meeting hall. 1 and 1 co-educational hall.
With the help of the German Cooperation Organization, a dormitory building with 10 rooms for female judges from rural areas and a meeting room and a library were built.
Currently, the location of the Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia has been moved to a new location with two large buildings on an area of more than 2 hectares, which is officially inaugurated now.
The second building is 52m x 40m, has 3 floors and a total area of 5,716 square meters and is used as a training venue of the Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia and the Bar Association Professional Training Center. Lawyer of the Kingdom of Cambodia as well.
The construction of the two buildings took 1 year, 6 months and 27 days and cost a total of 4.91 million US dollars. These two huge new buildings are new achievements in the field of justice that appear under the shadow of peace and under the wise leadership and long-term vision of Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
