Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the inauguration of the Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia and the awarding of diplomas to judicial students
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, June 6, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen inaugurated the Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia. And award diplomas to students, judges, clerks, bailiffs, notaries.
The following are the key messages of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the inauguration of the Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia and the awarding of diplomas to judicial students:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen told the Japanese Ambassador that the location of the Royal Academy of Justice in Cambodia was a place where the Khmer Rouge had fought.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalls the reform of the judiciary in Cambodia by changing the decision to appoint the President of the Court and the Prosecutor from the Prime Minister to the State Council, with the Minister of Justice as the Chairman.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommends the construction of dormitories for residential students, both judicial and economic students.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that more efforts must be made to train human resources in the field of justice in order to strengthen the justice sector in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he was very happy to see the ministries pay attention to human resource training.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the moral tradition of Cambodia is to respect the elders. Therefore, each family must take care to strengthen the traditions and morals of their children.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that only his family could not settle and ran to the Prime Minister.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen encourages extrajudicial resolution of disputes. If you go to court, there are only winners and losers. You win that court is fair, you lose that court is unfair.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says lawyers are not happy when he encourages extra-judicial settlement.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the rich and the poor must have equal rights before the law. Do not say that the rich always win, the poor always lose, the rich are always right or the poor are always wrong.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that strict action must be taken against those who encroach on state land. Not to be excused under the pretext of affecting the election.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks civil society organizations not to protect criminals from encroaching on state land.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia's democratic process is progressing every day, Cambodia is a democracy of the rule of law. Democracy without the rule of law is anarchy.
