The release of rare wildlife in Angkor National Park is a collaboration between the APSARA Authority, the Forestry Administration and the Wildlife Alliance.
Speaking to reporters on the occasion of visiting a rare wildlife sanctuary in Angkor National Park, Mr. Nick Mark, Director of Wildlife Rescue and Conservation of the Wildlife Alliance, said, "Cambodia is almost extinct from wildlife traps. "The reason why the big tiger is present in Cambodia, now they arrest the mother, they have all the children."
"I ask everyone not to set traps in the forest and I ask the government to make stronger laws to protect wildlife from traps, because if we do not do all the animals," he said.
At the same time, Nick Mark said that in the Angkor National Park and in the forests protected by the Wildlife Alliance, there are patrols everywhere, but the trappers have a hidden method that is difficult to find, and the trap. In addition, the hunters do not put only one place, they put hundreds of places to catch wild animals.
Nick considers the Angkor forest to be a good place for wildlife to live because the Apsara Authority and park rangers are there to protect the wildlife. However, the wildlife that is no longer brought here is clearly defined as not being a dangerous animal for tourists who come to visit here as well.
According to Mr. Chouradina, Deputy Director of the Department of Water Management, Forestry and Infrastructure of the APSARA Authority, "As of now, there are more than 10 species of wild animals that we have released here, a total of about 40 calves. During the project, we plan to find other species to release here (Angkor National Park).
He said that because Angkor National Park is a tourist area, so for the selection of animals to be released, it is necessary to check carefully to make sure that the wildlife does not endanger the safety of tourists. For this project, deer will be released in the Angkor forest.
"By releasing the rare wildlife present in Angkor National Park, Angkor National Park is not only a historical site, but also a natural tourist destination," said Juradina. "Periods of visiting rare and endangered wildlife have been brought here."
Net Pheaktra, secretary of state and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, said the establishment of a wildlife presence in the Angkor National Park was part of an increase in Cambodia's wildlife distribution. For the increase in the number of wildlife in the Angkor National Park, because Cambodia is completely peaceful, which can provide opportunities for consideration of wildlife conservation and natural resources.
The introduction of Samdech Lor Horm Sar Kheng was made during the meeting with the leaders, delegates, coaches, athletes and equipments of the National Police officers who are the winners of the gold, silver and bronze medals from participating in the event. The 32nd SEA Games 2023 on the afternoon of June 4, 2023 at the meeting hall of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
On that occasion, Mr. Sor Sithy, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, assisted the General Secretariat of the Sports Council of the Ministry of Interior. High in a meaningful conversation on this occasion.
On that special occasion, the Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Interior expressed his deep gratitude and appreciation to Samdech Krala Hom, who always pays attention, encourages and supports all of us with materials and budget. All sports.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng expressed his pleasure to meet with the leaders, delegates, coaches, athletes of the General Secretariat of the Sports Council of the Ministry of Interior, who won gold, silver and bronze medals from participating in the SEA Games. This is the 32nd time in 2023.
Samdech Krala Hom considered that the result obtained now is a great pride, not only for the Ministry of Interior, but it is the honor of the whole society that the athletes of the Ministry of Interior participated in the competition and won medals. With an unprecedented record in history.
In addition, Samdech Krala Hom also expressed his sincere appreciation to the leaders, delegates, coaches and athletes who worked hard to win medals for the nation and wished all athletes good health. Continue to win medals to bring honor to the nation in the next competition event.
During the ceremony, Samdech also gave some recommendations to the General Secretariat of the Sports Council of the Ministry of Interior as follows:
1. For the 33rd SEA Games 2025 in the Kingdom of Thailand, the leaders as well as the delegates and coaches of the General Secretariat of the Sports Council of the Ministry of Interior must take care to prepare the existing sports and potential. We need to send athletes to participate in the competition, at the same time, we also need to pay attention to and strengthen the kind of sport that is necessary, and we still do not have the ability to be strong, we also need to work hard to strengthen.
3: For athletes who are equipped with the rank now must continue to work hard to train to strengthen their ability to further, especially to avoid committing any inappropriate acts and to avoid the use of equipment. Addicted.
4. The General Secretariat of the Sports Council of the Ministry of Interior shall prepare documents related to the SEA Games to be kept at the Ministry of Interior for the history and achievements of the National Police Force in participating in sports events.
5. The General Secretariat of the Sports Council of the Ministry of Interior shall cooperate with partner countries and the private sector to develop its sports base and techniques for progress and quality.
6. All General Departments, General Secretariats, Departments under the Ministry of Interior must continue to pay attention to, support and promote sports in the Ministry of Interior as much as possible.
Please be reminded that the 32nd SEA Games 2023, which Cambodia participated in this historic event, Cambodia won a total of 282 medals (81 gold, 74 silver and 127 bronze). Among them, athletes from the General Secretariat of the Sports Council of the Ministry of Interior contributed a total of 132 medals (35 gold, 34 silver and 63 bronze), equivalent to 46.80 percent of the total medals.
