Mr. Sok Sokan: The people of Kirivong district, Takeo province, are committed to continue to support the government in maintaining the hard-earned peace in the last 500 years of Cambodia's history
(Takeo): Mr. Sok Sokan, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Chairman of the Kirivong District Field Team, said that the people of Kirivong District, Takeo Province, are committed to continuing to support the Royal Government in maintaining peace, which is rarely found. In the last 500 years of Cambodia's history.
Mr. Sok Sokan made this statement on the morning of Sunday, June 4, 2023 at Wat Kiri Kongkear (called Wat Buor) in Buor village, Prey Romdeng commune, Kirivong district, Takeo province, during the groundbreaking ceremony and inauguration of the new temple. Cross-achievement.
On that occasion, Mr. Sok Sokan expressed his congratulations and happiness for the new achievements in the series of Wat Kiri Kongkear (called Wat Buor), which is about 246 years old.
He pointed out that the construction of a huge and brand new temple, as well as other achievements at Wat Kiri Kongkea (called Wat Buor), is a symbol of unity, strength, dedication, time, physical and mental strength and personal budget to build. Joint achievements pass from one generation to the next for our descendants.
He also recalled the last stage of Cambodia's history in the phase of rescue and protection of the nation's resurrection, the stage of restoration and rebuilding the motherland until the Kingdom of Cambodia became a country with a single controlled area with a constitution. One with one king, one government and one armed force through the implementation of a win-win policy that has never been seen in Cambodia's 500-year history.
He also called on all the people of Kirivong district who are already here and who are already on the voter list to go to the 7th National Assembly election on Sunday, July 23, 2023. Let everyone not hesitate to exercise their civil rights as the masters of the destiny of their country and choose leaders who maintain peace and socio-economic development of Cambodia towards sustainable progress and prosperity.
