The owner of a frog farm in Prey Veng province complains about the problem of cheap frogs, the director of the Department of Agriculture urges farmers to contact experts to find a solution
(Phnom Penh): The owner of a large frog farm in Prey Veng province has complained that the price of frogs has dropped sharply this year, at only 5,400 riel per kilogram, up from 15,000 riel per kilogram.
According to farm owners, the drop in prices was due to the influx of Vietnamese frogs into Cambodia and continued to distribute the imported frogs to 25 provinces.
Vuthy, the owner of the Fisheries Frog Farm located in Svay Antor district, Prey Veng province, said he started raising frogs in 2016, which has been seven years now. For this year, the plan is to produce between 5-10 tons of meat frogs per month and between 700,000 baby frogs.
"Raising frogs depends on the big market, Phnom Penh, while the market in the provinces is small. In the last two years, the price of frogs has not dropped. At the beginning of 2023, frogs have maintained good prices "The price is between 10,000 and 11,000 riel per kilogram, but since April, the price of frogs has dropped sharply from 8,000 riel per kilogram to more than 5,000 riel per kilogram."
He added, "The drop in prices is due to the large import of frogs from Vietnam, and traders continue to distribute to provinces with cheap prices, making customers in the provincial capital and Phnom Penh began to lower prices and stop buying frogs from us. At the same time, these factors greatly affect the breeder.
The price of frogs has dropped to more than 5,000 riels per kilogram, which means that self-produced baby farms can withstand a small amount of losses, but for those who buy frogs to continue raising, it is impossible to resist these problems. Farms and adopters.
Ouk Samnang, director of the Prey Veng Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, confirmed to Fresh News that the drop in the price of frogs raised by farmers in Prey Veng province was largely due to the global economic crisis, the Russia-Ukraine war, and the impact on people's incomes. . He said that in some restaurants in Prey Veng province, there are not many guests to eat, so it is also a factor that makes the price of frogs fall.
He added that as the director of the department, all farmers with animal husbandry problems as well as falling prices must contact the Department of Agriculture to find a solution. Regarding the import of frogs from Vietnam, he did not get the basis that there are frogs imported, but a small number of traders always take the opportunity to import some.
He added that currently, the frog farming of farmers in Prey Veng province has decreased slightly to the existing farms, such as there is a hatchery for frogs is still raising. This frog is found in almost all districts of Prey Veng province. In order for the frogs to regain their value and market, restaurants and canteens in each of the provinces will open and have more visitors, and the frog prices will return to normal.
(Tbong Khmum): Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, said that Cambodia is now peaceful, harmonious, without conflict, violence and war. Under the shadow of peace for more than two decades, our youth really have a lot of opportunities, the comparison between the war youth and the peace youth is very different, almost incomparable.
This statement of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin was made this morning, June 5, 2023, on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the graduation ceremony for one of the winners of Heng Samrin University Tbong Khmum Tbong. , 249 people.
The President of the National Assembly continued that human resources are an important and indispensable factor for building and developing the national society. Each country can grow and prosper because it has human resources with knowledge, wisdom and good morals that can think, solve problems intelligently and can lead skillfully.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin emphasized that the wartime youth not only lost all good opportunities, enjoyed everything, but also lost their lives or were injured and disabled. Peaceful youth really get from the achievements of socio-economic development through education, vocational training and skills to participate in socio-economic development.
On that occasion, Samdech also asked the people, especially nephews and grandsons, who are the pillars of the nation, to unite and protect the peace that we have found with the greatest difficulty by making all kinds of sacrifices. Therefore, we must promote the spirit of compassion, love, understanding, empathy for others and work for the betterment of our society, "said the President of the National Assembly.
"We must remember that peace and development are closely linked," he said. Peace creates the necessary conditions for development. "Because of this complete peace, the country has achieved economic growth, social stability and sustainable development."
On behalf of the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party, Samdech is determined to continue to strengthen the unity of the whole nation, regardless of political affiliation, gender, religion, ethnicity and social status, to maintain and expand all achievements. Achieve peace, prosperity, and political stability in the process of building and defending the motherland.
