Samdech Techo Hun Sen Expresses Satisfaction with Women's Capacity Development in Cambodia and Has Contributed to National Economic Growth (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, expressed his satisfaction with the capacity development of women Women in Cambodia, in particular, have become women entrepreneurs who have made significant contributions to the family, society and the national economy.
Samdech Techo's remarks were made when he presided over the graduation ceremony for nearly 6,000 graduates from the Royal University of Law and Economics this morning, June 5, 2023.
Samdech Techo noted that at present, women play an important role in both the formal and informal economy. This factor urges the Royal Government to pay more attention to investment and encourage women to receive more training.
"At this point, we must not underestimate the investment in women. Now I am proud because when there is a gathering of women entrepreneurs or young entrepreneurs, we observe that women play a role in The economy is huge, so it is part of the responsibility in the family society. And the habit that when you have a husband depends on your husband's money, now you have no husband and no way, women also have a salary, do not underestimate them too much.
Samdech Techo also said that in the future, the Royal Government will spend money to provide training or training to about 1.5 million employees, especially those working in the informal economy.
Samdech Techo also noted that the number of female students who take the high school exam is higher than the number of male students and the number of female students who take the bachelor's degree exam is higher than the number of male students. Although the number of women undergraduate and doctoral degrees has decreased compared to male students, the number of women pursuing doctoral degrees has increased year by year, from 10% in the past to the present. This is up to almost 40%.
Speaking on the occasion of presenting diplomas to nearly 6,000 students of the Royal University of Law and Economics, Samdech Techo Hun Sen wants to draw the attention of all officials to their efforts to develop their abilities without stagnation One place, especially the digital economy stage.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Of course, we can not do anything in the past, but the past provides us with experience to guide the way for the present and the future." "Some theories say that in the past, no one can change the past."
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, what is the cause of the memorable experience of the past, both the progress at that time and the fact that the country fell into the flames of war?
The Prime Minister pointed out the experience of His Majesty the King in the 1960s, when he built so many achievements, even the National Olympic Stadium, which is now used for the SEA Games and the ASEAN Para Games. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also affirmed that the future must work together for Cambodia to move forward.
