Chinese defense minister warns against NATO-style military alliance in Asia-Pacific that could lead to regional conflict
BEIJING: China's defense minister on Sunday warned against forming a military alliance like NATO in the Asia-Pacific region, saying they would plunge the region into a serious conflict. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on June 4, 2023.
"Attempts to push for a military alliance like NATO in the Asia-Pacific region are a way to rob countries in the region and escalate conflicts," Li told a security conference in Singapore, also attended by the US Secretary of Defense. Confrontation.
He did not name any countries, but his comments echoed China's long-standing criticism of the United States for trying to strengthen alliances in the region. The United States is a member of the AUKUS Alliance, which cooperates with Australia and the United Kingdom, while Washington is also a member of QUAD, which includes Australia, India and Japan.
"We must not forget the bitter catastrophe brought by the two world wars to the people of all countries, and we must not allow such a tragic history to happen again," he said. No. ”
