Human resource training is a priority policy under the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister. Since liberating the country from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot on January 7, 1979, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has made every effort to promote training to rebuild human resources that were slaughtered during the Khmer Rouge regime.
With the introduction of policies to promote education, efforts to build schools, scatter schools closer to people's homes, Samdech Techo never tired of handing out diplomas to encourage graduates.
Samdech Techo's high presence at the graduation ceremony was a great source of emotional energy and honor for the graduates after their hard work overcoming difficulties during their studies.
Please note that the Royal University of Law and Economics is a well-known public higher education institution under the auspices of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
The University has been playing an important role in training human resources in law, public administration, economics and other areas to serve the economic and social development of Cambodia. From 1982 to the present, a total of 66,806 trainees and graduates (26,449 females or 39.5%), of which 226 are foreign students (96 females) 42.4 percent).
From 1993 to the present, the university has sent 1,799 students to study abroad for master's and doctoral degrees through partner universities.
In addition, 22 students participated in six direct international fiction competitions on international law organized by the United States, Austria, India, Hong Kong and Albania. By mid-2023, the university is preparing to send 12 students to four international fiction competitions in the Netherlands, Germany and India.
