(Phnom Penh): In human society on this planet since ancient times, in terms of numbers, it is considered as a magical power, giving glory to the organization of art: religion, architecture, city and human life in harmony.
Khmer civilization expert, Mr. Rath Sandab, stated that when it comes to the belief system of numbers, all nations, whether Khmer or any other nation in the world, always have rules according to their respective religious beliefs, cultures and traditions in order to Bring glory to society. The number 18 is in many belief systems, religions, cultures and traditions around the world.
Because the number 18 is in the Khmer belief system and the various ethnic belief systems are as follows:
In Buddhism, the number 18 is the power of the spirit of the Buddha, which represents the 18 arahants (disciples of the Buddha), the enlightenment of the Buddha. Because the 18 arahants are: the eight precepts and the ten precepts are 18.
Thus, the number 18 comes from a combination of the eight dharmas and the ten bodhisattvas, 18 called "the 18 arahants" is the enlightenment of the Buddha.
The spiritual significance of the number 18 is 1 + 8 is 9, which is considered a powerful spiritual number. Represents spiritual enlightenment, inner wisdom, and the end of a cycle, symbolizing good fortune, blessings, and longevity.
In China, the number 18 is considered the luckiest number because it sounds like the word "luck" in Mandarin. This is likely because the number 1 represents a new beginning and the 8 are identical to the word "jewelry", growing endlessly. When the two numbers are combined, it symbolizes unlimited potential for success. Is the lucky star ruling on Earth.
In meditation, the 18 evils are the bright light in front of you as you take a deep breath and relax into the state of all the good that will come into your life.
In love, the number 18 is the spiritual number of the love life, symbolizing the arrival of age and the beginning of puberty, commitment and eternal love.
9: Number 18 in the meaning of debate
Therefore, the number 18 is the power and energy of the spirit of the Buddha in enlightenment as our teacher, and that is why some parties with bad intentions want to destroy the nation and curse the spirit of our teacher before the election.
