Real estate experts say that while property prices in some areas are below market value, it is a good opportunity for the wealthy to make long-term investments to make a profit in the years to come. Return to better condition.
In an interview with Fresh News, Mr. Sorn Sieb, President of the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors, said that while the real estate sector is facing challenges due to the economic crisis, it is a good opportunity for the wealthy to buy for long-term investment. Long because at present some properties are sold below the market price of about 30% to 40%.
"I look at the present for those who have a lot of money, it is great for large investments such as usable buildings, office buildings, hotels, apartments or shops that can be rented back."
He said real estate products are the safest investment in the investment sector and more profitable than sending money to the bank.
He said that in the next three years, the real estate sector in Cambodia will return to normal, because since 2022, after the outbreak of Kovid 19, the Cambodian economy has continued to grow, according to the forecast. In 2023, the economy will grow by 5.6%, in 2024 it will grow by 6% and in 2025 it will return to 7%, so the real estate sector will continue to grow in line with economic growth.
According to the president of the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors, the current average price of property in Phnom Penh is around $ 2,000 per square meter. But for the five districts that have already been developed, such as Khan 7 Makara, Daun Penh, Toul Kork, Chamkarmon and Khan Boeung Keng Kang, the average price is around $ 4,000 per square meter.
