This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued to meet with more than 16,000 workers in Kong Pisey district
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Sunday, June 4, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued to meet with more than 16,000 workers. Others are from factories in Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that Samdech Techo Prime Minister had already met with workers in Kong Pisey District, Kampong Speu Province once on Wednesday, September 19, 2018, which was attended by workers. 27,444 people from 24 factories.
For the second meeting today, a total of 16,441 workers from 11 factories participated.
According to the Minister of Labor, the 11 factories where the workers participated in the meeting were 10 shoe factories and 1 bag factory. The products of these factories are exported to international markets, especially the European Union, the United States, Canada, Japan, etc.
The Minister also said that in Kampong Speu province in 2023, there are 385 factories with about 160,000 workers. There are 191 garment factories with a total of nearly 150,000 workers and it is the second province with the most industrial enterprises.
The Minister further stated that under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, Cambodia continues to maintain peace, stability and development in all areas of society and the national economy continues to grow proudly. Cambodia's economy has grown at an average rate of 7 percent for more than two decades, except during the Kovid-19 epidemic phase.
The labor market situation in Cambodia is strong, maintaining a high employment rate of 99.3 percent of the total labor force of about 10.8 million. Currently, there are 17,256 enterprises in the system registered with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training with 1.5 million workers.
It should be noted that in 1997, there were only 64 garment factories with about 80,000 workers, and exports were only 227 million US dollars.
In order to continue to promote economic growth, investment and better job and employment opportunities, from Sunday, August 20, 2017 to May 1, 2019, Samdech Ke Chou met with the first round of talks with 77 workers. There are about 1 million workers and 10 recommendations.
