Erdogan sworn in as Turkish president in new term
The new five-year term will allow Erdogan to pursue an increasingly authoritarian policy that has made Turkey a NATO member, but under consolidating its position as a regional military power.
"I, as President, swear by my honor and integrity to the Turkish people that I will defend the existence and independence of the state," Erdogan said at a ceremony at the Turkish National Assembly.
Following the swearing-in ceremony, another ceremony will be held at the Presidential Palace, attended by senior officials from 78 countries and international organizations, including the Secretary-General of NATO and the President of Venezuela, the Prime Minister of Hungary. And the Prime Minister of Armenia.
One dead and 27 others rushed to hospital in Pursat province on suspicion of alcohol poisoning
(Pursat): At least one man died and 27 others were rushed to Krakor District Referral Hospital and Pursat Provincial Referral Hospital on suspicion of alcohol poisoning at a funeral service in Krakor District. Pursat.
The case of alcohol poisoning occurred at 10 pm on June 1, 2023 at the house of the body named Sum Mey, located in Meat Prey village, Kampong Po commune, Krakor district, Pursat province.
Sources from the police force told Fresh News Agency that at low light on June 2, 2023, there was a case of a dead person on the victim named Hum Horn, male, 36 years old, farmer. Address: Meat Prey Village, Kampong Po Commune, Krakor District, Pursat Province. Another 27 people were rushed to Krakor District Referral Hospital and Pursat Provincial Referral Hospital.
According to the autopsy with the Pursat provincial forensic doctor and the explanation of the incident, we have not been able to conclude yet, that is, waiting for further research from the provincial PAC. The death was not linked to violence or murder, suspected to have been caused by alcohol poisoning at a funeral service called Sum Mey.
The bodies of the victims have now been handed over to their families to continue the traditional rites.
(Phnom Penh): After missing the last few years due to the crisis of Kovid 19, the whole world, in general, Cambodia, in particular, did not participate in the celebration of the World Blood Donor Day on June 14.
But for 2023, the National Blood Transfusion Center of the Ministry of Health is planning to re-organize this important event and call on the public, especially all blood donors, to donate blood to save the lives of patients who need blood. Every day.
World Blood Donor Day, June 14, is organized to address blood shortages and to promote voluntary and free blood donation. This is according to Dr. Sok Po, President of the National Blood Transfusion Center.
Dr. Sok Po continued, "Today, the voluntary and free blood donation in Cambodia, we still do not meet the needs yet. "So we need more volunteer blood donors to save lives urgently."
In Cambodia today, every six minutes a drop of blood is needed to save a patient's life. Therefore, the presence of free blood donors is very important to save our patients in time.
