This evening, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit open the ASEAN Para Games for the Disabled
(Phnom Penh): At around 6 pm on Saturday, June 15, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen. The President of the Cambodian Red Cross will invite the President to open the 12th ASEAN Para Games for the Disabled.
The opening ceremony of the historic event hosting the first Southeast Asian Games for the Disabled for Cambodia after this 24-year event will take place at the Moradok Techo National Stadium. The event will be grandly attended by senior leaders of the Royal Government of Cambodia, sports delegates from ASEAN with disabilities, national and international guests, athletes with disabilities and more than 60,000 people.
Please note that the ASEAN Para Games is a sport for people with disabilities in 11 countries in Southeast Asia. The tournament first kicked off in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia from October 26 to 29, 2001, with more than 700 athletes from Brunei, Myanmar, Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, the Philippines, Singapore, Thailand and Vietnam.
The ASEAN Para Games are held every two years, just like the SEA Games. Member countries are responsible for hosting the tournament in alphabetical order, one at a time.
In 2019, when the Philippines was scheduled to host, and in 2022, Vietnam was scheduled to host, but was missed by the COVID-19 crisis, the 10th and 11th ASEAN Para Games. In this situation, Indonesia also hosted the 11th ASEAN Para Games in July and August 2022.
The event was attended by a total of 2,692 sports delegates. The National Paralympic Committee of Cambodia organized 176 athletes, 76 female athletes, a total of 252 athletes, 70 coaches and assistant coaches, 16 leaders, 1 doctor, 4 team leaders and 1 mission leader. Three Deputy Chiefs of Mission.
Of the 252 disabled athletes, 32 were blind, 6 were female, 23 were cerebral palsy, 5 were female, 4 were mentally retarded, and 1 was female. Cambodian disabled athletes compete in a total of 261 events, 160 men's events, 80 women's events, 6 mixed doubles and 13 team events.
The National Paralympic Committee of Cambodia expects the medal index to increase by 50% compared to the 11th ASEAN Para Games, a total of 56 units, including 8 gold medals, 21 silver medals and 27 bronze medals. According to the Paralympics, Cambodia could be ranked 6th out of 11 participating countries.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has called on the Cambodian people to support the ASEAN Para Games in Cambodia as soon as the SEA Games ended on May 17.
Samdech Techo also announced to be a good host for the accommodation and welcome in the ASEAN Para Games.
