The United States and Taiwan's 21st Century Trade Initiative aims to boost trade by streamlining customs controls, improving regulatory procedures and establishing anti-corruption measures between the United States and the island, AFP reports. Autonomous Taiwan is claimed by China as part of its territory.
Although Washington and Taipei do not have formal diplomatic relations, the two sides maintain informal relations through the US Institute in Taiwan, which acts as the US Embassy informally.
The first agreement under the latest initiative was signed by representatives of the American Institute in Taiwan and the Office of Economic and Cultural Representatives, according to the US Trade Representative (USTR) on Thursday. Taipei, USA
China warned Washington on Thursday against signing any agreement that violates China's sovereignty or territorial integrity, according to the AFP news agency.
Foreign Ministry spokeswoman Mao Ning told a news conference that the United States "must not send false signals to Taiwan's independent forces in the name of trade."
