The following is the King's Decree: Cambodia, Vietnam sign agreement to boost bilateral trade for one more year
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and Vietnam have agreed to sign a bilateral trade promotion agreement for one more year (2023-2024), as this agreement has been implemented for seven years. The compromise was made to boost trade cooperation between the two countries.
The signing ceremony was held on the afternoon of June 2, 2023 under the chairmanship of Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Mr. NGUYEN HONG DIEN, Minister of Industry and Commerce. The ceremony was held on video, with the participation of leaders and relevant officials of both ministries.
The Prime Minister stressed that the initiation of the bilateral trade facilitation coordination was made under the high guidance of the two countries' leaders through a joint Cambodian-Vietnamese statement between the Prime Minister of Cambodia and the Prime Minister of Vietnam. Agreed in 2005 in Hanoi, Vietnam to develop a preferential tariff policy for goods originating in their respective countries.
The minister said that so far, representatives of the two ministries have signed the document seven times and agreed to renew it once on the bilateral trade facilitation agreement.
The Vietnamese Minister of Industry and Trade also praised the long-standing friendship, traditional and comprehensive relations between the two countries, especially the initiation of the Cambodia-Vietnam Joint Statement between Cambodia and Vietnam in formulating favorable policies. On customs duties for goods originating in their respective countries.
The Vietnamese minister also said that the bilateral trade facilitation agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Vietnam for 2023-2024, which has now been signed, is an important document for businesses and exporters and importers. Both will help boost exports and imports between the two countries in addition to the agreements within the framework of the ASEAN Commodity Trade Agreement.
The Vietnamese Minister of Industry and Trade also highlighted the two governments' efforts to promote the nation despite the global impact of the Kovid-19 epidemic crisis. In this regard, the Vietnamese Minister stressed the importance of signing and implementing the agreement to further boost trade volume, especially agricultural and industrial goods.
During the ceremony, the two ministers expressed great optimism about the bilateral trade facilitation coordination, stating that the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia and the Ministry of Industry and Trade of Vietnam will actively work together to promote producers and leaders. Exports, importers and businesses aim to maximize the implementation and maximize the benefits of the bilateral trade facilitation agreement.
