Commentary: Is the US Debt Problem Really Solved?
BEIJING (Reuters) - The US House of Representatives recently voted to pass a bill on the debt ceiling, which has suspended the debt ceiling until the beginning of 2025 and restricts spending in fiscal years. 2024 and the fiscal year 2025. This seems to have given some people some relief. But furthermore, is this issue really being addressed? Can America and the world be at peace again?
But the plan only delays the resolution of disputes, does not address the root causes, and instead makes the United States more indebted. Some analysts have speculated that US debt will reach an all-time high in early 2025, by which time the US economy may emerge with systemic problems.
