Chinese special envoy believes that both Ukraine and Russia are not yet completely closed on the possibility of negotiations
BEIJING: Chinese Special Envoy for Eurasian Affairs Li Hui said on Friday that in his view, both Ukraine and Russia do not seem to have closed completely. As for the possibility of negotiation, although it is currently difficult to push for negotiations to begin now. This was released by the AFP news agency on Friday, June 2, 2023.
"The risk of escalating the war between Russia and Ukraine remains high," said the Chinese special envoy. Both sides need to take concrete action to ease the situation. "As long as it can serve the purpose of easing the war situation, China is willing to do anything."
Li, who served as China's ambassador to Russia from 2009 to 2019, is the highest-ranking Chinese official to visit Ukraine since Russia launched the invasion in February. 2022 is coming. However, his visit did not seem to achieve any major diplomatic progress for the Ukraine crisis.
