According to Seng Teak, Executive Director of the Global Fund for the Conservation of Natural Resources (WWF), from 2019 to 2022, scientists have discovered more than 380 new species of wildlife and plants in the Mekong region, including Cambodia. .
Mr. Seng Teak said that among the new species and biodiversity found in the Mekong region, Cambodia is the smallest because the research capacity of Cambodian scientists is still limited compared to other countries.
