More than 1.5 tons of damaged chicken wings imported from Vietnam were seized and burned by Kandal Provincial Police
(Kandal): Defective chicken wings imported from Vietnam were seized by the competent authorities of Kandal Provincial Police and burned in Kien Svay District, Kandal Province on June 1, 2023.
In this case, the police arrested two people, the driver was Loun Sambath, 33 years old, in Thmey village, Bosim commune, Romduol district, Svay Rieng province, and the other was Sar Vuthy, 28 years old, in Samor village, Bos Mon commune, Romduol district, Svay Rieng province. The team then took the above exhibits and kept them at the Kien Svay District Police Inspectorate temporarily, waiting for the procedure to continue.
In this case, the representative of the owner of the goods agreed to pay the fine according to the law on quality control, safety of products and services, Article 62. 347 Families in Andong 6 Community, Khan Prek Pnov Receive Donations from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit
(Phnom Penh): 347 families in Andong 6 community, Sangkat Kork Roka, Khan Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh, on the evening of June 1, 2023, received donations from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen through Mr. Khuong Sreng. Governor of Phnom Penh.
Ms. Mom Chandani, Chairperson of the Kork Roka Sangkat Assistance Team, Khan Prek Pnov, stated that the priority tasks to help the local community in Kork Roka Sangkat include water, electricity, and school infrastructure, which are essential for the community.
The implementation of the cash support program for pregnant women and children under 2 years old now shows the virtuous and wise gestures of the leaders in providing confidence and warmth in accordance with the policy. Of the Royal Government and the strategy of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation.
