Ministry of Economy and Finance opens training course on "Review of investment projects at the capital and provincial level"
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hean Sahip, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and Chairman of the Working Group for the "OWSO" Meeting on June 2, 2023, presided over the opening of the training course. On "Review of Investment Projects at the Capital and Provincial Levels".
He said that this training is part of strengthening the capacity of human resources to fulfill the core and relevant mission of the Ministry of Economy and Finance in accordance with the "Vision of the Ministry 2030 as an institution of excellence with sufficient capacity and qualifications" under Led by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance.
At the same time, the Royal Government has issued a sub-decree on the organization and functioning of the Capital and Provincial Sub-Committees to give more decision-making power and delegation to the sub-national administration to review and approve existing investment projects. Equivalent investment capital is less than 5 million US dollars.
Dr. Hean Sahip stated that the Law on Investment of Cambodia provides more attractive and favorable incentives for investment by Cambodian and foreign individuals, including investment guarantee and protection, investment maintenance services and Dispute resolution. In addition, the Royal Government will issue a sub-decree on the implementation of the Investment Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which is more detailed and more than the previous sub-decree.
Dr. Hean Sahip encouraged the participants of this training to pay attention, listen, understand and record by focusing on the laws, regulations, procedures and experience of examining the investment projects of these institutions, especially those under Jurisdiction of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
He added that the training was a good starting point and that there would be a series of training sessions on similar and different topics, as well as outreach activities and the sharing of documents and information.
