(Kandal): Thirty-six families who bought a house from Borey Seng Socheat in Vihear Sour village, Vihear Sour commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province have a valid plan, but when they want to sell, they can not sell it, asking the management to help solve this problem. He.
Heng Thon, a representative of 36 families, said that he and the other 35 families had bought an apartment from Borey Seng Socheat and had a solid plan since 2019, but what was surprising was the sale of the house. On the other hand, the cadastre of Khsach Kandal district said that the whole Borey was protected by a protection order because there was a lawsuit between two shareholders in the business of selling the Borey in May 2022.
Hel Modeth, chief of the Khsach Kandal district cadastre, said he had seen the court's protection order and did not dare to sign the deal and had already reported it to the land department.
It should be informed that Civil Judgment No. 33 "D" dated 16 May 2022, which has Ms. Pech Maren as the Judge and Mr. Leng Thursday is the Clerk, has decided to dismiss the appeal dated 4 December 2021 by Seng Socheat 40 years old.
The verdict was issued orally and publicly announced on 16 May 2022 in the presence of a lawyer representing the plaintiff and anonymous defendant Seng Socheat.
The Forum on Tobacco Products Tax Measures was held on June 1, 2023 at the Sunway Hotel, Phnom Penh, with the participation of representatives of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, NGOs and about 200 stakeholders.
Mr. Van Puthipol further stated that Samdech Techo Prime Minister recently approved the request letter of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, which requires the taxation of cigarette products at all stages for imported cigarettes, while previously Cambodia only taxed on time. Import only once. At the same time, officials of the General Department of Customs and Excise and the General Department of Taxation also made efforts to inspect tobacco products in the target provinces effectively.
On that occasion, the NGO also supported the Ministry of Economy and Finance in the tobacco tax reform process and considered that the additional tax starting from 500 Riels per pack of cigarettes or more is most appropriate for now.
The World Health Organization has made it clear that raising tobacco taxes is the single most effective measure to reduce the risks posed by tobacco. About 15,000 Cambodians die each year from diseases caused by tobacco use, with more than 40 deaths a day.
These include stroke, coronary heart disease, lower respiratory tract infections, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and cancer of the lungs, bronchi and trachea. Thirty-three percent of all deaths occur in the lowest-income population. In addition, tobacco use caused a loss of US $ 649 million, equivalent to 3% of Cambodia's GDP.
Ukraine removes state of emergency claiming to have shot down 30 Russian drones and ammunition
(Kiev): Ukrainian authorities on Friday lifted the alert for airstrikes in various parts of the country as Kiev officials said the air defense system fired down missiles and drones. More than 30 Russian items and accessories. This was released by the AFP news agency on Friday, June 2, 2023.
Moscow has launched 20 separate drone strikes and missile launches on several Ukrainian cities since early May. According to the Ukrainian military, in the strikes, Russia fired cruise missiles and drone strikes at the same time.
Since early May, Ukraine has repeatedly claimed that its air defense system has shot down most Russian drones and missiles, including supersonic missiles.
Dr. Kun Nhem Leads a Cambodian Customs Delegation to the 24th Asia-Pacific Customs Director-General Conference of the World Customs Organization in Australia
(Australia): Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia from 28 to 31 May 2023 in Perth, Australia, led a delegation of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia. Attended the 24th Asia-Pacific Customs Director-General Conference of the World Customs Organization.
He noted the efforts of the customs administrations of all member countries in the region to jointly implement the Regional Strategic Plan (RSP), despite some challenges.
Kunio Mikuriya, Secretary-General of the World Customs Organization, thanked the Australian Border Forces for hosting the conference, and said that the large-scale direct participation of regional customs representatives was a sign of full and active cooperation. Disorders caused by the Kovid-19 epidemic.
The Secretary-General commended and appreciated the achievements made by the Asia-Pacific Customs Administration and highlighted the progressive progress and potential of the Asia-Pacific Customs in carrying out its roles and responsibilities. In the national and regional frameworks.
Australian Home Minister Clair O'Neil welcomed the distinguished guests and delegates and stressed the importance of customs cooperation, especially on trade facilitation, crime prevention and cross-border crime. Protect national security and so on.
The Minister praised the Customs Cooperation through the implementation of "Joint Operation" on a number of specific challenges and said that the current conference will provide an opportunity for the leaders of the Customs Administration to discuss and work out directions to strengthen Further, more active and effective regional cooperation.
During the meeting, Minister Kun Nhim intervened on a number of agendas and thanked the WCO ROCB / AP Regional Capacity Building Office for supporting the Cambodian Customs Administration in the process of preparing and implementing the application procedure. The National Customs School of Cambodia will become a WCO-recognized regional training center in the future.
The delegation of the Cambodian Customs Administration also paid a courtesy call on Dr. Kunio Mikuriya, Secretary-General of the World Customs Organization, to wish and express special gratitude to the Royal Government of Cambodia for its outstanding achievements in Lead the World Customs Organization and have good relations and support for the Cambodian Customs Administration in the past.
(Phnom Penh): Known as a security guard for almost 5 years, a security guard had an argument with a tourist police officer in a drinking circle, and suddenly a fight broke out, leaving the male police officer with his back to the stairs and seriously injured As of this morning, June 1, 2023, the family confirmed that the victim died of a blood clot in the brain.
This incident happened on May 31, 2023 in Ta Ngov village, Niroth commune, Chbar Ampov district. The victim was 48-year-old Sin Komsat, a tourist police officer of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police. Separately, the suspect is a security guard named Kang Sarath Charlie, 43 years old, living in Phum Sen Sok 1, Sangkat Khmuonh, Khan Sen Sok.
On the morning of June 1, 2023, doctors told the victim's family that there was no hope, with a serious injury, a blood clot in the brain, and the family took an ambulance to bring the victim home, then died at home. Niroth, Chbar Ampov district, and then reported to the authorities for a forensic examination on the victim's head from behind, causing a fatal collision.
US calls on UN to hold meeting on North Korean satellite launch
The United States has called on the UN Security Council to convene on Friday to discuss North Korea's attempt to launch a satellite this week. This was released by Reuters on Friday, June 2, 2023.
North Korea on Wednesday launched its first military reconnaissance satellite, but failed as a second batch of rockets and satellites crashed into the sea. Washington and its two main allies, South Korea and Japan, have condemned the satellite launch, accusing it of violating UN Security Council resolutions for using ballistic missile technology and destabilizing the region. .
The United States has called for a meeting to discuss a North Korean satellite launch, said Nate Evans, a spokesman for the US Mission to the United Nations. Japan, Malta, the United Kingdom, Albania, Ecuador and France also supported the call.
Interior Ministry spokesman: 37 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on June 1 yesterday
(Phnom Penh): At least 37 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on June 1, 2023 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on June 2, 2023.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 37 suspects, 19 were arrested in 12 criminal cases and 18 were arrested in eight drug offenses.
Kandal Provincial Court Charges and Detains Two Robbers After Robbery in Ang Snoul District
(Kandal): Investigating Judge Ouk Sovannarith and Prosecutor Chin Lida decided to charge and detain two robbers after a robbery in Ang Snoul district on charges of “aggravated theft due to an act Violence ”charged under Articles 353 and 357 of the Penal Code.
According to Mr. So Sarin, Spokesman of Kandal Provincial Court, on the evening of June 1, 2023, Article 353 - Definition of theft: Theft is an act of fraudulent confiscation of property or other objects. Of others by any means for the purpose of owning it.
Article 357: Aggravating circumstances for committing violence: Theft is punishable by imprisonment from 3 to 10 years in the following cases: This theft took place before, during or after the violence. 2. This theft is committed by cutting, breaking, breaking.
The story of the robbery and arrest is as follows: Police force of Ang Snoul district, Kandal province, in cooperation with the police of Khan Kampoul, Phnom Penh, arrested two out of three motorcycle thieves after robbing a motorcycle from a woman on May 29. 2023 on the back road of Ta Hor canal, Kandos village, Lumhach commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province.
The arrests were made on May 30, 2023. There were three suspects and two were arrested, Pheng Sophanna, 41, and Pheng Ra, 43. The fugitive was Phuong Thorn, alias Tran, 55 years old.
According to the police report, the victim was named Chhay Soloth, a 19-year-old female resident of Kandos Village, Lumhach Commune, Ang Snoul District, Kandal Province.
After receiving a complaint from the victim, the specialized police force cooperated with the Lumhach police force to investigate and identify the target and arrested two suspects with some exhibits. After the arrest, the police brought the suspect to the district police inspectorate for further questioning.
On the orders of Major General Chhoeun Socheat, Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner, and with the coordination of Mr. Leav Sreng, the Prosecutor of Kandal Provincial Court, the Special Forces were allowed to cooperate with the Boeung Thom Police Force of the Phnom Penh Police Inspectorate and Village and Sangkat authorities continue to search the suspect's rented room at Tuol Svay village, Sangkat Boeung Thom, Khan Kampol, Phnom Penh.
JAKARTA: Indonesia and Malaysia will delay trade talks with the European Union (EU) as the two countries seek fair treatment for small palm oil producers. According to Reuters.
Indonesia and Malaysia earlier this month sent top officials to the European Union to express concern over deforestation laws they believe could harm small agricultural businesses.
Both countries are the world's largest producers of palm oil and account for about 85 percent of the world's palm oil exports. The EU is their third largest market.
