11: International Analysis: Putin's war is an opportunity for the United States
NATO-supplied weapons to Ukraine are reportedly continuing to be used in attacks on Russian territory. The attack on Russian territory included both drones and artillery.
At the same time, US intelligence officials denied that there was any evidence that the drones that carried out the subsequent attacks on Russian territory were US-made.
Russian leader Vladimir Putin said after a Ukrainian drone strike on Moscow on Tuesday called the attack on civilian infrastructure on Russian soil an act of terrorism.
Vladimir Putin has said that the Kiev regime has chosen to intimidate Russia and its people by carrying out attacks on people's homes. Putin has called for further strengthening of Russia's air defense system.
The attack on Moscow prompted some Russian officials to want Vladimir Putin to declare a full-scale war with Ukraine. Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov said Wednesday that Russia has no plans to declare martial law to declare a full-scale war on Ukraine.
Observers say that while the counterattack has not yet begun, Ukraine appears to be shifting its military strategy by using drones to attack Russia in as many populated areas as it could in its territory. Russia. The Ukrainian military said the attack appeared to be more successful than on the battlefield and cost less ammunition than the drone.
Situation observers say the use of drones in this age of technology has changed the way they attack in the past. Both Ukraine and Russia are now using drones to attack each other.
Ukraine's drone unit says the use of drones in warfare has significantly reduced the lives of soldiers on the battlefield and the use of drones is cheaper than the more expensive weapons used in combat. The use of drones has helped them gain access to Russian information and hideouts in the jungle, and victory over attacks on Russian troops has always relied heavily on drones.
According to social media images, Ukrainian intelligence drones captured images of Russian soldiers drying blankets and seeing Russian war vehicles hidden in the forest. The Ukrainian military says the use of drones is useful in saving lives. If soldiers enter the forest without knowing the incident, they will be trapped by the enemy, so they must first know the information through aerial reconnaissance drones.
The Ukrainian military says drones, in addition to being used for intelligence purposes, can be used to sell cheap drones on the market by designing explosive devices to attack enemies.
