(Phnom Penh): One in five school boys drowned as they went to take a bath and ride in a raft in a pit, and while rowing, the raft suddenly slipped and fell. Enter the water. At that time, one of the boys jumped out of the swimming raft to pick it up, causing the boy to drown in the water, much to his surprise.
The above incident happened on the evening of June 1, 2023 at an old land pit located east of Wat Taphem, Tuol Talat Village, Sangkat Kampol, Khan Kampol, Phnom Penh.
According to the police, the dead boy named Kol Sambath Reach, 15 years old, an 8th grade student at Hun Sen Bun Rany Arunvati Secondary School, resided in Trapeang Tea Village, Sangkat Trapeang Krasaing, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
Authorities confirmed that at 2:30 pm, the victim boy and four other friends left the school, but did not go home, but took a bath and raft in the water pit. On the contrary. While riding the raft, the boy slipped and fell into the water, then one of the boys jumped out of the raft to get the boat, causing the boy to drown.
