Minister of Labor mentions factors that promote the development of the labor market in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): In a lecture on "Labor Market and Economic Development" at the Royal School of Administration on June 1, 2023, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, focused on the mission and success of the Ministry of Labor. Labor market development in Cambodia and contribution to national economic development.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng stated that the Ministry of Labor pays close attention to the development of the labor market in response to changes in the socio-economic and technological structure, as well as to promote economic growth and strengthen social welfare through active participation in Implement some important national strategies and policies set by the Royal Government.
The Minister said that the labor market situation in Cambodia is strong, maintaining a high employment rate of about 99.3% of the total labor force, and the jobs created today are jobs in the modern industry with added value. And higher productivity, demand for more skilled labor, better working conditions and better incomes.
The Ministry has continued to increase employment opportunities in the country through the National Employment Agency (NEA) by disseminating labor market information, expanding consulting and employment guides, organizing job forums, and training for job market preparation skills. The option to seek legal overseas employment opportunities with good working conditions and high income.
The Minister said that the Ministry is working to improve working conditions and harmonization of industrial relations and successfully implement the 10 recommendations of the Prime Minister during a face-to-face meeting with workers. Past.
In addition, the Ministry of Labor continues to improve occupational safety and health of workers through legislation, improving the quality of transportation to be safer and in line with technical standards, promoting the participation of employers in supporting community nurseries near the factory area. Original.
