He also pointed out that Cambodia has exported some spare parts and components to Korea, including: auto parts, car components, wiring, etc., all of which are manufactured. Up with quality recognition from the Korean market.
"These are testimonies that show that Cambodia can produce goods that are competitive with other countries in the Korean market, especially technical goods made by skilled workers, not just clothing, footwear, bicycles or bags," he said. "Processes produced by labor."
Please be informed that the negotiation of the CKFTA agreement is an initiative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the occasion of the state visit of the President of the Republic of Korea, MOON Jae-In, to Cambodia in March 2019 to strengthen And expand economic and trade ties between the two countries.
The CKFTA agreement was officially announced on July 9, 2020 via video by the two countries' trade ministers, and went through a total of 12 rounds of negotiations before signing the agreement. Officially on October 26, 2021. The agreement was ratified by the Korean National Assembly on September 27, 2022.
This agreement is Cambodia's second bilateral trade agreement after the Cambodia-China Bilateral Free Trade Agreement came into force in January 2022, while Cambodia also has an RCEP agreement with 15 participating countries, including: The 10 ASEAN members and five other free trade partners are Australia, China, Japan, South Korea and New Zealand.
The Cambodia-Korea Bilateral Free Trade Agreement (CKFTA) entered into force on December 1, 2022, which is expected to boost exports between the two countries and contribute to economic recovery after the crisis. Kovid-19 and the Russo-Ukraine War.
