(Oddar Meanchey): A female trader living in Trabek village, Sangkat Bosbov, Samrong city, Oddar Meanchey province, was robbed by two suspects in the uniform of an NGO worker who came to drink coffee and stole about 2 million wallets in her basket. Riel escaped safely. The incident happened at 10 am on May 31, 2023.
According to the description of the victim, Hin Khemara, 34 years old, a trader living in the commune, the incident occurred that before the incident, two suspects came on a motorcycle to drink. Coffee at his house, dressed as an organization employee.
The two suspects then asked him if he had any relatives who were disabled, while the victim replied to the two staff members that there may be relatives with disabilities in his village. .
According to the victim, while questioning him, one of the suspects asked to go to the bathroom and the other continued to question him and let him talk on the phone while he was talking on the phone. The suspect also saw a basket of money on the table and stole it, called another person, got on a motorcycle and quickly disappeared, then he shouted that the thieves, but no one helped because the location The place where he sells is quiet.
After the incident, the victim reported to the police of the Samrong City Police Inspectorate, immediately two police officers arrived at the scene and questioned the record.
According to the competent experts at the checkpoint above, in this incident, it is not a case of applying any medicine, it is a case of pretending to be an employee of an opportunistic organization when the victim woman is talking on the phone and alone. He also reached for the wallet in the basket that the victim had left behind and got on a motorcycle to escape.
Currently, the competent authorities are continuing to carefully research by checking the images on the security cameras to determine the real face of Phin Pheak in order to arrest the two suspects and take legal action. Eleven Families Affected by Convulsions and the Elderly in Chongkal District Receive Humanitarian Donations from the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Oddar Meanchey Province
