(Earth): Since ancient times, most people around the world have considered the sun as a star that revolves around the planet, always rising from the east and setting in the west, but also. Some later scholars discovered the fact that it is our earth that revolves around the sun.
Did you know that who knew that the earth revolved around the sun for the first time in our human history?
Aristotle not only claimed that the earth and other asteroids revolved around the sun, he also calculated the size and distance between the earth-sun and the earth-moon.
He also claimed that the sky is not as heaven as everyone believes, but it is a vast universe almost in size. The Samaritans' claim was not supported by the masses of the time, as they already believed in the religious theory that the sun and the moon revolve around the earth and that the sky is Heaven for the living gods.
It was not until Roman civilization that Aristotle re-introduced the same theory, calling him a genius in all kinds of science.
