Samdech Techo Hun Sen Calls for 8 Points to Contribute to the Promotion of Children's Rights for Full Rights
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Honorary President of the Cambodian National Council for Children, on the occasion of the 74th Anniversary of International Children's Day, June 1, 22nd Anniversary of the World Day Against Child Labor, June 12 and Cambodian Children's Day. 2023 calls for eight points to contribute to the promotion of children's rights so that they have full rights as stipulated in national and international law.
Samdech Techo added that in this spirit, please make the following calls:
1. The Cambodian National Council for Children must continue to coordinate and strengthen the implementation of legal documents related to child protection as an inter-ministerial, effective civil society development partner institution, especially on information literacy, and promote the Cambodian people to become A secure and beneficial digital population.
2. All relevant ministries and institutions, including the competent authorities, parents, guardians, communities and children, must cooperate to find solutions and develop strategies to change social attitudes through positive counseling and discipline for children, and to work together to prevent all forms of child exploitation and abuse. Online appropriately and on time.
3. Ministries, institutions, local authorities at all levels, development partners, civil society organizations must pay attention to consult with children every time to develop laws, policies and legal documents related to their lives, needs, challenges and concerns. In particular, promote the comprehensive implementation of children's rights.
4. Raise awareness of online security and digital citizenship and strengthen effective enforcement of laws and regulations related to victim protection.
5: Ministries, institutions, local authorities, communities and all citizens must participate in the implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes, sangkats, especially to take measures to protect children from all forms of violence, to educate children on how to protect against all forms of sexual abuse and abuse. Intimidation of all kinds and must make children understand how to report to the authorities or adults who care for them in all forms of abuse.
6. Ministries and institutions must continue to implement the core conventions of the International Labor Organization to eliminate all forms of child labor by raising awareness, training and disseminating the prevention of the use of child labor in all economic activities and strengthening child labor inspection measures and mobilizing resources. And the public movement to find appropriate solutions to save child labor.
7. All public and private radio and television stations, as well as social media, continue to help spread the word about online child sexual exploitation and abuse and all forms of child labor, especially to improve the quality of children's programs. With the content of education to prevent children from becoming victims.
8. Increase cooperation between ministries, institutions, local authorities at all levels, development partners, national and international NGOs to prevent, intervene and provide appropriate and timely response services to contribute to the prevention of child sexual exploitation and abuse. Online system and eliminate child labor in Cambodia.
