Senior officials of the Ministry of Health, Ambassador of Australia and UNICEF inspect the provision of health services in Takeo province
(Takeo): The delegation of Dr. Prak Sophorn Neary, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, together with the Australian Ambassador to Cambodia and UNICEF Country Director for Cambodia, began a two-day visit from 30 to Wednesday 31 May 2023. Come to Takeo to inspect the provision of primary health care and integrated services after the global Kovid epidemic.
Dr. Prak Sophoan Neary, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works, stated that the purpose of the visit was to find out the status of the provision of essential health services in the aftermath of the Kovid Outbreak and to inspect the use of refrigeration systems and freezers for storing vaccines. Both establish routine activities for children and provide Kovid vaccine.
"It is very important that the essential health services are quality and accessible to all people, including the most affected communities and in remote areas," he said. Australia's latest contribution to UNICEF demonstrates our commitment to our commitment to inclusive and equitable health services.
"We are committed to continuing to work together under the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia to improve the health outcomes of Cambodian children and their families," said Dr. Will Phat, UNICEF Country Director for Cambodia. "The experience of Kovid vaccination shows that integrated services that provide equity, active community participation and local provision of services can have a broader impact on the health and well-being of the Cambodian people."
It should be noted that since the launch of the 19 19 measles vaccination in Cambodia in early 2021, the Australian Government, through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade and UNICEF, has been working together to provide support to The Ministry of Health of Cambodia to provide safe, effective and equitable vaccines, including the introduction of mRNA vaccines and the development of the first extreme cooling system in Cambodia.
