(Phnom Penh): From a letter from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Honorary President of the Cambodian National Council for Children on the occasion of the 74th anniversary of International Children's Day, June 1, the 22nd anniversary of the World Day Against Child Labor, June 12 and Cambodian Children's Day 2023 emphasizes that children are an indispensable resource for the development of the nation. This is according to the message that Fresh News received on May 31, 2023.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in all stages of the implementation of the Rectangular Strategy, the Royal Government of Cambodia has identified "people" as the top priority. Child development is an important foundation in building potential human capital for Cambodia's future development.
According to Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the Royal Government of Cambodia has fully implemented and has a clear vision to promote the rights and interests of children, ensuring that children, families and communities enjoy the quality and value of living in freedom. Dignity, equality and security in accordance with the Constitution and the rule of law through active, full and equal participation in the development of all sectors and at all levels.
The Royal Government of Cambodia attaches great importance to strengthening the health sector through the promotion of reproductive health, child nutrition and the reduction of maternal, infant and child mortality. The maternal mortality rate of children under 5 years old and infant mortality rate have decreased significantly, which is a further acceleration of progress towards achieving the 2030 Sustainable Development Goals.
At the same time, the Royal Government of Cambodia has integrated information and communication technology into the curriculum and education system in order to implement it effectively and in accordance with the new context of globalization. In addition, the Royal Government of Cambodia has set out a national social protection policy and is promoting the implementation of this policy to indigenous peoples to promote welfare, social unity and reduce poverty to the maximum.
The social assistance system provides support to people living below and near the poverty line, with a particular focus on children, pregnant women, the disabled, the elderly and the homeless. In fact, the Royal Government of Cambodia has implemented a cash support program for pregnant women and children under 2 years of age in poor families to alleviate the burden of improving the lives and nutrition of women and children.
In addition, the cash assistance program for poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid-19 and the cash support program for vulnerable families during inflationary pressures are effective government intervention programs in Poverty reduction.
