(Phnom Penh): The peace that is prevailing in Cambodia, combined with the strong leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has led to a series of achievements for the benefit of the nation and the people of Cambodia.
Two other important achievements for the traffic of the people in Phnom Penh, the bridge across the Tonle Sap and the Russey Keo flyover, will be officially inaugurated on Tuesday, the 12th day of the month of Ches. It will be on May 31, 2023, after giving people temporary transit for more than a month.
The inauguration of these two bridges will take place under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The growth of the population, the increase of traffic under the current growth of the society has made the traffic in Phnom Penh very congested. Seeing the traffic congestion, the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, has always considered and studied ways to relieve traffic by building flyovers and bridges across rivers in Phnom Penh.
The bridge over the Tonle Sap and the Russey Keo flyover are important bridges for people to travel between National Roads 5 and 6, as well as people living on both sides of the Tonle Sap.
The bridge is 510 meters long, 20.5 meters wide and has a total length of 922 meters. The runway of the bridge has 6 lanes for two-way traffic, 3 lanes to and 3 lanes. There are two lanes on each side for cars and one lane for motorcycles.
The bridge has 40-meter-high cable-stayed pillars and four octagonal pillars, with a minimum spacing of 72 meters and a maximum spacing of 120 meters. The diameter is 2 meters and the depth is between 33 meters and 62 meters.
In addition to the construction of the bridge and the road connecting the bridge, there are also some infrastructures to be installed in this project, including the installation of street lighting poles, the arrangement of the drainage network on both sides of the bridge road, the installation of traffic signs and Paint traffic signs in the construction area.
After the construction is completed, with the permission of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has temporarily put the people and passengers to use the Russey Keo Bridge across the Tonle Sap from April 10, 2023 until This.
The Russey Keo flyover is located along National Road 5 at the intersection of Street 36 in Russey Keo, Phnom Penh. The bridge was inaugurated on January 31, 2022 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
The bridge took more than 16 months to build. After the construction is completed and with the permission of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the administration of Phnom Penh has put the people and passengers to use temporarily from March 1, 2023 until now.
The Russey Keo flyover was built at a cost of US $ 9,710,474 from the Koh Nora Development Fund of the Overseas Cambodian Investment Company (OCIC). This bridge is the sixth flyover that has been built under the cooperation between the administration of Phnom Penh and the private sector in accordance with the recommendations and strict actions of Samdech Techo Prime Minister: "Take the city to feed the city or take palm leaves to pack sugar. "Brown."
The Russey Keo flyover is 15.8 meters wide, 145 meters long, and the road connecting the northern part of the bridge is 157 meters long and the southern part is 181 meters long, with a total length of 483 meters.
The runway of the bridge is 3.25 meters wide plus 3.50 meters for two-way traffic, divided into 2 lanes to 2 cars and 2 lanes. One-way along National Road 5 towards Prek Pnov Bridge, one-way along National Road 5 towards Chroy Changva Bridge and two-way road across National Road 5 towards Russey Keo Bridge.
In addition to the construction of the bridge and the road connecting the bridge, there are also some infrastructure to be installed in this project, including the installation of street lighting poles, traffic signs, traffic signs, road sewerage, and Editing sidewalks in the construction area.
This is a new achievement and a new history on the waters of Phnom Penh, separately and collectively for the whole of Cambodia under the leadership of the Royal Government, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. This achievement is possible because Cambodia has maintained complete peace, no flames of war and national unity and territorial integrity for more than 20 years.
In addition to peace, this achievement reflects the spirit and will of the leadership of the Royal Government, which always puts the interests of the nation and the people first. The people of Cambodia, especially those living in Phnom Penh, have expressed great enthusiasm for this great achievement. Vietnam's exports and industrial output fall in first five months
(VOVworld) - Vietnam's exports in the first five months of this year fell 11.6 percent from a year earlier to 136.7 billion, government data showed on Monday. Million dollars. According to Reuters.
Industrial output during the January-May period also fell 2 percent from a year earlier, Reuters reported, citing a report released by Vietnam's General Statistics Office (GSO). The report added that the average consumer price in this period increased by 3.55% compared to the same period last year.
The latest data underscores the slowdown in economic growth for Vietnam, a major regional manufacturing hub, due to declining global demand.
This sharp drop in imports could indicate further industrial production declines in the future as businesses cut back on purchases of raw materials and equipment. Vietnam is a major exporter of electronics, clothing and textiles, footwear and wooden items, as well as world-renowned brands.
US says revision of tariffs on Chinese imports does not depend on talks
(Detroit): The United States is taking steps to scrutinize whether to keep tariffs on Chinese goods or remove them, and any decision will not depend on the outcome of trade relations between the United States and China. No, China. According to Reuters.
Reuters quoted Sarah Bianchi, deputy director of the USTR Trade Representative, as saying in an interview last weekend that the government of US President Joe Biden does not expect a breakthrough. Of any such trade relations between the two countries, but will continue the dialogue with China on various levels.
Instead, she said, the USTR Trade Representative Office is continuing to study the views of industry insiders and stakeholders on the tariff, in consultation with the US Department of Commerce, the Treasury Department and other agencies to determine the strategy. Which type means strategy.
Former US President Donald Trump imposed tariffs in 2018 and 2019 on thousands of goods imported from China worth about $ 370 billion at the time. Tariffs currently range from 7.5 percent for most consumer goods to 25 percent for automobiles, industrial parts, electronics and other electronics. According to Reuters.
