A concrete road with a length of nearly 2 km in Kampong Chet Tbong commune, Stong district, Kampong Thom province will be opened for construction and will be completed in mid-June.
(Kampong Thom): This concrete road is 1,700 meters long, 6 meters wide and 0.15 meters thick in Leap Tong village to Kampong Chen village in Kampong Chet Tbong commune, Stong district, Kampong Thom province, which is a construction project of the Ministry of Rural Development. On May 30, 2023, this road will be completed in mid-June 2023.
On the occasion of the opening of the road construction site, Mr. Say Kim Lam, Governor of Stong District, urged the people living on both sides of the road to take care of the road to ensure the long-term quality of the road construction and beauty. Hygienic and environmentally friendly, especially to maintain the sewer system and avoid throwing waste or other debris into the sewer, which leads to congestion of the drainage system.
At the same time, the district governor instructed the Kampong Chet Tbong authorities to conduct regular guidance and follow-up by disseminating widely to the people living on both sides of the road to ensure efficiency and cooperation with the people.
He added that the road is good and clean only if there is cooperation between all local people as well as travelers and local authorities to develop and maintain security, order and beauty of Stong district and call on people to take care of the road to Quality, beauty, environment, hygiene and public order.
General Khieu Sopheak: Authorities are ready to take legal action against Rong Chhun, who warned of protests
(Phnom Penh): General Khieu Sopheak, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, confirmed to Fresh News that the Cambodian authorities are ready to take legal action against Rong Chhun, Vice President of the Candlelight Party. Warn of demonstrations.
General Khieu Sopheak confirmed that: "We are ready to implement the measures of the Royal Government, the instructions of Samdech Techo are still in force, whoever leads the people to protest will be held accountable before the law."
"All prisons are open to wait for the stubborn former CNRP leaders, including Rong Chhun," he said. "Within the party, he also did not agree, only Rong Chhun demanded a demonstration that was instigated by prisoners abroad, and then the party would be dissolved," he said. "Loss of both commune councilors and the upcoming election."
On May 29, 2023, Rong Chhun, Vice President of the Candlelight Party, announced that the party planned to gather about 10,000 members and supporters at Freedom Park to advocate for the NEC to allow the party to participate. National election for the 7th mandate in July.
However, on May 13, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on supporters of the Candlelight Party to remain silent and not to follow the appeals and actions of the candlelight party leaders.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen ordered the authorities and the armed forces to take immediate action not to rally, arresting the leaders of the Candlelight Party, both national and sub-national leaders.
