(Phnom Penh): International tourists are gradually coming to Cambodia, while new investment is expected to continue after Cambodia successfully closes the SEA Games.
Top Sopheak, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Tourism, said that the SEA Games is a great historical event of Cambodia through this event has greatly contributed to the promotion of Cambodia, so through this SEA Games not only attract tourists. But attract new investment to Cambodia, attract the economy, trade and other sectors that contribute to national economic development.
He said the Ministry of Tourism expects to receive about 4 million tourists this year. In the first quarter of 2023, Cambodia received more than 1 million tourists, an increase of 709 percent, the number of tourists who came to Cambodia were China, Thailand, Vietnam, Laos, the United States, Indonesia and Korea. 1 and through the SEA Games, the expectation of receiving 4 million tourists this year will be achieved.
He said that currently the largest number of tourists coming to Cambodia are tourists in the neighboring area, 32.8 percent Thai tourists, 16 percent Vietnamese tourists and 10 percent Chinese tourists, in addition to Europe. Also growing, such as France, England, Russia, increased by receiving about 2,000 tourists per day to visit Angkor.
Mr. Thuon Sinan, President of the Asia-Pacific Tourism Association of Cambodia, said that the SEA Games will bring a lot of fruits to Cambodia, because it does not pass immediately, but Cambodia will receive in the future.
He continued, "Through this SEA Games, the world has become more familiar with Cambodia. As the world becomes more aware of Cambodia as a peaceful, newly developed country, Cambodia will benefit not only the tourism sector." "But will attract foreign investment that will make the Cambodian economy stronger and stronger."
Draft Environmental and Natural Resources Code and Draft Law on the Approval of the ASEAN Trade in Services Agreement
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly resumed its ninth session of the 6th legislature on Tuesday morning, May 30, 2023, under the chairmanship of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, in the presence of 100 members of the National Assembly at the beginning of the session.
The ninth session of the 6th legislature discussed and approved two agendas: the draft Code of Environment and Natural Resources and the draft law on the approval of the ASEAN Trade in Services Agreement.
According to the press release on the outcome of the meeting, after discussing each of the draft sections of the Environmental and Natural Resources Code, as well as the discussion of each article of the draft law on the approval of the agreement. The ASEAN Trade in Services Agreement was approved by the National Assembly by a unanimous vote.
The draft Environmental and Natural Resources Code consists of 12 articles and 865 articles. Mr. Loy Sophat, Chairman of the National Assembly's Investment, Agriculture, Rural Development, Environment and Water Resources Planning Committee, reports to the National Assembly on the results of the study of the draft code.
The draft law on the ratification of the ASEAN Trade in Services Agreement has two articles. Mrs. Nin Saphon, Chairperson of the Public Works, Transport, Telecommunication, Post, Industry, Mining, Energy, Trade, Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction Committee of the National Assembly, reports to the National Assembly on the results of the study of the draft law. Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and his colleagues, representing the Royal Government, defended the draft law.
