(Phnom Penh): The concrete bridge across the Tonle Sap River and the Russey Keo flyover will be inaugurated on May 31, 2023 tomorrow under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In connection with the above program, on the afternoon of May 30, 2023, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Governor of Phnom Penh, and she presided over the Krong Pali ceremony to ask the landlord in a religious way to Happiness and progress in the inauguration of the cable-stayed concrete bridge across the Tonle Sap River and the Russey Keo flyover.
During this ceremony, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration also temporarily suspended traffic for all types of vehicles traveling across the concrete bridge, cable, crossing the Tonle Sap River and around the venue from the afternoon of May 30, 2023 until the end of the program. .
It should be noted that the cable-stayed concrete bridge across the Tonle Sap River is 922 meters long, 20.5 meters wide, the sidewalk of the pedestrian bridge is 1.25 meters wide on each side, and the height of the bridge piers for hanging the cable to the bridge floor is 34 meters.
There are 4 poles for hanging cables, 3.75 meters wide lane, 2 lanes to 2 lanes, maximum height under the bridge in the rainy season 10.5 meters, minimum height under the bridge in the dry season 20.5 meters equipped with lighting poles and traffic signs.
Separately, for Russey Keo flyover, the construction site was opened on January 31, 2022, with a length of 483 meters, a width of 15.8 meters and a height of 5 meters, flying along National Road 5 between the concrete bridge across the new Tonle Sap using the Construction time 15 months.
It should be reminded that Samdech Techo Hun Sen presided over the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the cable-stayed concrete bridge across the Tonle Sap River on October 23, 2017 and will be inaugurated on May 31, 2023 tomorrow with the bridge. Air Russey Keo at the same time.
(Sihanoukville): On May 28, 2023, more than 100 workers gathered in front of the casino building, formerly known as the Sikang International Hotel, located along Street 400, Sangkat 4, Preah Krong. Sihanouk to demand intervention to resolve the payment of salaries to the judges.
Workers told Fresh News that nearly 40 of the 158 workers who had not been paid by the company had sought the intervention of the relevant authorities and landlords to resolve the payment issue. Wages for workers, they confirm that the casino company has not paid workers since November 2022.
