Former Samlot District Candlelight Party Secretary Admitted to CPP
(Battambang): Another senior member of the Candlelight Party in Samlot district, Battambang province, has been added as a member of the Cambodian People's Party in Battambang province upon request.
Mr. Khy Odom, Secretary of the Executive Committee of the Candlelight Party in Samlot District and Deputy Chairman of the Executive Committee of the Candlelight Party in Kampong Lpou Commune, Samlot District, Battambang Province, announced his departure from the Candlelight Party and asked to join the CPP.
Through this request, the Cambodian People's Party of Battambang welcomed. Mr. Uy Ry, Chairman of the Standing Committee of the Standing Committee of the CPP in Battambang Province, handed over the decision of the party to recognize Mr. Khy Udom as a member of the Cambodian People's Party on the afternoon of May 30, 2023.
Uy Ry considered Khy Udom's decision to be the right one to participate in building Cambodian society under the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party.
Please note that the inclusion of Mr. Khy Udom as a member of the Cambodian People's Party was made at his own request.
On the morning of May 30, Mr. Khy Udom made a video respecting the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party to join the political life with the Cambodian People's Party.
In the video, Mr. Khy Udom expressed his opinion that only the Cambodian People's Party has the will, conscience and ability to lead the building of Cambodian society.
Mr. Khy Udom also called on other members of the Samlot Candlelight Party to leave the Candlelight Party and engage in political activities with the Cambodian People's Party for the opportunity to participate in building the national society.
Members of the North Atlantic Treaty Organization, or NATO, such as Denmark, reduced their military capabilities after the end of the Cold War. But in response to the Ukraine crisis, Copenhagen promised in 2022 that it would permanently increase defense and security spending by 2% of its GDP by the end of 2030, a key goal for NATO members. .
Danish defense spending will increase from $ 1 billion in 2024 to $ 2.84 billion by 2033. The government says its proposal will limit the size of defense spending as a whole as decisions on military procurement continue to be made.
