(Phnom Penh): At the invitation of Dr. John Chipman, Director General and Executive Director of the International Institute for Strategic Studies, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, will lead a high-level delegation of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to attend the Summit. The 20th Asia Security (Sangila Dialogue) will be held from 2 to 4 June 2023 in Singapore.
According to a press release obtained by Fresh News on May 30, 2023, the Summit for 2023 will have a plenary session on key topics, including: Indo-Pacific issues. New partnerships, model development for security, and so on.
The summit will also have small panel discussions at special sessions, including: cyber security, military capabilities development, regional balancing.
On the occasion of attending the 20th Asia Security Summit, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh will deliver a meaningful statement at the 7th Plenary Session on "Developing a Model for Cooperative Security". In view of the challenges posed by the rapid military development in the region and the functions that these new capabilities can play in balancing regional stability.
During the 20th Asia Security Summit, there was also a joint meeting of US Secretary of Defense with Defense Ministers of several ASEAN countries.
In addition to attending the summit, Samdech Pich Sena will also hold bilateral meetings with the defense ministers of the countries of Australia, Singapore and the People's Republic of China, as well as receive courtesy calls from dignitaries. Important in the Asia-Pacific region as well. Samlot District Candlelight Party Secretary Asks to Join Political Life with CPP (Video inside)
