Working Group of the National Council for Social Protection inspects the implementation of school feeding program using agricultural products in the community in Siem Reap
(Phnom Penh): Working Group of the Executive Committee of the National Council for Social Protection inspected the implementation of school feeding program using agricultural products in the community in the target schools in Bakong and Banteay Srey districts in Siem Reap province on the morning of May 30. This year 2023.
The visit to implement the school feeding program was led by Mr. Ros Silva, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Executive Committee of the National Council for Social Protection.
Mr. Ros Silva said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has always considered the development of human capital, especially young children, which is an important nursery in the development of the country, trying to expand education services to all villages and communes across the country.
Since 2019, in line with the social protection system development plan, the program has been gradually transferred from the World Food Program to the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
As of 2023, the Royal Government has decided to accept 427 target schools under the Ministry of Education in 10 provinces, including: Siem Reap, Kampong Thom, Preah Vihear, Battambang, Stung Treng, Banteay Meanchey, Kampong Cham, Kampong Chhnang, Pursat and Oddar Meanchey with 110,645 students. People. For 2024, the Royal Government will expand to 126 target schools, which will lead to a total of 553 target schools implementing this program.
