Dr. Yang Saing Koma presents the results of 6 months and claims that joining the Royal Government and the Cambodian People's Party is the right decision (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Dr. Yang Saing Koma, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister And Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries presented the results and activities for 6 months as of May 29, 2023 after joining the Royal Government and the Cambodian People's Party.
He said that in the past, he, along with Mr. Loek Sothear and Mr. Khat Sothy, colleagues have been given important values, trust and responsibilities in the agricultural sector, such as building breeding systems and building chains. Rice production, preparation of agricultural contracts for rice crops, deployment of agricultural coordinators in 10 pilot communes in Cheung Prey district, and leadership of agricultural development and orientation in Preah Vihear province.
He said that the huge responsibility for leading these important works was beyond his expectations and that it was contrary to the opinion of some critics who thought that joining the government led by The CPP is only for the sake of reverence and dignity and that he will be left without a clear job responsibilities.
Through these 6 months of experience, Dr. Yang Saing Koma can conclude that joining the CPP and the Royal Government is the right decision because he has enough opportunities and possibilities in line with his ability, passion and vision. He is very proud to be able to be a part of helping to solve the national problems of the farmers to ensure the sustainable development of the country and keep the peace.
He added that this success could be due to the support and appreciation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly, Chairman of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development and Mr. Dith Tina, Minister. Agriculture, forestry and fishing as well.
For the time being, he will continue to lead and implement key strategic political programs, focusing on:
1: Building rice seed systems and production chains to improve farmers' livelihoods, food security and the competitiveness of the Cambodian rice sector.
2: Deployment of commune agricultural coordinators throughout the country, starting from communes with the potential to produce rice in the first year.
3. Promoting the development of the agricultural sector in Preah Vihear province by making this province a leading province in the field of organic agriculture in connection with agriculture, tourism, culture and nature.
4. Participate in strengthening and expanding solar irrigation systems, which will not only reduce production costs, but will also promote sustainability and increase confidence and realism in rice and horticultural production, as well as make the sector more prosperous. Intensifying competitive potential.
