This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen inaugurated a new school building worth nearly 2 million dollars at Sihamoni Raja Buddhist University
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, the 11th day of the month of Chesth, the year of Thao 2567 On May 30, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, inaugurated a new school building at Sihamoni Raja Buddhist University in Wat Svay Po Pe, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Chhit Sokhon, Minister of Cults and Religions, said that the building of Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Bour Kry has classrooms, offices, Techo Santepheap Library, courtroom for law students and a meeting hall. The building has 9 floors, equal to 45 rooms.
The groundbreaking ceremony was held on July 4, 2022 under the presidency of General Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army, High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Mr. Chhit Sokhon said that the new building was designed with contemporary Khmer style architecture in the post-peace era and developed by synthesizing key Khmer architectural styles, including traditional architecture, Khmer ancient houses, Buddhism, Khmer ancient temples (Angkor Wat). Banteay Srei and Bakong Temple) Colonial heritage construction and modern architecture.
The main features of this building are as follows: * Ground floor: It is a space without walls, with air passing through (like a Khmer house built out of land), used as a meeting place for monks, students, information display area, bicycle parking and green garden.
* 1st floor: Seat holding the signature of Samdech Bhumibol Adulyadej - Rector's Office - Vice Chancellor's Room - OWSO - OWSO - Administration Office - Accounting Office - Academic Office - Lecturer Room
Architectural construction of Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Bour Kri building is a kind of Ame concrete structure that complies with technical standards, fancy, exquisite design and beautiful aesthetics. This building has been in use for more than 10 months from the opening day of the construction site.
This building is an important part of showing the national identity, which combines many Khmer architectural styles, emerging as contemporary Khmer architecture in the era of Techo Peace and Development for the heritage of the state forever.
After graduation, all generations of undergraduate and graduate students received a degree from His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
On October 17, 2022, Sihamoni Raja Buddhist University became a member of the International University Association of UNESCO (IAU), which has more than 600 member universities from 130 countries around the world. This has become a new history that has never been seen in the history of Buddhist studies in Cambodia in promoting the excellence of Buddhist studies on the international stage.
In addition to the building inaugurated above, Sihamoni Raja Buddhist University has three other academic buildings, including: The building of His Majesty King Sihamoni has 9 rooms, 2nd. The administrative building has 9 rooms, the third. Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen building has 24 rooms.
