India, although advanced in the production of arms for sale to some countries in the world, but its advanced military technology can not be compared to Russia, the United States, France or China. Russia is a country that provides modern weapons to India, which is why India is seen to be wary of its foreign policy on Russia.
Recommendations for India's inclusion in NATO Plus will help the United States and its allies become more confident in resisting Chinese influence and what is considered peacekeeping and stability in the Indo-Pacific region.
That action means that India's inclusion in NATO Plus is important for the United States in resisting the strategic competition posed by the Chinese Communist Party and what the United States has always recited the theory that China has. Threatening activities in the Indo-Pacific region
The proposed move comes as India itself recognizes the need to counter Chinese influence, which the Indian government says is growing in areas where stability is needed to maintain stability. Indo-Pacific.
