Three former Battambang candlelight party leaders have been announced as members of the Cambodian People's Party.
(Battambang): Three other former candlelight party leaders in Battambang province have been announced as members of the Cambodian People's Party after they decided to leave their former party and join the CPP.
Former leaders of the Battambang Provincial Candlelight Party who have been announced as members of the Cambodian People's Party include: Mr. Youm Doung, former Chairman of the Battambang Municipal Candlelight Party Executive Committee, Mr. Hong Thona, former member of the Battambang Provincial Candlelight Party Executive Committee, and Mr. Sim Borey, former Deputy Chairman of the Executive Committee of the Candlelight Party, Battambang Municipality, Kamrieng District, Battambang Province.
The ceremony to announce the former leader of the Candlelight Party in Battambang province as a member of the Cambodian People's Party was held on the afternoon of May 29, 2023, presided over by Mr. Sok Lou, President of the Cambodian People's Party in Battambang province. The ceremony was also attended by Mr. You Sereyvuth and Mr. Keo Phong.
During the ceremony, Mr. Sok Lou warmly welcomed the presence of the leaders of the Candlelight Party who participated in political life with the Cambodian People's Party.
He considered their decision to be the right decision to jointly build and develop the country with the CPP and the government. Mr. Sok Lou advised the former leaders of the Candlelight Party in Battambang province to work hard to mobilize all its members to vote for the CPP so that the CPP can continue its mission to serve the people.
Mr. Sok Lou added that many parties participated in the election, but the CPP is still a key player in ensuring lasting peace for the people.
Please note that the three former leaders of the Candlelight Party in the first three provinces above decided to leave the Candlelight Party after they lost faith in this party. In particular, the corruption and partisanship of party leaders.
