Hun Manet and his wife donate 10 million riels to soldiers injured by landmines in an operation to rescue Thai women from minefields
(Banteay Meanchey): Dr. Hun Manet and his wife, Mrs. Pech Chanmony, donated 10 million Riels to a soldier injured by a landmine in an operation to rescue a Thai woman from a minefield.
The donation from Dr. Hun Manet and his wife was handed over to Lieutenant Colonel Seng Chhorn, Deputy Chief of Staff of the 5th Military Zone, on Monday, May 29, 2023.
On that occasion, Major General Seng Thearin conveyed the greetings of Dr. Hun Manet and his wife to Lt. Col. Seng Chhorn, who worked hard to save until he suffered serious eye injuries that could cause blindness. This is an expression of the humanitarian spirit of the Cambodian army in helping each other to maintain the border, peace, friendship and development in accordance with the high recommendation of the head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
It should be noted that on the morning of May 27, 2023, a 40-year-old Thai woman went to pick vegetables in a minefield on the Cambodian-Thai border and stepped on a landmine, causing severe injuries to her left leg and head. .
After the incident, 27 demining forces of the 5th Army Division, in cooperation with the Thai side forces in front of the scene, immediately launched a rescue operation by clearing the forest to search for mines.
However, during the operation, another landmine hit the face of Lt. Col. Seng Chhorn, a soldier in the 5th Army Division, seriously affecting his face and causing him to be blind.
However, both Seng Chhorn and the Thai woman were rescued from the minefield and taken to hospital.
