(Kandal): A joint working group of Kandal Provincial Authority led by Mr. Nop Dara, Deputy Provincial Governor, on May 28, 2023, inspected the location of a pit of Tycoon Ouk Ratha alias Oknha Moha Ratha in Puk Russey Kandal Village. Puk Russey commune, Khsach Kandal district.
According to provincial officials, a joint team of relevant departments and district authorities, with the co-ordination of Deputy Prosecutor of the Provincial Court, Hor Lina, inspected the actual location of a pit named after the site owner. Ouk Ratha to inspect the technical characteristics, implementation of legal measures and licenses.
The team found that the pit site was actively transporting and that the site was unlicensed. The provincial joint working group required the site to be suspended and handed over to the provincial Department of Mines and Energy for processing. In case the business owner continues to act, the team will build a case and follow the legal procedure, and the business owner must pay royalties according to the amount of land that has been done in the past.
The pit of Tycoon Ouk Rathachik has a size of 17 hectares, equivalent to more than 1.2 million cubic meters. The royalties are charged at 2 cents per cubic meter for legal businesses, but without the law, all market prices for land sold in the area are 100% paid to the state and even subject to legal penalties.
