The provincial administration would like to thank all the media for participating in disseminating and reflecting on the current management mechanism of the Pursat provincial administration. NEC Starts Distribution of Voter Information Cards for the 7th National Assembly Election 2023
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) said that the distribution of voter information cards to people whose names are on the official voter list 2022 for the National Assembly election. 7 2023 has started to operate throughout the country.
The NEC produced 9,710,655 voter information leaflets, equivalent to the total number of registered voters in the 2022 official voter list.
The Commune / Sangkat Election Commission (CEC) is responsible for organizing the distribution of voter information leaflets in each village in each commune for a period of one month from 28 May to 26 June. 2023 and the remaining information leaflets will be kept and distributed at the CEC office until July 21, 2023.
Pursuant to Resolution 125 of the NCDD dated 13 March 2023, political parties and associations or non-governmental organizations (NGOs) that are not members of the leaflet distribution group may send their representatives to Observe the process of distributing information leaflets in the relevant communes.
The purpose of providing voter information is to:
* Assist voters who are on the official voter list to understand the numbering, names, data related to the person on the voter list, the code and location of the polling station, the date and time of the election, as well as the types of official identification documents to be used at Voting time
* Help voters to easily find the location of the polling station where they want to vote
* Assist the Polling Station Commission (PEC) to quickly find the names of eligible voters on the official voter list, which facilitates a smoother election process and less time for voters.
