Tehran accuses Zelensky of using Iran as a stepping stone to Western aid
(Tehran): Iran has accused Ukrainian President Vladimir Putin of using Iran as a stepping stone to gain military support and financial support from the West only by accusing Tehran of supplying Russia with weapons. . This was released by the AFP news agency on Sunday, May 28, 2023.
The United States and the European Union have imposed economic sanctions on Iran, accusing Tehran of supplying drones to Russia for use in the war of aggression against Ukraine. Iran has denied the allegations but later admitted that it did sell drones to Moscow, but that was before the war broke out.
Iran's reaction comes after Zelensky on Wednesday questioned Iran's support for Russia and its atrocities. In response, Iranian Foreign Ministry spokesman Nasser Kanani called Zelensky's allegations "false" and "just propaganda against Iran" and that the allegations were aimed at attracting military aid. And finance from Western countries only.
Russia has reportedly used 1,160 Iranian-made Shahed suicide drones in attacks against Ukraine.
