Understand the business: Food processing experts tell some points to make Cambodian processed products export to China
(Phnom Penh): Currently, very few Cambodian processed agricultural products can be exported to China, although both countries have been implementing the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement and the RCEP Agreement.
Mr. Mieu Soktry, President of the Cambodian Food Producers Association, said that very few of Cambodia's processed agricultural products were exported due to the limited standards of Cambodian products that did not meet national standards. Most processing enterprises and handicrafts are still too small, limiting the implementation of standards due to location and production factors.
"In order to export processed food products in this country, the relevant ministries need to find more information from their standard centers to teach our traders," he added.
However, he observed that the Royal Government is now paying more attention to national standards so that all artisans comply with this standard and apply international standards to export to other countries easily.
Zhou Khun, vice chairman of the Phu Van Dalian Economic Zone Management Committee, who came to study Cambodia's processed agricultural products, said that Cambodia's processed agricultural products have high potential for export to China, most of which do not exist. Do not mix any other chemicals, so Cambodian processed food products can have more opportunities to import to the Chinese market.
He explained that products imported into China require further development to comply with international standards and standards set by China. At the same time, Cambodia needs to have factories to process these products.
"In order to be able to export to China, it is necessary to make these products internationally recognized and comply with Chinese safety standards before these products can be imported into the Chinese market," he said. "It requires the relevant institutions of the two countries to recognize food standards and adhere to China's regulations and hygienic principles."
He added that he would cooperate with the Cambodian Food Producers Association to promote these agricultural products to the Chinese market as soon as possible in the near future. If these products are imported to China, he will widely promote to consumers in China to expand the market in China and make consumers recognize Cambodian products.
"I believe that if Cambodian products are standardized and have clear production, these products will have a larger market in China," he said.
Mr. Mieu Soktry said that the Cambodian Food Producers Association will cooperate with the ASEAN Plus 6 community to study the possibility of exporting products to ASEAN Plus 6 countries, including China, as well as examine the possibility of expanding production to Make the product price cheaper, have a better management system. Natural disasters! An elderly man was killed by lightning while fetching cows from a rice field in Prey Veng province's Pearang district.
(Prey Veng): Rain, wind and lightning caused the death of a young man as the victim went to tie a cow in a field near the village. This case happened at 5:30 pm on May 27, 2023 at the eastern point of Melob village, about 400 meters, Roka commune, Pearang district, Prey Veng province.
Authorities said that the victim was Mao Pov, a 48-year-old man. Prior to the incident, there was heavy rain, thunder and strong winds, while the victim was fetching cows in a field near the village when he was struck by lightning in the middle of a rice field, much to the surprise of the villagers. See and rescue, but unfortunately died of asphyxiation.
The body is now being taken to the family for a traditional ceremony at home. Pearang district authorities have called on residents to be careful when it comes to thunderstorms, not to go out into the fields or shelter under trees, and to turn off radioactive electronic devices to prevent any possible risks. Occurs eventually.
