Baghdad: Iraq on Saturday announced the start of a $ 17 billion project to connect a major cargo port on the country's southern coast by building railways and roads to the border with Turkey. A new move to transform the country's economy after decades of war and crisis. This is according to the publication by the AFP news agency on Saturday, May 27, 2023.
The development aims to connect the oil-rich port of Grand Faw in southern Iraq to Turkey to turn Iraq into a transit hub, reducing travel time between Asia and Europe.
The Iraqi government has predicted that high-speed trains will be able to transport goods and passengers at speeds of up to 300 kilometers per hour, connecting to local industrial and energy centers, which could include oil and gas pipelines. If work begins in early 2024, the project will be completed in 2029.
