Royal Government issues sub-decree on collection and distribution of benefits from the use of genetic resources
This sub-decree sets out the procedures and conditions for the equitable and equitable distribution of benefits from the collection of genetic resources, derivatives of genetic resources or relevant traditional knowledge in order to establish specific mechanisms for the implementation of the Nagoya Protocol of the United Nations Convention on Biology. Diversity aims to contribute to the conservation of biodiversity and the sustainable use of biodiversity components.
This sub-decree applies to the collection of genetic resources, derivatives of genetic resources and relevant traditional knowledge that originate or are present in the Kingdom of Cambodia or are accepted by the Kingdom of Cambodia or by any person under its jurisdiction. Its for the purpose of using genetic resources and relevant traditional knowledge.
This sub-decree does not apply to the collection of genetic resources and derivatives of genetic resources for the purpose of being used as a direct commodity, but the direct commodity is not used for the purpose of studying, researching or developing genetic resources.
