Constitutional Council issues statement: Rejection of complaints by the Candlelight Party and the Khmer National Unity Party is strictly in accordance with the spirit of the Constitution and the election law
(Phnom Penh): The Constitutional Council on May 27, 2023 issued a statement regarding the rejection of the Petition of the Candlelight Party and the Khmer National Unity Party regarding the registration of political parties to stand for election. In the past, the 7th legislature has consistently exercised its powers in accordance with the spirit of the Constitution and the election law.
The Constitutional Council stated in a statement that as the supreme body of the nation in charge of ensuring the protection of the Constitution, the Constitutional Council is based on the rule of law in exercising its powers in accordance with the fundamental principles of liberal, pluralistic democracy. People and the rule of law.
The Constitutional Council added that in the implementation of the Constitution for the past 30 years, all national institutions and general social components have been firmly implementing in the spirit of the Constitution, and liberal democracy, pluralism, and human rights on the path of the rule of law have been rooted in Citizens' society has the full right to participate in the political, economic, social and cultural life of the nation under the umbrella of the Constitution and peace.
Please be informed that on May 25, 2023, the Constitutional Council decided to reject the complaint of the Candlelight Party and the Khmer National Unity Party regarding the non-registration of candidates for the National Assembly election by the National Election Committee (NEC). .CEC). This decision was made after the meeting chaired by Dr. M. Chhun Lim.
