Director General of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture encourages farmers to transform from ordinary farmers to entrepreneurial farmers
(Prey Veng): Dr. Kao Thach, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Rural Development Bank for Agriculture and Rural Development (ARDB), encourages farmers to transform themselves from ordinary farmers to entrepreneurs and adopt modern technology. In rice cultivation to get high yields and harvest planning.
This encouragement was made on the occasion that Dr. Kao Thach and Mrs. and the management of ARDB attended the inauguration ceremony of Chhit Bunthon Rice Storage and Drying Plant in Prey Veng Province under the special financing project of the Royal Government of Cambodia. May 25, 2023
The inauguration of the rice depot and dryer reflects the Royal Government's commitment to supporting the rice sector. The rice depot and dryer will play an important role in collecting rice from farmers in Prey Veng province to help stabilize rice prices, especially during the harvest season.
He said that in order to increase the capacity in the value chain of the rice sector, especially the production capacity of rice warehousing, rice drying and rice processing in a competitive and stable manner, ARDB Bank has been working closely with ministries and institutions. Relevant.
In particular, the Rice Federation of Cambodia, rice mills, rice processing companies and exporters, agricultural communities and farmers who produce rice to meet the need for capital investment to build infrastructure such as: construction of warehousing, rice drying Rice mills and working capital for the stockpiling of rice mainly serve the milling of rice for export.
In addition, work to expand the connection between rice mills and farming communities or farmers through agricultural production contracts in order to create markets in order to stabilize rice prices and boost rice exports in line with the policy. Of the Royal Government. This is the additional confirmation of Dr. Kao Thach.
Chhit Bunthon, owner of Chhit Bunthon rice mill in Prey Veng province, said that the investment in this rice mill was made because he wanted to contribute to the rice sector in Prey Veng province.
He added that currently, this province is highly favorable for the production of rice, both dry season and wet season rice, as the province produces a total amount of rice more than other provinces, which in a year produce more than 1.5 tons of rice. Million tons and the remaining amount of rice for export more than 1 million tons.
Farmers' current rice production is for sale to the market, and most of the rice produced by farmers is sold to middlemen for export to neighboring countries, according to unofficial records in 2022. Vietnam through the gate of Prey Veng province has a volume of more than 1.6 million tons.
Mr. Chhit Bunthorn added that the rice mill will contribute in part to reducing exports to neighboring countries to buy rice from farmers at a reasonable price.
It should be noted that Chhit Bunthon Rice Mill has a warehouse of 50,000 tons of rice and a kiln with a drying capacity of 1,500 tons of rice per day.
Currently in Prey Veng province, there are 6 rice mills that have been operating in one year. These 6 rice mills have the capacity to collect 302,800 tons of rice that has been processed to produce rice to supply the market in In the country, there are three rice mills that have the ability to process rice into supply for export to international markets.
