Kandal Provincial Court Charges and Detains 1 Kilo Drug Dealer in Muk Kampoul District
(Kandal): Ms. Hong Marinech, Investigating Judge of Kandal Provincial Court, and Ms. Phat Sokunthea, Prosecutor, decided to charge and detain 24-year-old Song Veng Seng, who was active in drug distribution in Muk Kampul District. Imprisonment.
The two spokesmen said that the suspect was charged with "trafficking, storing and using drugs" under Articles 40 and 45 of the Law on Drug Control.
Article 40: Illegal storage, transportation and trafficking of drugs: shall be punished by imprisonment from 2 to 5 years. In addition to imprisonment, offenders can be fined from 4 million to 10 million riels.
Article 45: Illegal Use of Drugs: Any person who illegally uses drugs in the first and second tables in all forms and has been subjected to compulsory medical treatment shall be punished by imprisonment for one month. 6 months can be fined from 100,000 to 1 million riels. In case of non-recidivism, shall be punished from 6 months to 1 year and fined from 1 million to 2 million riels.
According to the story of the arrest of the suspect provided by the police: The arrest was made on May 23, 2023 at 14:30 at a rented house in Kandal village, Prek Anchanh commune, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province.
Suspect's name is Song Veng Seng, male, 24 years old, Khmer, unreliable occupation. Place of birth: Prek Ta Ton village, Preah Prosop commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province (arrested).
