The Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia and the Ministry of Commerce of the United Kingdom sign a Memorandum of Understanding to establish a trade and investment forum
The Minister of Commerce stated that the Cambodia-UK Joint Trade and Investment Forum is a positive step in strengthening the trade cooperation between the two countries in a sustainable manner and demonstrates the will of the Ministry of Commerce as Staff of the Royal Government of Cambodia to contribute to improving the investment and business environment and promote national economic diversification.
It should be noted that the contents of the Memorandum of Understanding on the Establishment of the Joint Trade and Investment Forum have been carefully studied and consulted by professional officials of the two governments, aimed at expanding trade volume. Bilateral trade, especially by promoting the export of potential Cambodian products to the UK market, including agricultural and industrial products, and increasing British investment imports to Cambodia.
In addition, the forum also organized a trade policy meeting between the inter-ministerial representatives of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the British Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia and between the Royal Government of the United Kingdom and the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to share. About the current implementation of new policies and seek opportunities to increase the volume of trade in goods and services and investment.
Based on data from the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia: The United Kingdom is a major trading partner of Cambodia in the past, with trade volume between the two countries in 2022 to reach a total of 977.43 million US dollars. An increase of 24.42% compared to 2021.
