(Foreign): Missile is a type of weapon used for long-range attack, it can fly by itself. Today, there are many types, from conventional missiles to ballistic missiles that can be equipped with nuclear warheads and can fly across continents.
The first missiles used in the operation were missiles developed by the German military during World War II. Among them, the most well-known missiles are the V-1 and V-2 missiles. However, the first missiles used in that era were produced in small quantities and were not very effective.
Currently, missiles have key components such as guidance systems, flight systems, engines and warheads. Navigation systems are very important for each missile. Some missiles can be equipped with infrared probes to track the heat emitted from the aircraft engine, while others are guided to their attack targets by pointing to the infantry 's laser system. Near the target directly.
