Most farmers in Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province, have started plowing and sowing rice after heavy rains at the beginning of this year's rainy season.
(Kampong Chhnang): Farmers almost everywhere in Kampong Chhnang province, who are engaged in farming, have started to cultivate and plow their farmland gradually after the heavy rains at the beginning of the rainy season. This.
The fact that farmers started plowing and sowing their fields at the beginning of the season was due to natural conditions, with heavy rains at the beginning of the season, which gave them the opportunity to plow and sow rice early. Years and have time to continue doing other business.
Mr. Phorn Mao, a farmer living in Aleng village, Chrey Bak commune, Rolea Bier district, described that most of our farmers who are engaged in farming are in the past, they have to sow seedlings before removing seedlings. That to take to transplant further. For sowing the seedlings, it is also necessary to soak them in water to plow the soil, leave the weeds to die, then plow a second time and sow rice to do this so that no weeds grow in the nursery.
He said that the field for transplanting rice is the same, it must be plowed to leave the weeds to plow a second time, this is not difficult to maintain or remove weeds in the rice. Get good yields too.
Mr. Ngin Hun, Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said this morning, May 26, 2023, that the cultivation of farmers in Kampong Chhnang province at the beginning of this year's rainy season, plowed land for cultivation. 19,371 hectares, equivalent to 5.57% of the plan of 122,000 hectares, of which 952 1 hectares were sown with light rice.
