WASHINGTON (Reuters) - Debt rating agency Fitch on Wednesday put the US credit rating under negative scrutiny as discussions on the debt ceiling remain pending. According to Reuters.
Fitch has placed its highest rating on US debt, AAA, under negative scrutiny, meaning it could be downgraded if lawmakers fail to increase lending to the US Treasury Department. Before the ministry runs out of cash next week.
Reuters reports that the downgrade could affect the pricing of billions of dollars in treasury bonds.
The government of President Joe Biden and Republican lawmakers are stuck in talks to raise the $ 31.4 trillion debt ceiling, and Fitch says it could downgrade the US debt if the United States Do not raise or suspend its debt levels in a timely manner.
"However, we believe that the risk has increased that the debt limit will not be raised or suspended before the default date, and as a result the government may begin to default on certain debt obligations," Fitch said.
