Nokor Democrat Party announces support for Constitutional Council decision
(Phnom Penh): The Nokor Democrat Party has issued a statement fully supporting the legal decision of the Constitutional Council, which issued a decision to close the protest route of the Candlelight Party and the Khmer National Unity Party in registration. Political parties stand for election and the list of candidates for the 7th National Assembly election.
According to the statement from the Democratic Party, both parties have violated and contrary to the election law in the Kingdom of Cambodia, which is the rule of law recognized by international organizations and the United Nations.
It should be noted that the Constitutional Council on May 25, 2023 decided to reject the complaint of the Candlelight Party and the Khmer National Unity Party regarding the non-registration of candidates for the National Assembly election by the National Election Committee. (NEC).
Following this decision, Dr. Prohm Vichet Akhara, Deputy Secretary General and spokesman for the Constitutional Council, further explained that the Candlelight Party and the Khmer National Unity Party will not be able to participate in the 7th National Assembly election. Lok Chumteav Pheung Sakona Supports the Constitutional Council's Decision to Reject the Complaints of the Candlelight Party and the Khmer National Unity Party
(Phnom Penh): Lok Chumteav Dr. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, on May 26, 2023, announced her support for the decision of the Constitutional Council to reject the complaints of the Candlelight Party and the Khmer National Unity Party.
Her Excellency Dr. Pheung Sakona affirmed that the decision of the Constitutional Council is to show the correctness of the implementation of the law by adhering to two important legal principles: First, the principle of strict interpretation of the law, which is the foundation of Apply properly (the law is the law and the law must be strictly enforced) and secondly, the principle of equality between all political parties and political parties before the law.
She added that the decision of the Constitutional Council also clearly shows that the process of liberal multi-party democracy must go hand in hand with the rule of law, which is the foundation for ensuring the long-term political and social stability of the nation.
It should be informed that on May 25, 2023, the Constitutional Council decided to reject the complaints of the Candlelight Party and the Khmer National Unity Party regarding the non-registration of the National Assembly Election by the National Election Committee. (NEC). This decision was made after the meeting chaired by Dr. M. Chhun Lim on the morning of May 25, 2025.
Please be informed that the NEC has issued a decision to reject the registration of candidates for the 7th National Assembly election of the Khmer National Unity Party and the Candlelight Party on the grounds that both parties did not meet all the requirements of National Assembly Election Law.
Separately, 18 political parties have been officially recognized by the NEC on the registration of political parties for the 7th National Assembly election to be held on July 23, 2023 after Those parties meet all the conditions of the election law.
