For Hopkins, Kiev could not get Western fighter jets to replace its Soviet-era fighter jets as long as they showed despair and defeat in battle. He added that Ukraine does not currently have an effective combat air force, so Ukraine needs new fighter jets for the future of the Air Defense Forces, and the transition to a Western fighter force is very reasonable.
