Senior Social Affairs Officials Attend the 11th ASEAN Social Affairs Ministers 'Meeting and the 7th ASEAN Plus Three Social Ministers' Meeting
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Eam Kunthy, Secretary of State, Representative of Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, chaired and participated in the 11th ASEAN Social Affairs Ministers 'Meeting and the 7th ASEAN Social Ministers' Meeting Plus Three under the theme "Acceleration In Implementing the ASEAN Commitment to Gender Equality through Gender Mainstreaming and the Social Environment ”via Video on May 25, 2023.
The meeting was attended by the Ministers for Social Welfare and Development of ASEAN Member States, China, Japan, the Republic of Korea and the Secretary-General of ASEAN.
The outcome of the meeting was that all ASEAN Member States agreed and issued a joint statement with the following contents:
1. Encourage all Member States to develop and review relevant policies and programs in line with ASEAN's commitment to gender equality through gender mainstreaming and socialization through the three ASEAN pillars (including security). And politics, economy and socio-culture) with the full support of the ASEAN Secretariat.
2. Encourage all Member States to implement the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities through the mid-term review of the ASEAN Master Plan 2025: Mainstreaming the Rights of Persons with Disabilities and the continuation of the ASEAN Master Plan.
3. Accelerate ASEAN-led national and regional efforts that contribute to the sharing of knowledge, technical capacity and capacity building on gender mainstreaming and social environment.
4. Establish a network of stakeholders with stakeholders, including civil society organizations, for meaningful exchanges and dialogue towards a people-centered and people-centered ASEAN.
5. Support an ASEAN-wide institutional mechanism for gender equality and intergovernmental processes among member states to develop gender-oriented initiatives and programs that are gender-sensitive in the region.
7. Encourage all ASEAN Member States to develop an ASEAN Strategy focusing on a core family approach that strengthens family well-being and develops family resilience and family solidarity in response to challenges facing families and resolving issues that arise and Concerns of families in general through the celebration of "ASEAN Family Day" to celebrate in May every year.
The 7th ASEAN Plus Three Ministerial Meeting on Social Welfare and Development achieved the following results: Reaffirming its commitment to work together to enhance regional cooperation on social welfare and development through Accelerate ASEAN's commitment to gender equality by mainstreaming gender and social environment.
