Dr. continued that the program to provide cash to poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid-19 is a special and large program to support the Royal Government like never before. So far, some countries in the region have completed such social assistance programs, and after the global Kovid-19 epidemic has slowed and the economy has returned to normal.
For Cambodia, under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Royal Government of Cambodia has always considered the well-being of the people without abandoning any citizen and decided to continue to implement this program until the end of 2023 for the people All poor and vulnerable families have been protected and their livelihoods have been stabilized.
Please be informed that the cash support program for poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid-19 was made in order to support and improve the lives of poor families affected by the epidemic. Of Kovid-19 since June 2020.
The 13-volume summary of the Vinaya Veda, an excerpt from the 13-volume Vinaya Veda, edited by Mam Chhay, first published
(Prey Veng): A 13-volume excerpt of the Vinaya Pidak, a summary and edited by Mr. Mam Chhay, Advisor to the Ministry of Interior and a former member of the Prey Veng Provincial Council, was first published after the recognition and permission of Samdech Moha Priest.
This book quotes the main contents of the 13 volumes of the scriptures, which are the roots of Buddhism, as the Sangha states: Yet the name of the religion endures forever.
Mr. Mam Chhay expressed his pleasure that this book was published. The first edition may have some bugs that require correction, and he is reviewing them. He said that in the future, if possible, he will continue to print more to give to the pagoda to keep and facilitate monks and Buddhists to study.
