(Siem Reap): The National Committee Against Torture (NEC) on May 25, 2023 organized a training course on disseminating national / international norms related to respect for human rights and the role and responsibilities of the National Opposition Committee. Torture at Siem Reap Provincial Hall.
He also presented national / international norms related to respect for human rights and national and international norms related to the fight against torture, as well as the role and responsibilities of the National Committee against Torture. This outreach training course also made some suggestions to the NEC to establish a committee at the provincial level.
Meanwhile, Nuth Saan, chairman of the National Committee Against Torture, said the purpose of the outreach was to raise awareness of the rights of the National Committee against Torture and the UN Subcommittee on Torture Prevention.
He said torture and ill-treatment were not necessary measures to be taken against those deprived of their liberty. On the contrary, such acts are illegal and a serious violation of human rights, it is an injustice that can lead to endless animosity.
He added that this outreach education will provide insights into national / international norms regarding the treatment of deprived persons, the Convention against Torture and the additional methods of roles, duties and rights of the National Committee against Torture and the Sub-Committee. Prevent UN torture.
He also expects authorities at all levels and relevant officials to gain an understanding of the relevant national / international norms on those deprived of their liberty to prevent and combat torture, as well as to understand the role and responsibilities of the National Committee against Torture. The NEC as well. 149 disabled people from both countries come to receive 1 million Riels from the fund of Duke Dr. Chea Ratana and Duke Ly Hiek Ratana
(Phnom Penh): After announcing the appeal to the two disabled people all over the country to receive support from the Foundation, this morning, May 25, 2023, the Foundation of Duke Dr. Chea Ratana and Duke Ly Hiek Ratana and philanthropists Donated one million Riels per person to the 149 disabled people at the Sun & Moon Riverside Hotel next to the flyover.
Duke Dr. Chea Ratana said that in line with the call of the Foundation, the 12th National Meeting and Donation for People with Disabilities in Cambodia today was attended by 149 people with disabilities. Each received a budget of 1 million riels.
The Duke continued, "Apart from giving him 1 million Riel per person, our fund also helped him to study a specific skill to earn a living and improve his family's economy. We help him. To continue studying for a bachelor's degree as well. So far, some people with disabilities in both arms are strong in spirit and life to become independent.
"However, our fund continues to help the most vulnerable people in Cambodia. "As my business as a businessman, I am still committed to helping the society through charitable activities to join the Royal Government of Cambodia in reducing poverty." This is according to the additional confirmation of the duke.
During the meeting, Duke Dr. Chea Ratana also encouraged all the disabled people, "Our fitness is disabled and there is nothing to fix it, however, we must not give up our courage. No more disability because fitness is another thing, but if we are more disabled, it makes us lose the struggle to do anything.
In addition, Duke Bandith has made many comparisons in society to capitalize on the disabled, motivated and hopeful in overcoming obstacles to achieve the goal of improving family life.
It should be reminded that in the past, both disabled people who received support from the fund of Duke Dr. Chea Ratana and Duke Ly Hiek Ratana learned agricultural skills and came to raise pigs, chickens, ducks and expand some of the regimes. They already exist and some are still studying.
Taking the opportunity to meet people with disabilities, Duke Bandith also celebrated 108 monks and people with disabilities. Then, on the same day, through Duke Dr. Chea Ratana and wife of Duke Ly Hiek Ratana also handed over the 58th ambulance as a precious gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen also handed over to Kien Svay District Referral Hospital.
Customs officials and Kien Svay district authorities burn and destroy 500 kilograms of frozen buffalo meat imported from India
These frozen buffaloes were smuggled in from India via Vietnam and intercepted by Kandal Provincial Customs and Excise under the leadership of On Sinuon on 20 May 2023. At the point of km 39, National Road 8 in Prey Bang village, Sithor commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province.
Mr. On Sinuon, Head of Kandal Provincial Customs Branch, stated that he requested the cooperation of Kandal Provincial Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud Branch (Kandal Provincial Branch) to check the quality to prevent the spread of contaminants and ensure Food safety to protect and promote public health. The results of the inspection of the Kandal branch of the CPP confirmed that the frozen buffalo meat was of poor quality and was burnt today.
Taking this opportunity, Mr. On Sinuon appealed to all importers, especially meat importers, to import in accordance with the law, do not evade taxes, because the importation of meat by evading this way damages the quality of meat, which affects the health of the people and Leads to loss of national income.
At the same time, Mr. Toch Chao Koy, Branch Manager of Kandal Province, asked all traders to love the life and health of the Cambodian people, do not want this kind of money, it is a sin and this sin is very serious, not because they want to Profit money to sell defective products to people to drink, it is very dangerous, very serious health, there is a disease that can not be cured because it is defective and full of chemicals.
He also pledged to cooperate with the customs team and local officials as well as relevant officials to continue to monitor the welfare, especially on the quality of goods to ensure the quality of food safety to all people.
Cambodian-Chinese Association for Education Exchange, Establishment of Study Centers in China Seek Scholarships for Cambodian Students
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian-Chinese Association for Education Exchange has just set up a study center in China to seek cooperation with partners in China to apply for scholarships for Cambodian students and facilitate them to study in China. More than 100 schools have cooperated.
He added that the association is currently looking for scholarship partners in China, which has so far contacted more than 1,000 universities, of which more than 100 have agreed to provide scholarships to Cambodian students.
He added that upon receiving scholarships from partners in China, the Study Center in China will provide those scholarships to the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo AMK Scholarship Association to distribute to poor students who wish to go. Study in China.
According to Sar Rithy, the Cambodian-Chinese Association for Education Exchange also has a Chinese language training program for Cambodian students before sending them to study in China. This is an opportunity for Cambodian students to get the opportunity to study in China, get information, readiness and additional knowledge of Chinese.
The skills offered by the scholarship are many fields such as tourism, public administration, agriculture, technology, business, politics, but the association implements the necessary priority areas first and appropriate to the level of Cambodian students, especially to meet the needs of the labor market because there are many labor markets in Cambodia. Who are in need of skilled staff. This is according to Mr. Sar Rithy.
On the other hand, the Cambodian-Chinese Association for Education Exchange will organize the first International Education Fair, which is scheduled to be held from 3-5 November 2023 in Koh Pich, Phnom Penh to disseminate information to Cambodian students about the opportunity. Study through scholarships in China. Cambodian students will get to know universities and educational institutions in China better, especially the opportunity to receive scholarships to study there.
It should be informed that the efforts of the Cambodian-Chinese Association to change education as well as the establishment of study centers in China are in line with the spirit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Li Keqiang, Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China. Aiming to promote the training and development of human resources, while the Cambodian-Chinese friendship is as strong as steel.
