Analyst: What are the scenarios behind the Candlelight Party's failure to run in the 7th National Assembly election?
On May 19, 2023, the Candlelight Party decided to appeal to the Constitutional Council against the NEC decision. According to the law in force, the Constitutional Council will have to make a decision within 10 days from the date of receiving the complaint, and the decision of the Constitutional Council is the highest legal decision and closes the appeal.
After the NEC decided to reject the registration of the Candlelight Party, observers and analysts of the political situation in Cambodia raised various scenarios around the candlelight party's failure to meet the legal requirements. To get registered, stand like many other political parties that get registered without any hindrance.
Why the Candlelight Party did not survive the document "Prakas on the registration of political parties at the Ministry of Interior", which everyone is well aware that this document is the single most important legal document of the political party And what are the possible scenarios behind the failure to register to vote by the NEC?
Based on the monitoring, analysis and evaluation of the political situation in Cambodia, the situation of the Candlelight Party's failure to receive the NEC's voter registration can be analyzed in the following two scenarios:
Now there is word of mouth, how can such a breakthrough party lead and decide the fate of the nation and the people if only one piece of paper can not be maintained? If this party accidentally wins the election, it will inevitably become a national disaster, and now there are ideas from opposition politicians demanding the removal of the leader of this candlelight party.
On the other hand, if this document really disappeared during that time, why did the Candlelight Party remain silent and not raise this issue or file a lawsuit, either administratively or in court, since Then?
First, it can serve as a political strategy to destroy multi-party liberal democratic elections in order to call on the international community not to recognize the election results and the resulting government, because if the Candlelight Party participates in the election. This is useless politically and turns out to be a seal on the ruling party of the Cambodian People's Party.
Second, this political blame can be blamed on the CPP to create an excuse for mobilizing local protests as well as inciting aggression in the upcoming election process. For the shadow leaders of this party, if there is a local protest, it will be a good opportunity to organize a return to Cambodia, as they have tried by all means many times in the past.
