The body of a man was found in the jungle in Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province, the authorities concluded that it was a murder case
(Pursat): The body of a man was found in the forest swelled and rotten and reported to the authorities and doctors for examination and autopsy, after the autopsy, the authorities concluded that it was a murder case .
That incident caused a surprise at 06:35 on May 22, 2023 at O Ting point in Kseth Borey village, Sornre commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province.
Brigadier General Molida, Deputy Commissioner of Pursat Provincial Criminal Police, said that after receiving the above information, the specialized force went to the scene to inspect the scene and the body with a doctor to see the scene. To the south of Phnom Chrak Ha, about 2,000 meters to the west of the access road to Kbal O Ting, 200 meters, in Kseth Borey village, Sornre commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province.
The body of the victim was named Phon Sna, 30 years old, male, height 1.63 meters, Khmer nationality, farmer, and his wife was named Yem Srey Leak, female, 30 years old, currently living in Kseth Borey village, Sontre district. Cardamom Mountain, Pursat Province.
According to the autopsy with Pursat provincial forensic doctor and the explanation of the incident, the police concluded that the victim may have died from a collision with a hard object with a sharp face on the neck to the bone could be a murder case.
The bodies of the victims have now been handed over to their families for traditional rites. In this case, the authorities are also continuing to investigate to find the perpetrators to comply with the law.
