A fire broke out in a mansion in Po Sen Chey district due to the collapse of a welder, the authorities used 20 trucks of water to extinguish it
(Phnom Penh): A mansion caught fire in the third floor room, causing surprise to the people and the police to intervene to rescue. This incident happened on the morning of May 24, 2023 in Kakap village, Sangkat Kakap II, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
Colonel Prohm Yorn, director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Fire Prevention and Rescue Office, told Fresh News that after receiving information from residents to report to professional officers, he immediately ordered a fire truck. All targets work out fire trucks to intervene.
Colonel Prohm Yorn said that during the operation, the specialized force immediately intervened to put out the fire so that the flames would not spread further. During this operation, the police used 20 water trucks, including 14 fire trucks from Phnom Penh Capital Office, 14 water trucks, 3 vehicles of the 70th Brigade, 2 water trucks and 1 Cambodian Beer Company car. Use 1 truck of water.
In the case of the above fire, two rooms on the third floor were on fire and did not cause the fire to spread to the neighbors. Among which is a type of concrete construction with a size (25 meters by 30 meters). No one was injured in the blaze, which was caused by a welder falling to the ground. Preah Sihanouk Provincial Red Cross Branch Distributes Relief to Families Affected by House Fire in Prey Nob District
