(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Wednesday, the 5th day of the month of Chesth, the year of Thao Panchasak, B.C. 2567 On May 24, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, inaugurated the new location of the Royal University of Fine Arts and handed out diplomas to students who graduated from this university.
The Royal University of Fine Arts is the only public higher education institution under the auspices of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and has played an active role in training human resources in the field of arts, culture, national identity.
Under the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, the Royal University of Fine Arts was completely closed. After the liberation on January 7, 1979, the school officially opened in high school and was called the "School of Fine Arts", which taught music, dance, circus and visual arts.
Since the resurrection of Second Life, the Royal University of Fine Arts has trained a total of 4,516 human resources (1,409 females or 30.2%) in its five majors. The above human resources are currently working in national institutions, the private sector, organizations, associations and some continue to study abroad, while others have become teachers who are training the next generation of students as successors.
The construction process of the new Royal University of Fine Arts is the first step in the construction of the first phase of Building "B", which began on May 2, 2017 and ended on May 13, 2022. With a budget of 12 million dollars from the Royal Government.
Another one hectare will be developed as a Cambodian-Korean arts training center under the cooperation between the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts of Cambodia and the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism of the Republic of Korea with a budget of approximately $ 5.3 million.
The center focuses on training in the arts of music, choreography and visual arts, and construction will begin in the near future, scheduled for completion in 2024.
