Thai rice exports rise to nearly 2.8 million tonnes
BANGKOK: The Thai government said yesterday that rice exports reached 2.79 million tonnes in the January-April period, with full-year exports expected to increase. There will be more than 8 million tons. According to the Bangkok Post.
Anucha added that the Thai prime minister has instructed state agencies to work hard to increase rice exports and increase crop production while pushing up rice prices in foreign markets.
He said Thai rice exports are expected to continue to grow after growing demand in many countries.
Thailand is now the world's second largest rice exporter after India. In April, the rise in rice prices was due to the stabilization of the baht, which kept rice exports competitive in foreign markets.
As a result, the price of most types of rice has risen beyond the government's price guarantee. The Ministry of Agriculture and Cooperatives now predicts that rice exports will exceed the annual target.
Major markets for Thai rice include Iraq, Indonesia, the United States, South Africa, Senegal, Bangladesh, China, Japan, Cameroon and Mozambique. Thailand is the largest exporter of white rice, followed by jasmine rice. According to the Bangkok Post.
