Cambodia-Thailand Air Force reconvenes annual meeting to strengthen cooperation
(Phnom Penh): The meeting of the Cambodia-Thailand Bilateral Air Force Officers Working Group has resumed its annual meeting after the Kovid 19 epidemic crisis has eased in the community.
The meeting of the Cambodia-Thailand Bilateral Air Force Officers Working Group began in 2014 and the meeting was rescheduled in accordance with the host parties, one at a time.
The meeting of the Bilateral Air Force Officers Working Group is an initiative of the Cambodian Air Force and the Royal Thai Air Force aimed at strengthening cooperation, exchanging experiences, providing information on various situations, training human resources and exchanging visits. Officers between the two air forces ... etc.
Despite the Kovid 19 plague, the two air forces continued their operations through the ZOOM system without interruption. The meeting brought significant benefits to the skills training of both Air Force officers. This means that the meeting brought the fruits of joint cooperation between the two air forces in the ASEAN community.
The 9th Air Force Officers Working Group Meeting kicked off on May 23, 2023 at the Phnom Penh Hotel. During the visit of the Royal Thai Air Force officers to Cambodia, a group of officers paid a study visit to the Victory Monument, the Royal Palace ... etc.
The Cambodia-Thailand Bilateral Air Force Staff Working Group Meeting was chaired by Lt. Gen. Yin Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Air Force and attended by Brigadier General Kuch Sinit, Brigadier General Yem Bon Reth, Brigadier General Meas Vutha and officers. Many more assistants.
Separately, the Royal Thai Air Force led by Lt. Gen. Pi Bunvaravan Pricha, Deputy Chief of Staff of the Royal Thai Air Force, along with several professional officers.
As a result of the ninth meeting of 2023, the two sides agreed to provide mutual human resource training and invite the Air Force as observers of the 2024 Rescue and Humanitarian Exercise.
