Cambodia prepares to sign memorandum of understanding with China on increasing rice exports
The seventh MOU on Cambodia's rice exports to China comes after the sixth MOU on 400,000 tonnes of rice signed in November 2021 was fully implemented as planned. Which will end at the end of May.
Oknha Chan Sokheang, president of the Cambodian Rice Federation, told Fresh News on May 23 that after the Cambodian Rice Federation met with the Corporation of the People's Republic of China (COFCO) last week to review the progress of the implementation of the memorandum. Sixth Memorandum of Understanding The two sides discussed the possibility of drafting a seventh Memorandum of Understanding to export more rice to China.
Please be informed that in the past implementation of the MOU, both sides are satisfied with the progress of the development of the Cambodian-Chinese rice sector, the Chinese side bought rice from Cambodia in the past 10 years increased from 600 tons in 2011. More than 300,000 tons per year, equivalent to 10% of China's total rice imports per year.
According to the report of the Cambodian Rice Federation, in the first quarter of 2023, Cambodia exported more than 170,000 tons of rice to 42 target markets with a budget of more than 126 million US dollars, of which more than 8 were exported to China. Ten thousand tons, accounting for 48% of total exports. Minister of Agriculture inspects family chicken raising business and vegetable business group, small house, solar water pump in Chit Borey district, Kratie province
