On May 19, 2023, at a meeting of the Council of Ministers, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, authorized an in-depth study of the project to dig a waterway connecting the river to the sea of Cambodia, which is an important project for the transportation of goods. It is planned to cost about $ 1.7 billion and take four years.
Oknha Lim Heng, vice president of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, told Fresh News that the creation of a waterway connecting the river to the sea is another historic milestone for Cambodia in transporting goods to international markets.
He emphasized that the new waterway project will make it easier to transport goods to international markets at affordable prices, help reduce the cost of Cambodian goods sold in international markets, making Cambodian goods more competitive in the market. .
Mr. Chea Chandara, President of the Association of Freight Forwarders and Supply Chains, said that this is a new historical project for Cambodia that will benefit the transportation of goods by water as well as benefit investors, owners of industries, handicrafts and factories. Others that will make the Cambodian economy more prosperous.
"Once we have the river access to the sea through this project of the Royal Government, if the study is successful, it will make the Cambodian economy grow even more because it provides very convenient transportation because we have times," he said. "Rivers connected to the sea, which makes transportation, whether it is agriculture, textiles, garments and other goods, will be convenient, cost-effective and easy to complete."
Dr. Hong Vannak, an economist at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that the project to dig a waterway connecting the river to the sea of Cambodia is a great project ever in Cambodia and a long-term strategic road for economic growth. Cambodia.
He said the new waterway would boost the growth of inland waterways by replacing time-consuming and time-consuming land transport, as well as costly national roads that need to be repaired and improved. . Not only that, this waterway project also helps reduce traffic accidents and environmental impact, as well as provide benefits to the agricultural sector for farmers who have land next to the canal.
At the same time, this project also contributes to the growth of tourism by attracting national and international tourists who like to travel and new experiences by traveling along this canal.
"Another point is that there may be an increase in some investment, meaning that some investors who are willing to invest in agriculture, industry or other sectors involved in transportation, which facilitates them in Shipping to sell without the need for transport by car or train. "Apart from attracting investment, it will also increase the value of real estate along the canal."
